/-!
# The Wilson two-scale bridge: abstract finite-dimensional results

A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalisation of the abstract results of the note *Wilson two-scale
block-Poincaré bridge* (sections 1–17) that are not already formalised elsewhere in this series.
The file imports Mathlib only and its namespace is `WilsonTwoScale`. A section sign (§) refers to
the note. Hilbert spaces of the note are real inner-product spaces here, finite-dimensional
(`EuclideanSpace ℝ ι`, `Fin r → Fin n`, matrices) wherever the argument needs it; this is said at
each item.

Already formalised and not repeated: §3.1, the existence and converse parts of §4.1 (existence is
re-proved inside `stable_splitting_min_norm`, which needs the vector `u`), and §4.2
(`stable_splitting_of_lower`, `lower_of_stable_splitting` and `coarse_primitive_splitting` in
`Certified4DCoarse2.lean`, with `κ ≤ 3321/500` and `C_coarse ≤ 10000/23851`); the finite version of
§7.1 (`total_variance`, lean10); the finite version of §8.3 (`FiniteFibre2.chi_eq_certV_add`). The
finite-fibre, one-parameter form of the score identity `∇g = h + r` of §8 is
`FiniteFibre2.averaging_error_eq` with connection `X = 0`.

## What is proved

* **§4.1, minimum-norm reconstruction.** Let `K_b` be finitely many subspaces of a
  finite-dimensional real inner-product space `E` and `J : ⊕_b K_b → E`, `J (c_b) = ∑_b c_b` the
  synthesis map (`synth`, with `⊕_b K_b` the `ℓ²` sum `PiLp 2`). Then `J* v = (Π_b v)_b`
  (`adjoint_synth`) and `J J* = ∑_b Π_b` (`synth_comp_adjoint`). If `∑_b ‖Π_b c‖² ≥ q ‖c‖²` for all
  `c` in a subspace `F` containing every `K_b`, with `q > 0`, then each `c ∈ F` equals `J J* u` for
  some `u ∈ F` (so `u = S⁻¹ c`); the reconstruction `R c = J* u` satisfies
  `‖R c‖² = ⟨c, u⟩ ≤ q⁻¹ ‖c‖²`; and every `z` with `J z = c` satisfies
  `‖z‖² = ‖R c‖² + ‖z − R c‖²`, so `R c` is the unique decomposition of least norm
  (`stable_splitting_min_norm`, `min_norm_of_synth_eq`).
* **§5.1, localization transfer** (`localization_transfer`). For chart spaces `E_i` (a finite family
  of real inner-product spaces), bounded maps `A_i : E → E_i`, `B_i : E_i → E` with
  `∑_i B_i A_i = I`, `∑_i ‖A_i c‖² ≤ A₀ ‖c‖²` and `‖B_i‖ ≤ B₀`, chart subspaces `K_{i,j}` with
  stable splitting constant `C₀` on each `E_i`, `B_i K_{i,j} ⊆ K_{b(i,j)}`, and at most `M₀` pairs
  `(i, j)` with a given label: every `c ∈ E` is `∑_b c_b` with `c_b ∈ K_b` and
  `∑_b ‖c_b‖² ≤ M₀ B₀² C₀ A₀ ‖c‖²`. The volume index `q` is suppressed: the constant depends only on
  `M₀, B₀, C₀, A₀`, so the theorem applied at each `q` is the uniform statement.
* **§5.2, one volume does not give all volumes.** In `ℝ²` with `K₁ = span e₁` and
  `K₂ = span (cos θ, sin θ)`: `∑_b ‖Π_b x‖² = xᵀ P x` for the matrix
  `P = [[1 + cos² θ, cos θ sin θ], [cos θ sin θ, sin² θ]]` (`angleMat_form`), of trace `2` and
  determinant `sin² θ`, with eigen-equations for `1 ± cos θ` (`angleMat_eig_low`,
  `angleMat_eig_high`; the vector for `1 − cos θ` is nonzero if `cos θ ≥ 0`, `lowVec_ne_zero`). For
  `cos θ ≥ 0` the best lower bound of `∑_b Π_b` is exactly `1 − cos θ` (`angleSys_isGreatest`).
  Along `θ_q = π/(2(q + 1))` it equals `1` at `q = 0` and tends to `0` (`angleSeq_zero`,
  `tendsto_angleSeq`), and no `α > 0` is a lower bound for every member (`no_uniform_lower`).
* **§6.1, fixed-space perturbation.** If `⟨c, S c⟩ ≥ α ‖c‖²` and `|⟨c, (S̃ − S) c⟩| ≤ ε ‖c‖²` for
  all `c` in a subspace `F`, then `⟨c, S̃ c⟩ ≥ (α − ε) ‖c‖²` on `F` (`perturbation_lower`); if
  moreover `S̃ = ∑_b Π̃_b` with `K̃_b ⊆ F` and `ε < α`, every `c ∈ F` splits with constant
  `(α − ε)⁻¹` (`perturbation_splitting`).
* **§6.2, stability from the synthesis map** (`synthesis_stability`). For bounded `J, J̃` between
  real Hilbert spaces (complete, not necessarily finite-dimensional), `J J* ≥ α`,
  `‖J̃ − J‖ ≤ δ < √α` imply `J̃ J̃* ≥ (√α − δ)²`. The identity `⟨v, J J* v⟩ = ‖J* v‖²` is
  `inner_comp_adjoint_self`.
* **§8.1, vector response bound** (`vector_response_bound`, `vector_response_bound_solve`):
  `⟨t · s, u⟩² ≤ (tᵀ X t) 𝒱(u)`; the two forms are described under the departures below.
* **§8.2, inter-fibre comparison** (`inter_fibre_comparison`,
  `inter_fibre_comparison_of_response`): `√E_B ≤ √H + χ √V` on a finite coarse space.
* **§8.3, form-domain version** (`poisson_residual`): if `w` represents `s`
  (`⟨s, u⟩ = ⟨w, R u⟩`, the role of `L^{-1/2} s`) and `L h` is represented by `R h`, then
  `w − R h` represents `r = s − L h`, and `‖w‖² = 2 ⟨s, h⟩ − ⟨h, L h⟩ + ‖w − R h‖²`.
* **§9.1, the algebraic step** (`cstar_spec`, `quad_le_cstar`, `two_level_bound`). With
  `C* = (A + D + √((A − D)² + 4B²))/2`: `C* ≥ A`, `C* ≥ D`, `(C* − A)(C* − D) = B²`, and
  `A x² + 2 B x y + D y² ≤ C* (x² + y²)` for all real `x, y`. Hence `Var = v̄ + Var_ν(g)`,
  `v̄ ≤ λ⁻¹ V`, `Var_ν(g) ≤ γ⁻¹ E_B` and `√E_B ≤ √H + χ √V` give `Var ≤ C* (V + H)` with
  `A = λ⁻¹ + χ²/γ`, `B = χ/γ`, `D = γ⁻¹`. Also `C*(A, 0, D) = max(A, D)` (`cstar_zero`).
* **§10.1, pair representation** (`pair_representation`, `norm_pairVec_sq`). On a finite
  configuration space with weights `μ ≥ 0` and an exterior map `e`,
  `‖f − P f‖²_μ = ½ ∑_η ν(η) ∑_{u,v} μ^η(u) μ^η(v) (f(u) − f(v))²`, where `ν` is the exterior
  marginal, `μ^η` the conditional law on `{e = η}` and `P` the conditional expectation. With
  finitely many cubes, `D_n f` realised in `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Σ x, H_x × Ω × Ω)` satisfies
  `‖D_n f‖² = ℰ_n(f) = n⁻⁴ ∑_x ‖f − P_x f‖²` for `n > 0`.
* **§10.2, energy factorization** (`energy_factorization`, `energy_factorization_cube`): if
  `(T_V f, T_H f) = A (D f)` with `A : 𝒵 → 𝒱 ⊕ ℋ` bounded and `‖A‖² ≤ K`, then
  `V(f) + H(f) ≤ K ‖D f‖²`, in particular `≤ K ℰ_n(f)` for the cube energy.
* **§10.3, the circle** (`no_gradient_bound_by_resampling`). For the normalised Lebesgue measure on
  `[0, 2π]`, `f_j(θ) = sin(jθ)` has full-resampling energy `Var(f_j) = 1/2` and gradient energy
  `j²/2`, so no constant `K` satisfies `∫ |f′|² ≤ K Var(f)` for all `2π`-periodic `f` of class
  `ContDiff ℝ ⊤`. In this Mathlib `ContDiff ℝ ⊤` is analyticity (`C^ω`); the statement for this
  smaller class implies the one for smooth functions.
* **§11.1, defect absorption** (`defect_absorption`, `defect_absorption_pos`): from
  `Var ≤ C* (V + H)` and `V + H ≤ K ℰ + δ Var` with `C*, K > 0`,
  `ℰ ≥ ((1 − C* δ)/(C* K)) Var`, and the constant is positive when `C* δ < 1`. For a bad set of
  probability `p` and `f = 1_B − p` on a finite probability space: `E f = 0`, `Var f = p(1 − p)`,
  `∫_B f² = p(1 − p)²` (`bad_set_ratio`), the ratio is `1 − p` (`bad_set_ratio_eq`) and tends to
  `1` as `p → 0⁺` (`tendsto_bad_set_ratio`). A concrete instance with `C* δ = 1/2 < 1` on the
  two-point space is `defect_absorption_example`.
* **§12.1, the uniform bridge** (`uniform_bridge`): for any family of domains `𝒟_p` (`p` standing
  for the pairs `(k, L)`) carrying the inputs of §7–§9 and §11 with `λ_p ≥ λ₀ > 0`,
  `γ_p ≥ γ₀ > 0`, `0 ≤ χ_p ≤ χ₀`, `K_p ≤ K₀`, `δ_p ≤ δ₀`, `K₀ > 0` and `C₀ δ₀ < 1`, every member
  satisfies `ϖ₀ Var ≤ ℰ` with `ϖ₀ = (1 − C₀ δ₀)/(C₀ K₀) > 0` and `C₀ = C*(A₀, B₀, D₀)`. The
  extension from a dense domain is `bp_extend_of_dense` (continuity of `Var` and `ℰ` is a
  hypothesis). Constants: `(3321/500)(10000/23851) = 66420/23851` (`primitive_cost`); for
  `λ₀ = 2/9`, `γ₀ = 1`, `χ₀ = 2` one has `C₀ = 9` (`cstar_example`), and with `K₀ = 1`,
  `δ₀ = 1/18`, `ϖ₀ = 1/18` (`varpi_example`, `uniform_bridge_example`).
* **§13.1, first-chaos transfer.** Abstractly (`first_chaos_transfer`, any real inner-product
  space): for each block `x` let `Q_{x,0}, …, Q_{x,r−1}` be pairwise commuting orthogonal
  projections and `w_x ≥ 0`; then `I − ∏_j Q_{x,j} ≥ (1/r) ∑_j (I − Q_{x,j})`
  (`one_sub_pprod_ge_avg`), and `∑_x w_x (I − Q_{x,j}) ≥ g` for every `j` gives
  `∑_x w_x (I − ∏_j Q_{x,j}) ≥ g`, also on any subspace. On the coordinate model
  `H = ℝⁿ`, `H^{⊗r} = ℝ^{(Fin r → Fin n)}` (`first_chaos_transfer_tensor`): for symmetric
  idempotent matrices `P_x` with `∑_x w_x (I − P_x) ≥ g` on `ℝⁿ`,
  `∑_x w_x (I − P_x^{⊗r}) ≥ g` on `H^{⊗r}` and on the symmetric tensors (`symTensors`). Here
  `P^{⊗r}` (`tpow`) is the product of the `r` position operators, and its kernel is the Kronecker
  power `∏_j P(i_j, k_j)` (`tpow_apply`).
* **§14.1, propagation across scales** (`scale_propagation`): `ℰ_{j+1} ≥ c_{j+1} ℰ_j` with
  `c_j ≥ 0` and `ℰ_0 ≥ ϖ_base Var` give `ℰ_J ≥ ϖ_base (∏_{j=1}^{J} c_j) Var`; for `0 ≤ c < 1`,
  `c^J → 0` (`tower_degenerates`).

## Departures from the note

* **Finite dimensions.** §4.1, the splitting part of §6.1, the solvability lemma `exists_solve` of
  §8.1, §10.1 and the tensor model of §13.1 are proved in finite dimensions; §5.1, the lower bound
  of §6.1, §6.2, both forms of §8.1, §8.3, §10.2 and the abstract §13.1 hold in arbitrary real
  inner-product spaces (§6.2 in complete ones); §8.2 uses a finite coarse space with arbitrary
  fibre spaces; §9.1, §11.1, §12.1 and §14.1 are statements about real numbers.
  The note's §4.1 argument for infinite-dimensional `F` (closed and dense range of `S`) is not
  formalised.
* **§5.1.** `C₀` may be any real number; no sign is assumed. `M₀` is a natural number.
* **§6.1.** `S` and `S̃` need not be self-adjoint or bounded; only their quadratic forms on `F`
  enter. `ε ≥ 0` is not assumed.
* **§8.1.** The note takes `L_y ≥ 0` self-adjoint on `L²₀(μ_y)` with `𝒱_y(u) = ‖L_y^{1/2} u‖²`
  and `s_i ∈ Dom L_y^{-1/2}`, and derives `⟨s_i, u⟩ = ⟨L^{-1/2} s_i, L^{1/2} u⟩` by spectral
  calculus.
  In `vector_response_bound` a linear map `R` plays `L^{1/2}` (`𝒱(u) = ‖R u‖²`), vectors `w_i`
  play `L^{-1/2} s_i`, the identity `⟨s_i, u⟩ = ⟨w_i, R u⟩` is the hypothesis, and
  `X_{ij} = ⟨w_i, w_j⟩` (`Matrix.gram`); the spectral-calculus step is not formalised. In finite
  dimensions no spectral calculus is needed: `vector_response_bound_solve` takes `L` symmetric with
  `⟨u, L u⟩ ≥ 0` and solutions `L g_i = s_i` (the finite form of `s_i ∈ Dom L^{-1/2}`; they exist
  when `ker L = 0`, `exists_solve`) and `X_{ij} = ⟨s_i, g_j⟩`, which does not depend on the chosen
  solutions (`inner_solve_symm`). That this `X` equals `⟨L^{-1/2} s_i, L^{-1/2} s_j⟩` is not
  formalised, because no square root of `L` is constructed.
* **§8.2.** Integrals against `ν` are finite sums with weights `ν(y) ≥ 0`. The fibre at `y` is a
  real inner-product space `E_y` (the centred space), `u_y = f_y − g(y) ∈ E_y`,
  `r_y = (⟨s_{y,i}, u_y⟩)_i`, `𝒱_y = ‖R_y u_y‖²`, and `∇g(y) = h_y + r_y` is a hypothesis (it is
  the derivative identity of §8). The square root `M(y)^{1/2}` is replaced by any matrix `S(y)` with
  `M(y) = S(y)ᵀ S(y)`, and `M^{1/2} X M^{1/2} ≤ χ²` by `S X Sᵀ ≤ χ²`; taking `S = M^{1/2}`, which
  is symmetric, gives the note's hypothesis, so nothing is lost. Positive definiteness and
  measurability of `M` are not needed.
* **§9.1.** Only the algebra is formalised. The measure-theoretic inputs (total variance for a
  disintegration, the fibre and coarse bounds, the comparison) enter as real-number hypotheses;
  `λ > 0` and `χ ≥ 0` are not needed for the step.
* **§10.1.** The conditional law given the exterior `η` is `μ` restricted to `{e = η}` and
  normalised; the interior variables `u, v` range over the configuration space (the conditional law
  vanishes off the fibre); `μ` need not be normalised. The Hilbert space `𝒵` is realised
  isometrically by absorbing the pair weights into square roots.
* **§10.2.** `𝒱 ⊕ ℋ` is the `ℓ²` direct sum `WithLp 2 (𝒱 × ℋ)`; `T_V`, `T_H` and `D` need not be
  linear.
* **§11.1.** `C* > 0` and `K > 0` are assumed (the note divides by `C* K`); `δ ≥ 0` and
  `C* δ < 1` are not needed for the inequality, and `C* δ < 1` gives the positivity of the constant.
* **§12.1.** The Wilson data (the finite Wilson law, the cube conventions of S3, the gauge-invariant
  subspace `𝒜`, the continuity of `ℰ_n` on `L²(μ)`) are not formalised; the theorem is stated for
  abstract real functionals. Nonnegativity of `Var, V, H, E_B, ℰ` and `K₀ > 0` are explicit
  hypotheses (`K₀ > 0` follows from `0 < K_p ≤ K₀` once one pair exists); the lower bounds
  `K_p > 0`, `δ_p ≥ 0` are not needed.
* **§13.1.** The tensor product of an infinite-dimensional `H` is not constructed; the coordinate
  model covers `H = ℝⁿ` with its standard basis. `g` may be any real number (`g ≥ 0` is not
  assumed).
* **§14.1.** The scales `ℓ_j` appear only through their index `j`; `c_j ≥ 0` suffices.

## Corrections to the note

* §4.1, proof: two adjoint stars were lost. "Thus `Jv = (Π_b v)_b`" should read
  `J* v = (Π_b v)_b` (`adjoint_synth`), and "Set `S = JJ`" should read `S = J J*`
  (`synth_comp_adjoint`).
* §6.2, proof: the same lost star. "`‖Jv‖² = ⟨v, JJv⟩`" should read `‖J* v‖² = ⟨v, J J* v⟩`
  (`inner_comp_adjoint_self`).
* §3: "These are lower and upper certificates, respectively" reads reversed. As bounds on the
  constants, `‖φ‖² ≤ κ₀ ‖dφ‖²` is an upper certificate (for the fibre constant) and
  `∑_b ‖Π_b c‖² ≥ α₀ ‖c‖²` a lower certificate (for the lowest eigenvalue of `∑_b Π_b`), so they
  are upper and lower certificates, respectively; read as eigenvalue bounds, both are lower
  bounds. This is a matter of wording, not of mathematics. §3 itself is formalised in
  `Certified4DCoarse2.lean`, not here.

## Not formalised here

* The continuous-measure statements: §7.1 for regular conditional laws on standard Borel spaces,
  the measure-theoretic part of §9.1, §10.1 with Fubini, and the derivation of `∇g = h + r` in §8 by
  differentiation under the integral. They need disintegration and dominated convergence; the
  finite versions are the ones cited above.
* The spectral-calculus step of §8.1 for an unbounded `L` (see the departures).
* In §13: countably many blocks, the Gaussian identification of block conditional expectations
  with second quantisations `Γ(P_x)`, and the chaos decompositions `Var(f) = ∑_r ‖f_r‖²`,
  `ℰ(f) = ∑_r ⟨f_r, A_r f_r⟩`; they need the Wiener chaos of a Gaussian field.
* §12.1 for the Wilson family itself, and §15 (S3's transfer theorem, `m_* = 16ϖ₀/(625e²ℓ)`,
  units): these concern the physical continuum transfer and are outside the scope of this file. No
  statement here is the hypothesis (U), the estimates D4, D8 or (E), the continuum limit or the mass
  gap.
* §16 and §17 are a status table and a work order, not mathematical statements.

## Non-vacuity

The last section (`ClosedApplications`) applies every theorem with hypotheses to concrete data in a
closed theorem: the lines at
angle `π/3` in `ℝ²` (§4.1, §5.2, §6.1, where `perturbation_lower` returns the sharp bound
`1 − cos(π/3) = 1/2`), the two coordinate charts of `ℝ²` (§5.1), `J = I`, `J̃ = I/2` on `ℝ`
(§6.2), the fibre `ℝ` with `R = 2` (`L = 4`) in the representer forms and `L = 2` in the solve
form (§8), the two-point space (§10.1, the cube form of §10.2, §11.1), `ℝ ⊕ ℝ` (§10.2), `sin θ`
on the circle (§10.3), a family indexed by `ℕ` with `C₀ = 9`, `ϖ₀ = 1/18` (§12.1), and two blocks
`diag(1, 0)`, `diag(0, 1)` on `ℝ² ⊗ ℝ²` (§13.1). Some witnesses are degenerate and are backed by a
nondegenerate one: `first_chaos_transfer_example` and `first_chaos_transfer_restrict_example` use
`Q = 0` (`first_chaos_transfer_tensor_example` applies `first_chaos_transfer` to genuine
projections); `min_norm_of_synth_eq_example` takes `z = J* u` (the `∀ z` part of
`stable_splitting_min_norm_example` is general); `uniform_bridge_example` has `E_B = H` and
`V + H = ℰ`, so its `χ` and `δ` terms are unused (`two_level_bound_example` uses the `χ` term);
`bp_extend_example` is trivially true. Numerical agreement is never used as proof: every
statement is kernel-checked.

Nothing here is about the Yang–Mills measure; (D), (E) and the mass gap remain open.
-/

namespace WilsonTwoScale

open Finset Real Filter Topology
open scoped Matrix

/-! ## 1. §4.1: the synthesis map, its adjoint, and minimum-norm reconstruction

`⊕_b K_b` is the `ℓ²` sum `PiLp 2 (fun b => K b)`. With the adjoint stars restored (see the module
docstring), `J* v = (Π_b v)_b` and `S = J J* = ∑_b Π_b`. -/

/-- The synthesis map `J : ⊕_b K_b → E`, `J (c_b) = ∑_b c_b`. -/
noncomputable def synth {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b) →ₗ[ℝ] E where
  toFun z := ∑ b, ((z.ofLp b : K b) : E)
  map_add' x y := by simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib]
  map_smul' a x := by simp [Finset.smul_sum]

/-- The analysis map `v ↦ (Π_b v)_b`; by `adjoint_synth` it is `J*`. -/
noncomputable def anal {ι : Type*} {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) :
    E →ₗ[ℝ] PiLp 2 (fun b => K b) where
  toFun v := WithLp.toLp 2 (fun b =>
    (⟨(K b).starProjection v, (K b).starProjection_apply_mem v⟩ : K b))
  map_add' x y := by ext b; simp
  map_smul' a x := by ext b; simp

/-- `J z = ∑_b z_b`. -/
theorem synth_apply {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (z : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b)) :
    synth K z = ∑ b, ((z.ofLp b : K b) : E) := rfl

/-- The `b`-th component of `J* v` is `Π_b v`. -/
theorem anal_apply {ι : Type*} {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (v : E) (b : ι) :
    (((anal K v).ofLp b : K b) : E) = (K b).starProjection v := rfl

/-- `⟨J* v, z⟩ = ⟨v, J z⟩`: the defining identity of the adjoint. -/
theorem inner_anal_left {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (v : E)
    (z : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b)) :
    inner ℝ (anal K v) z = inner ℝ v (synth K z) := by
  rw [PiLp.inner_apply, synth_apply, inner_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun b _ => ?_
  rw [Submodule.coe_inner, anal_apply]
  have h := Submodule.starProjection_inner_eq_zero v ((z.ofLp b : K b) : E) (z.ofLp b).2
  rw [inner_sub_left] at h
  linarith

/-- **`J* v = (Π_b v)_b`** (the corrected form of "`Jv = (Π_b v)_b`" in §4.1). -/
theorem adjoint_synth {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) :
    LinearMap.adjoint (synth K) = anal K :=
  ((LinearMap.eq_adjoint_iff (anal K) (synth K)).mpr fun v z => inner_anal_left K v z).symm

/-- **`S = J J* = ∑_b Π_b`** (the corrected form of "`S = JJ`" in §4.1). -/
theorem synth_comp_adjoint {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) :
    synth K ∘ₗ LinearMap.adjoint (synth K) = ∑ b, ((K b).starProjection : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) := by
  rw [adjoint_synth]
  ext v
  simp [synth_apply, anal_apply, LinearMap.sum_apply]

/-- The norm of `⊕_b K_b`: `‖z‖² = ∑_b ‖z_b‖²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_piLp {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (z : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b)) :
    ‖z‖ ^ 2 = ∑ b, ‖((z.ofLp b : K b) : E)‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [PiLp.norm_sq_eq_of_L2]
  rfl

/-- **Minimality.** If `J z = J (J* u)`, then `‖z‖² = ‖J* u‖² + ‖z − J* u‖²`. -/
theorem min_norm_of_synth_eq {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (u : E)
    (z : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b)) (hz : synth K z = synth K (anal K u)) :
    ‖z‖ ^ 2 = ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 + ‖z - anal K u‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h0 : inner ℝ (anal K u) (z - anal K u) = 0 := by
    rw [inner_anal_left, map_sub, hz, sub_self, inner_zero_right]
  have := norm_add_sq_real (anal K u) (z - anal K u)
  rw [add_sub_cancel] at this
  rw [this, h0]; ring

/-- `⟨∑_b Π_b u, u⟩ = ∑_b ‖Π_b u‖²` (restated from `Certified4DCoarse2`, same statement). -/
theorem inner_sum_starProjection_self {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (u : E) :
    inner ℝ (∑ b, (K b).starProjection u) u = ∑ b, ‖(K b).starProjection u‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [sum_inner]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun b _ => ?_
  have h := Submodule.starProjection_inner_eq_zero u ((K b).starProjection u)
    ((K b).starProjection_apply_mem u)
  rw [inner_sub_left, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq] at h
  rw [real_inner_comm]
  linarith

/-- `J (J* u) = ∑_b Π_b u`. -/
theorem synth_anal {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (u : E) :
    synth K (anal K u) = ∑ b, (K b).starProjection u := rfl

/-- `‖J* u‖² = ∑_b ‖Π_b u‖²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_anal {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E) (u : E) :
    ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 = ∑ b, ‖(K b).starProjection u‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [norm_sq_piLp]; rfl

/-- **§4.1, stable splitting with minimum-norm reconstruction.** Let `F` be a subspace of a
finite-dimensional real inner-product space and `K_b ≤ F` finitely many subspaces with `q ‖c‖² ≤ ∑_b
‖Π_b c‖²` on `F`, `q > 0`. For `c ∈ F` there is `u ∈ F` (namely `u = S⁻¹ c`) such that the
reconstruction `R c = J* u` satisfies `J (R c) = c`, `‖R c‖² = ⟨c, u⟩ ≤ q⁻¹ ‖c‖²`, and `‖z‖² = ‖R
c‖² + ‖z − R c‖²` for every `z ∈ ⊕_b K_b` with `J z = c`. The existence part is
`Certified4DCoarse.stable_splitting_of_lower`; it is re-proved here because minimality needs `u`. -/
theorem stable_splitting_min_norm {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (F : Submodule ℝ E) (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E)
    (hK : ∀ b, K b ≤ F) {q : ℝ} (hq : 0 < q)
    (hlow : ∀ c ∈ F, q * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ b, ‖(K b).starProjection c‖ ^ 2) {c : E} (hc : c ∈ F) :
    ∃ u ∈ F, synth K (anal K u) = c ∧ ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 = inner ℝ c u ∧
      ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 ≤ q⁻¹ * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ∧
      ∀ z : PiLp 2 (fun b => K b), synth K z = c →
        ‖z‖ ^ 2 = ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 + ‖z - anal K u‖ ^ 2 := by
  let T : E →ₗ[ℝ] E := ∑ b, ((K b).starProjection : E →ₗ[ℝ] E)
  have hT : ∀ u, T u = ∑ b, (K b).starProjection u := fun u => by
    simp only [T, LinearMap.sum_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe]
  have hmaps : ∀ u ∈ F, T u ∈ F := fun u _ => by
    rw [hT]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun b _ => hK b ((K b).starProjection_apply_mem u)
  let TF : Module.End ℝ F := T.restrict hmaps
  have hTF : ∀ x : F, (TF x : E) = T x := fun _ => rfl
  have hinj : Function.Injective TF := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, LinearMap.ker_eq_bot']
    intro x hx
    have h0 : T x = 0 := by rw [← hTF, hx, Submodule.coe_zero]
    have h1 := hlow x x.2
    rw [← inner_sum_starProjection_self, ← hT, h0, inner_zero_left] at h1
    have h2 : ‖(x : E)‖ ^ 2 ≤ 0 := by nlinarith
    have h3 : ‖(x : E)‖ = 0 := by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (x : E)]
    exact Subtype.ext (by rw [norm_eq_zero.mp h3, Submodule.coe_zero])
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := LinearMap.injective_iff_surjective.mp hinj ⟨c, hc⟩
  have hTu : T u = c := by rw [← hTF, hu]
  have hJ : synth K (anal K u) = c := by rw [synth_anal, ← hT, hTu]
  have hS : ‖anal K u‖ ^ 2 = inner ℝ c (u : E) := by
    rw [norm_sq_anal, ← inner_sum_starProjection_self, ← hT, hTu]
  refine ⟨u, u.2, hJ, hS, ?_, fun z hz => min_norm_of_synth_eq K u z (hz.trans hJ.symm)⟩
  have hcs : inner ℝ c (u : E) ≤ ‖c‖ * ‖(u : E)‖ := real_inner_le_norm _ _
  have hl := hlow u u.2
  rw [← norm_sq_anal, hS] at hl
  rw [hS, le_inv_mul_iff₀ hq]
  nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hcs hq.le, mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hl hq.le,
    sq_nonneg (q * ‖(u : E)‖ - ‖c‖)]

/-! ## 2. §5.1: localization transfer -/

/-- **§5.1, localization transfer.** Chart spaces `E_i` (a finite family of real inner-product
spaces), bounded maps `A_i : E → E_i` and `B_i : E_i → E` with `∑_i B_i A_i = I`, `∑_i ‖A_i c‖² ≤ A₀
‖c‖²` and `‖B_i‖ ≤ B₀`; chart subspaces `K_{i,j}` (`j` in a finite type depending on `i`) such that
every `z ∈ E_i` splits as `∑_j z_j`, `z_j ∈ K_{i,j}`, `∑_j ‖z_j‖² ≤ C₀ ‖z‖²`; labels `b(i, j)` with
`B_i K_{i,j} ⊆ K_{b(i,j)}` and at most `M₀` pairs per label. Then every `c ∈ E` is `∑_b c_b` with
`c_b ∈ K_b` and `∑_b ‖c_b‖² ≤ M₀ B₀² C₀ A₀ ‖c‖²`. -/
theorem localization_transfer {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {β : Type*} [Fintype β] [DecidableEq β] (K : β → Submodule ℝ E)
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {Ec : ι → Type*} [∀ i, NormedAddCommGroup (Ec i)]
    [∀ i, InnerProductSpace ℝ (Ec i)] (A : ∀ i, E →L[ℝ] Ec i) (B : ∀ i, Ec i →L[ℝ] E)
    {κ : ι → Type*} [∀ i, Fintype (κ i)] (Kc : ∀ i, κ i → Submodule ℝ (Ec i))
    (lab : (Σ i, κ i) → β) {A₀ B₀ C₀ : ℝ} {M₀ : ℕ}
    (hrec : ∀ c, ∑ i, B i (A i c) = c)
    (hA : ∀ c, ∑ i, ‖A i c‖ ^ 2 ≤ A₀ * ‖c‖ ^ 2)
    (hB : ∀ i, ‖B i‖ ≤ B₀)
    (hsplit : ∀ i, ∀ z : Ec i, ∃ zj : κ i → Ec i, (∀ j, zj j ∈ Kc i j) ∧ ∑ j, zj j = z ∧
      ∑ j, ‖zj j‖ ^ 2 ≤ C₀ * ‖z‖ ^ 2)
    (hmap : ∀ i j, (Kc i j).map (B i : Ec i →ₗ[ℝ] E) ≤ K (lab ⟨i, j⟩))
    (hmult : ∀ b, #{p | lab p = b} ≤ M₀) (c : E) :
    ∃ cb : β → E, (∀ b, cb b ∈ K b) ∧ ∑ b, cb b = c ∧
      ∑ b, ‖cb b‖ ^ 2 ≤ M₀ * B₀ ^ 2 * C₀ * A₀ * ‖c‖ ^ 2 := by
  choose zj hzj hzsum hzle using fun i => hsplit i (A i c)
  let z : (Σ i, κ i) → E := fun p => B p.1 (zj p.1 p.2)
  have hzmem : ∀ p, z p ∈ K (lab p) := fun p =>
    hmap p.1 p.2 (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (hzj p.1 p.2))
  refine ⟨fun b => ∑ p with lab p = b, z p, fun b => Submodule.sum_mem _ fun p hp => ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [(mem_filter.mp hp).2.symm]; exact hzmem p
  · rw [sum_fiberwise univ lab z, Fintype.sum_sigma]
    calc ∑ i, ∑ j, z ⟨i, j⟩ = ∑ i, B i (∑ j, zj i j) := by
          refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
          rw [map_sum]
      _ = c := by simp only [hzsum]; exact hrec c
  · have hBz : ∀ p, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 ≤ B₀ ^ 2 * ‖zj p.1 p.2‖ ^ 2 := fun p => by
      have h1 : ‖z p‖ ≤ B₀ * ‖zj p.1 p.2‖ :=
        ((B p.1).le_opNorm _).trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hB p.1) (norm_nonneg _))
      calc ‖z p‖ ^ 2 ≤ (B₀ * ‖zj p.1 p.2‖) ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) h1 2
        _ = _ := by ring
    have hchart : ∑ i, ∑ j, ‖zj i j‖ ^ 2 ≤ C₀ * A₀ * ‖c‖ ^ 2 := by
      rcases le_or_gt 0 C₀ with hC | hC
      · calc ∑ i, ∑ j, ‖zj i j‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ i, C₀ * ‖A i c‖ ^ 2 := sum_le_sum fun i _ => hzle i
          _ = C₀ * ∑ i, ‖A i c‖ ^ 2 := by rw [mul_sum]
          _ ≤ C₀ * (A₀ * ‖c‖ ^ 2) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hA c) hC
          _ = _ := by ring
      · have hAi : ∀ i, A i c = 0 := fun i => by
          have h0 : 0 ≤ ∑ j, ‖zj i j‖ ^ 2 := sum_nonneg fun _ _ => sq_nonneg _
          have h1 := hzle i
          have h2 : ‖A i c‖ ^ 2 ≤ 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg ‖A i c‖]
          exact norm_eq_zero.mp (by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (A i c)])
        have hc0 : c = 0 := by rw [← hrec c]; simp [hAi]
        have hle0 : ∀ i, ∑ j, ‖zj i j‖ ^ 2 ≤ 0 := fun i => by
          have h1 := hzle i
          rw [hAi i, norm_zero] at h1
          simpa using h1
        rw [hc0, norm_zero]
        simpa using sum_nonpos fun i (_ : i ∈ univ) => hle0 i
    have hfib : ∀ b, ‖∑ p with lab p = b, z p‖ ^ 2 ≤ M₀ * ∑ p with lab p = b, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 :=
      fun b => by
        calc ‖∑ p with lab p = b, z p‖ ^ 2 ≤ (∑ p with lab p = b, ‖z p‖) ^ 2 :=
              pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) (norm_sum_le _ _) 2
          _ ≤ #{p | lab p = b} * ∑ p with lab p = b, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 := sq_sum_le_card_mul_sum_sq
          _ ≤ M₀ * ∑ p with lab p = b, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 :=
              mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (by exact_mod_cast hmult b)
                (sum_nonneg fun _ _ => sq_nonneg _)
    calc ∑ b, ‖∑ p with lab p = b, z p‖ ^ 2
        ≤ ∑ b, (M₀ : ℝ) * ∑ p with lab p = b, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 := sum_le_sum fun b _ => hfib b
      _ = M₀ * ∑ p, ‖z p‖ ^ 2 := by rw [← mul_sum, sum_fiberwise univ lab]
      _ ≤ M₀ * ∑ p, B₀ ^ 2 * ‖zj p.1 p.2‖ ^ 2 :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (sum_le_sum fun p _ => hBz p) (Nat.cast_nonneg _)
      _ = M₀ * B₀ ^ 2 * ∑ i, ∑ j, ‖zj i j‖ ^ 2 := by
          rw [← mul_sum, Fintype.sum_sigma, mul_assoc]
      _ ≤ M₀ * B₀ ^ 2 * (C₀ * A₀ * ‖c‖ ^ 2) := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hchart (by positivity)
      _ = _ := by ring


/-! ## 3. §5.2: one volume does not give all volumes -/

/-- The unit vector `(cos θ, sin θ)`. -/
noncomputable def dir (θ : ℝ) : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) := !₂[cos θ, sin θ]

/-- `‖(cos θ, sin θ)‖ = 1`. -/
theorem norm_dir (θ : ℝ) : ‖dir θ‖ = 1 := by
  have h : ‖dir θ‖ ^ 2 = 1 := by
    rw [EuclideanSpace.real_norm_sq_eq]; simp [dir, Fin.sum_univ_two, cos_sq_add_sin_sq]
  nlinarith [norm_nonneg (dir θ)]

/-- The system `K₁ = span e₁`, `K₂ = span (cos θ, sin θ)` in `ℝ²`. -/
noncomputable def angleSys (θ : ℝ) : Fin 2 → Submodule ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :=
  ![ℝ ∙ dir 0, ℝ ∙ dir θ]

/-- `⟨(cos θ, sin θ), x⟩ = cos θ x₀ + sin θ x₁`. -/
theorem inner_dir (θ : ℝ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    inner ℝ (dir θ) x = cos θ * x 0 + sin θ * x 1 := by
  simp [dir, PiLp.inner_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two]; ring

/-- `‖Π_{span(cos θ, sin θ)} x‖² = (cos θ x₀ + sin θ x₁)²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_proj_dir (θ : ℝ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    ‖(ℝ ∙ dir θ).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 = (cos θ * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 := by
  rw [Submodule.starProjection_unit_singleton ℝ (norm_dir θ), norm_smul, norm_dir, mul_one,
    Real.norm_eq_abs, sq_abs, inner_dir]

/-- `∑_b ‖Π_b x‖² = x₀² + (cos θ x₀ + sin θ x₁)²`. -/
theorem angleSys_form (θ : ℝ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    ∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 = x 0 ^ 2 + (cos θ * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 := by
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_two]
  simp only [angleSys, Matrix.cons_val_zero, Matrix.cons_val_one]
  rw [norm_sq_proj_dir, norm_sq_proj_dir]
  simp only [cos_zero, sin_zero, one_mul, zero_mul, add_zero]

/-- `‖x‖² = x₀² + x₁²` in `ℝ²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_two (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) : ‖x‖ ^ 2 = x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2 := by
  rw [EuclideanSpace.real_norm_sq_eq, Fin.sum_univ_two]

/-- The matrix `[[1 + cos² θ, cos θ sin θ], [cos θ sin θ, sin² θ]]` of `Π₁ + Π₂`. -/
noncomputable def angleMat (θ : ℝ) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℝ :=
  !![1 + cos θ ^ 2, cos θ * sin θ; cos θ * sin θ, sin θ ^ 2]

/-- `angleMat θ` is the matrix of the quadratic form `∑_b ‖Π_b x‖²`. -/
theorem angleMat_form (θ : ℝ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    dotProduct (fun i => x i) ((angleMat θ).mulVec fun i => x i) =
      ∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [angleSys_form]
  simp [angleMat, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  ring

/-- Its trace is `2`. -/
theorem angleMat_trace (θ : ℝ) : (angleMat θ).trace = 2 := by
  rw [angleMat, Matrix.trace_fin_two_of]; nlinarith [cos_sq_add_sin_sq θ]

/-- Its determinant is `sin² θ`. -/
theorem angleMat_det (θ : ℝ) : (angleMat θ).det = sin θ ^ 2 := by
  rw [angleMat, Matrix.det_fin_two_of]; nlinarith [cos_sq_add_sin_sq θ]

/-- `(sin θ, −(1 + cos θ))` is an eigenvector for `1 − cos θ`. -/
theorem angleMat_eig_low (θ : ℝ) :
    (angleMat θ).mulVec ![sin θ, -(1 + cos θ)] = (1 - cos θ) • ![sin θ, -(1 + cos θ)] := by
  have h := sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [angleMat, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two] <;>
    nlinarith [h]

/-- `(1 + cos θ, sin θ)` is an eigenvector for `1 + cos θ`. -/
theorem angleMat_eig_high (θ : ℝ) :
    (angleMat θ).mulVec ![1 + cos θ, sin θ] = (1 + cos θ) • ![1 + cos θ, sin θ] := by
  have h := sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [angleMat, Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, Fin.sum_univ_two] <;>
    first | linear_combination (sin θ) * h | linear_combination (cos θ) * h

/-- For `cos θ ≥ 0`: `∑_b ‖Π_b x‖² ≥ (1 − cos θ) ‖x‖²`. -/
theorem angleSys_lower {θ : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ cos θ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    (1 - cos θ) * ‖x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [angleSys_form, norm_sq_two]
  have h := sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  have key : (1 + cos θ) * (x 0 ^ 2 + (cos θ * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 -
      (1 - cos θ) * (x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2)) = cos θ * ((1 + cos θ) * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 := by
    have : sin θ ^ 2 = 1 - cos θ ^ 2 := by linarith
    ring_nf; rw [this]; ring
  have hpos : 0 < 1 + cos θ := by linarith
  have hr : 0 ≤ cos θ * ((1 + cos θ) * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 := by positivity
  rw [← key] at hr
  have h3 := (mul_nonneg_iff_of_pos_left hpos).mp hr
  linarith

/-- The eigenvector `(sin θ, −(1 + cos θ))` for the lower eigenvalue. -/
noncomputable def lowVec (θ : ℝ) : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2) := !₂[sin θ, -(1 + cos θ)]

/-- Equality in `angleSys_lower` at `lowVec θ`. -/
theorem angleSys_lowVec (θ : ℝ) :
    ∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection (lowVec θ)‖ ^ 2 = (1 - cos θ) * ‖lowVec θ‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [angleSys_form, norm_sq_two]
  simp only [lowVec]
  have h := sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  simp
  nlinarith [h]

/-- `lowVec θ ≠ 0` when `cos θ ≥ 0`. -/
theorem lowVec_ne_zero {θ : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ cos θ) : 0 < ‖lowVec θ‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [norm_sq_two]; simp [lowVec]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg (sin θ)]

/-- **The best lower bound of `Π₁ + Π₂` is exactly `1 − cos θ`** (for `cos θ ≥ 0`). -/
theorem angleSys_isGreatest {θ : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ cos θ) :
    IsGreatest {α : ℝ | ∀ x, α * ‖x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2}
      (1 - cos θ) := by
  refine ⟨fun x => angleSys_lower hc x, fun α hα => ?_⟩
  have h1 := hα (lowVec θ)
  rw [angleSys_lowVec] at h1
  exact le_of_mul_le_mul_right h1 (lowVec_ne_zero hc)

/-- The family `θ_q = π / (2 (q + 1))`, with `θ_0 = π/2`. -/
noncomputable def angleSeq (q : ℕ) : ℝ := π / (2 * (q + 1))

/-- `cos θ_q ≥ 0`. -/
theorem cos_angleSeq_nonneg (q : ℕ) : 0 ≤ cos (angleSeq q) := by
  apply cos_nonneg_of_mem_Icc
  constructor
  · have : 0 ≤ angleSeq q := by unfold angleSeq; positivity
    linarith [pi_pos]
  · unfold angleSeq
    rw [div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) (by norm_num)]
    have : (1 : ℝ) ≤ q + 1 := by have := Nat.cast_nonneg (α := ℝ) q; linarith
    nlinarith [pi_pos]

/-- At the first member the best lower bound is `1`. -/
theorem angleSeq_zero : 1 - cos (angleSeq 0) = 1 := by
  simp [angleSeq]

/-- The best lower bounds `1 − cos θ_q` tend to `0`. -/
theorem tendsto_angleSeq : Tendsto (fun q => 1 - cos (angleSeq q)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by
  have h1 : Tendsto angleSeq atTop (𝓝 0) := by
    unfold angleSeq
    have : Tendsto (fun q : ℕ => (2 * ((q : ℝ) + 1))) atTop atTop := by
      apply Tendsto.const_mul_atTop (by norm_num)
      exact tendsto_atTop_add_const_right _ 1 tendsto_natCast_atTop_atTop
    exact tendsto_const_nhds.div_atTop this
  have h2 := (continuous_cos.tendsto 0).comp h1
  simpa using (tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).sub h2

/-- **§5.2.** No `α > 0` is a lower bound of `Π₁ + Π₂` for every member of the family. -/
theorem no_uniform_lower :
    ¬ ∃ α > 0, ∀ q x, α * ‖x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ b, ‖(angleSys (angleSeq q) b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 := by
  rintro ⟨α, hα, h⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := (tendsto_angleSeq.eventually (gt_mem_nhds hα)).exists
  have := (angleSys_isGreatest (cos_angleSeq_nonneg q)).2 (h q)
  linarith


/-! ## 4. §6.1: fixed-space perturbation -/

/-- **§6.1.** If `⟨c, S c⟩ ≥ α ‖c‖²` and `|⟨c, (S̃ − S) c⟩| ≤ ε ‖c‖²` for all `c ∈ F`, then `⟨c, S̃
c⟩ ≥ (α − ε) ‖c‖²` on `F`. Self-adjointness is not needed. -/
theorem perturbation_lower {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (F : Submodule ℝ E) (S S' : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) {α ε : ℝ}
    (hS : ∀ c ∈ F, α * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ c (S c))
    (hpert : ∀ c ∈ F, |inner ℝ c ((S' - S) c)| ≤ ε * ‖c‖ ^ 2) :
    ∀ c ∈ F, (α - ε) * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ c (S' c) := by
  intro c hc
  have h1 := neg_abs_le (inner ℝ c ((S' - S) c))
  have h2 := hpert c hc
  have h3 := hS c hc
  rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, inner_sub_right] at h1 h2
  linarith

/-- For the system of §5.2, `|∑_b ‖Π_b x‖² − ‖x‖²| ≤ |cos θ| ‖x‖²` (used in the closed
applications). -/
theorem angleSys_pert (θ : ℝ) (x : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)) :
    |∑ b, ‖(angleSys θ b).starProjection x‖ ^ 2 - ‖x‖ ^ 2| ≤ |cos θ| * ‖x‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [angleSys_form, norm_sq_two]
  have h := sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  have e : x 0 ^ 2 + (cos θ * x 0 + sin θ * x 1) ^ 2 - (x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2) =
      cos θ * (cos θ * x 0 ^ 2 + 2 * sin θ * x 0 * x 1 - cos θ * x 1 ^ 2) := by
    linear_combination (x 1 ^ 2) * h
  rw [e, abs_mul]
  apply mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left _ (abs_nonneg _)
  have hN : 0 ≤ x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2 := by positivity
  have key : (x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2 -
      (cos θ * x 0 ^ 2 + 2 * sin θ * x 0 * x 1 - cos θ * x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2 =
      (sin θ * x 0 ^ 2 - 2 * cos θ * x 0 * x 1 - sin θ * x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2 := by
    linear_combination (-(x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2) * h
  have hsq : (cos θ * x 0 ^ 2 + 2 * sin θ * x 0 * x 1 - cos θ * x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2 ≤
      (x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2) ^ 2 := by
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (sin θ * x 0 ^ 2 - 2 * cos θ * x 0 * x 1 - sin θ * x 1 ^ 2)]
  exact abs_le_of_sq_le_sq' hsq hN |> fun h => abs_le.mpr h

/-- **§6.1, splitting part.** If `S ≥ α` on `F` and `S̃ = ∑_b Π_b` (with `K_b ≤ F`) satisfies `|⟨c,
(S̃ − S) c⟩| ≤ ε ‖c‖²` on `F` with `ε < α`, then every `c ∈ F` splits as `∑_b c_b`, `c_b ∈ K_b`,
with `∑_b ‖c_b‖² ≤ (α − ε)⁻¹ ‖c‖²`. -/
theorem perturbation_splitting {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (F : Submodule ℝ E) (K : ι → Submodule ℝ E)
    (hK : ∀ b, K b ≤ F) (S : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) {α ε : ℝ} (hεα : ε < α)
    (hS : ∀ c ∈ F, α * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ c (S c))
    (hpert : ∀ c ∈ F,
      |inner ℝ c ((∑ b, ((K b).starProjection : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) - S) c)| ≤ ε * ‖c‖ ^ 2)
    {c : E} (hc : c ∈ F) :
    ∃ cb : ι → E, (∀ b, cb b ∈ K b) ∧ ∑ b, cb b = c ∧
      ∑ b, ‖cb b‖ ^ 2 ≤ (α - ε)⁻¹ * ‖c‖ ^ 2 := by
  have hform : ∀ v, inner ℝ v ((∑ b, ((K b).starProjection : E →ₗ[ℝ] E)) v) =
      ∑ b, ‖(K b).starProjection v‖ ^ 2 := fun v => by
    rw [LinearMap.sum_apply, real_inner_comm]
    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe]
    exact inner_sum_starProjection_self K v
  have hlow : ∀ c ∈ F, (α - ε) * ‖c‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ b, ‖(K b).starProjection c‖ ^ 2 := fun c hc => by
    rw [← hform]; exact perturbation_lower F S _ hS hpert c hc
  obtain ⟨u, -, hJ, -, hle, -⟩ := stable_splitting_min_norm F K hK (sub_pos.mpr hεα) hlow hc
  refine ⟨fun b => (K b).starProjection u, fun b => (K b).starProjection_apply_mem u, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← synth_anal]; exact hJ
  · rw [← norm_sq_anal]; exact hle

/-! ## 5. §6.2: stability from the synthesis map -/

/-- `⟨v, J J* v⟩ = ‖J* v‖²` (the corrected form of "`‖Jv‖² = ⟨v, JJv⟩`" in §6.2). -/
theorem inner_comp_adjoint_self {K F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup K] [InnerProductSpace ℝ K]
    [CompleteSpace K] [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] [CompleteSpace F]
    (J : K →L[ℝ] F) (v : F) :
    inner ℝ v ((J ∘L ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J) v) = ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J v‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ← ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left,
    real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]

/-- **§6.2.** For bounded `J, J̃ : 𝒦 → F` between real Hilbert spaces, `J J* ≥ α` and `‖J̃ − J‖ ≤ δ
< √α` imply `J̃ J̃* ≥ (√α − δ)²`. -/
theorem synthesis_stability {K F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup K] [InnerProductSpace ℝ K]
    [CompleteSpace K] [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] [CompleteSpace F]
    (J J' : K →L[ℝ] F) {α δ : ℝ}
    (hJ : ∀ v, α * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ v ((J ∘L ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J) v))
    (hδ : ‖J' - J‖ ≤ δ) (hδα : δ < √α) (v : F) :
    (√α - δ) ^ 2 * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ v ((J' ∘L ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J') v) := by
  have hform := fun A : K →L[ℝ] F => inner_comp_adjoint_self A v
  have hJv := hJ v
  rw [hform] at hJv ⊢
  have hδ0 : 0 ≤ δ := (norm_nonneg _).trans hδ
  have hα0 : 0 ≤ α := by
    by_contra h
    push Not at h
    rw [Real.sqrt_eq_zero'.mpr h.le] at hδα
    linarith
  have h1 : √α * ‖v‖ ≤ ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J v‖ := by
    have h2 : √α * ‖v‖ = √(α * ‖v‖ ^ 2) := by
      rw [Real.sqrt_mul hα0, Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)]
    rw [h2]
    calc √(α * ‖v‖ ^ 2) ≤ √(‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J v‖ ^ 2) := Real.sqrt_le_sqrt hJv
      _ = _ := Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)
  have h3 : ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (J' - J) v‖ ≤ δ * ‖v‖ := by
    calc ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (J' - J) v‖ ≤ ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (J' - J)‖ * ‖v‖ :=
          ContinuousLinearMap.le_opNorm _ _
      _ = ‖J' - J‖ * ‖v‖ := by rw [LinearIsometryEquiv.norm_map]
      _ ≤ δ * ‖v‖ := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hδ (norm_nonneg _)
  have h4 : ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J' v =
      ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J v + ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (J' - J) v := by
    rw [map_sub]
    simp
  have h5 : (√α - δ) * ‖v‖ ≤ ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J' v‖ := by
    rw [h4]
    have := norm_sub_norm_le (ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J v)
      (-(ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint (J' - J) v))
    rw [sub_neg_eq_add, norm_neg] at this
    nlinarith
  have h6 : 0 ≤ (√α - δ) * ‖v‖ := mul_nonneg (by linarith) (norm_nonneg _)
  calc (√α - δ) ^ 2 * ‖v‖ ^ 2 = ((√α - δ) * ‖v‖) ^ 2 := by ring
    _ ≤ ‖ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint J' v‖ ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ h6 h5 2


/-! ## 6. §8.1: the vector response bound -/

/-- On `ℝ`, `⟨x, y⟩ = x y`. -/
theorem real_inner_apply (x y : ℝ) : inner ℝ x y = x * y := by
  simp [inner, mul_comm]

/-- `⟨∑_i t_i s_i, u⟩ = ∑_i t_i ⟨s_i, u⟩`. -/
theorem inner_sum_smul_left {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (t : ι → ℝ) (s : ι → E) (u : E) :
    inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • s i) u = ∑ i, t i * inner ℝ (s i) u := by
  rw [sum_inner]; simp [real_inner_smul_left]

/-- `‖∑_i t_i w_i‖² = tᵀ G t` for the Gram matrix `G_{ij} = ⟨w_i, w_j⟩`. -/
theorem norm_sq_sum_smul {F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F]
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (t : ι → ℝ) (w : ι → F) :
    ‖∑ i, t i • w i‖ ^ 2 = dotProduct t ((Matrix.gram ℝ w).mulVec t) := by
  rw [← real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, sum_inner]
  simp only [inner_sum, real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_smul_right, dotProduct, Matrix.mulVec,
    Matrix.gram_apply, mul_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by ring

/-- **§8.1, representer form.** Let `R : E → F` be linear (the role of `L^{1/2}`, with `𝒱(u) = ‖R
u‖²`) and let `w_i ∈ F` represent the score components, `⟨s_i, u⟩ = ⟨w_i, R u⟩` for all `u` (the
role of `L^{-1/2} s_i`). With `X_{ij} = ⟨w_i, w_j⟩`, for all `t` and `u`: `⟨t · s, u⟩² ≤ (tᵀ X t) ‖R
u‖²`. -/
theorem vector_response_bound {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    (R : E →ₗ[ℝ] F) (s : ι → E) (w : ι → F)
    (hw : ∀ i u, inner ℝ (s i) u = inner ℝ (w i) (R u)) (t : ι → ℝ) (u : E) :
    inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • s i) u ^ 2 ≤ dotProduct t ((Matrix.gram ℝ w).mulVec t) * ‖R u‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h1 : inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • s i) u = inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • w i) (R u) := by
    rw [inner_sum_smul_left, inner_sum_smul_left]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [hw]
  rw [h1, ← norm_sq_sum_smul, ← mul_pow]
  calc inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • w i) (R u) ^ 2 = |inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • w i) (R u)| ^ 2 := (sq_abs _).symm
    _ ≤ (‖∑ i, t i • w i‖ * ‖R u‖) ^ 2 :=
        pow_le_pow_left₀ (abs_nonneg _) (abs_real_inner_le_norm _ _) 2

/-- Cauchy–Schwarz for a symmetric `L` with `⟨u, L u⟩ ≥ 0`: `⟨x, L y⟩² ≤ ⟨x, L x⟩ ⟨y, L y⟩`. -/
theorem sq_inner_le_of_psd {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (L : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hsym : L.IsSymmetric) (hpos : ∀ u, 0 ≤ inner ℝ u (L u)) (x y : E) :
    inner ℝ x (L y) ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ x (L x) * inner ℝ y (L y) := by
  have hyx : inner ℝ y (L x) = inner ℝ x (L y) := by
    rw [real_inner_comm, hsym]
  have h := discrim_le_zero (a := inner ℝ y (L y)) (b := 2 * inner ℝ x (L y))
    (c := inner ℝ x (L x)) fun τ => by
      have := hpos (x + τ • y)
      simp only [map_add, map_smul, inner_add_left, inner_add_right, real_inner_smul_left,
        real_inner_smul_right, hyx] at this
      nlinarith
  unfold discrim at h
  nlinarith

/-- If `L` is symmetric, `L g = s` and `L g' = s'`, then `⟨s, g'⟩ = ⟨g, s'⟩`; so `⟨s_i, g_j⟩` does
not depend on the chosen solutions. -/
theorem inner_solve_symm {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (L : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hsym : L.IsSymmetric) {s s' g g' : E} (hg : L g = s) (hg' : L g' = s') :
    inner ℝ s g' = inner ℝ g s' := by
  rw [← hg, ← hg', hsym]

/-- **§8.1, finite-dimensional operator form.** For `L` symmetric with `⟨u, L u⟩ ≥ 0` and solutions
`L g_i = s_i`, with `X_{ij} = ⟨s_i, g_j⟩`: `⟨t · s, u⟩² ≤ (tᵀ X t) ⟨u, L u⟩`. -/
theorem vector_response_bound_solve {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (L : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hsym : L.IsSymmetric)
    (hpos : ∀ u, 0 ≤ inner ℝ u (L u)) (s g : ι → E) (hg : ∀ i, L (g i) = s i) (t : ι → ℝ)
    (u : E) :
    inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • s i) u ^ 2 ≤
      dotProduct t ((Matrix.of fun i j => inner ℝ (s i) (g j)).mulVec t) * inner ℝ u (L u) := by
  set gt := ∑ i, t i • g i
  have h1 : inner ℝ (∑ i, t i • s i) u = inner ℝ gt (L u) := by
    have : ∑ i, t i • s i = L gt := by simp [gt, map_sum, hg]
    rw [this, hsym]
  have h2 : inner ℝ gt (L gt) =
      dotProduct t ((Matrix.of fun i j => inner ℝ (s i) (g j)).mulVec t) := by
    simp only [gt, map_sum, map_smul, hg, inner_sum, sum_inner, real_inner_smul_left,
      real_inner_smul_right, dotProduct, Matrix.mulVec, Matrix.of_apply, mul_sum]
    rw [sum_comm]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun i _ => sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
    rw [← inner_solve_symm L hsym (hg i) (hg j)]
    ring
  rw [h1, ← h2]
  exact sq_inner_le_of_psd L hsym hpos gt u

/-- If `ker L = 0` on a finite-dimensional space, `L g = s` is solvable for every `s`. -/
theorem exists_solve {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] (L : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hker : ∀ u, L u = 0 → u = 0) (s : E) :
    ∃ g, L g = s := by
  have hinj : Function.Injective L := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, LinearMap.ker_eq_bot']; exact hker
  exact LinearMap.injective_iff_surjective.mp hinj s

/-! ## 7. §8.3: the Poisson residual identity, form-domain version

The finite-fibre version is `FiniteFibre2.chi_eq_certV_add`; this is the abstract statement in
which `L^{-1/2} s` is a representer, as in the note ("the left side means `‖L^{-1/2} s‖²` even
when `L⁻¹ s` is not an `L²` vector"). -/

/-- **§8.3, form-domain version.** Let `w` represent `s` (`⟨s, u⟩ = ⟨w, R u⟩`, so `w` plays
`L^{-1/2} s`) and let `L h` be represented by `R h` (`⟨L h, u⟩ = ⟨R h, R u⟩`). Then `w − R h`
represents `r = s − L h`, and `‖w‖² = 2 ⟨s, h⟩ − ⟨h, L h⟩ + ‖w − R h‖²`. -/
theorem poisson_residual {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F] (R : E →ₗ[ℝ] F) {s : E} {w : F}
    (hw : ∀ u, inner ℝ s u = inner ℝ w (R u)) {h Lh : E}
    (hLh : ∀ u, inner ℝ Lh u = inner ℝ (R h) (R u)) :
    (∀ u, inner ℝ (s - Lh) u = inner ℝ (w - R h) (R u)) ∧
      ‖w‖ ^ 2 = 2 * inner ℝ s h - inner ℝ h Lh + ‖w - R h‖ ^ 2 := by
  refine ⟨fun u => by rw [inner_sub_left, inner_sub_left, hw, hLh], ?_⟩
  have e1 : inner ℝ h Lh = ‖R h‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [real_inner_comm, hLh, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]
  have e2 : inner ℝ s h = inner ℝ w (R h) := hw h
  rw [e1, e2, norm_sub_sq_real]
  ring

/-! ## 8. §8.2: the inter-fibre comparison -/

/-- Minkowski's inequality in `L²(ν; ℝ^ι)` for weights `ν ≥ 0`. -/
theorem weighted_minkowski {Y ι : Type*} [Fintype Y] [Fintype ι] (ν : Y → ℝ)
    (hν : ∀ y, 0 ≤ ν y) (a b : Y → ι → ℝ) :
    √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (a y + b y) (a y + b y)) ≤
      √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (a y) (a y)) + √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (b y) (b y)) := by
  let emb : (Y → ι → ℝ) → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Y × ι) :=
    fun c => WithLp.toLp 2 (fun p => √(ν p.1) * c p.1 p.2)
  have hn : ∀ c, ‖emb c‖ = √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (c y) (c y)) := fun c => by
    rw [EuclideanSpace.norm_eq]
    congr 1
    rw [Fintype.sum_prod_type]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun y _ => ?_
    simp only [emb, Real.norm_eq_abs, sq_abs, mul_pow, Real.sq_sqrt (hν y), dotProduct, mul_sum]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun k _ => by ring
  have hadd : emb (a + b) = emb a + emb b := by
    ext p; simp [emb, mul_add]
  rw [← hn, ← hn, ← hn]
  have : (fun y => a y + b y) = a + b := rfl
  calc ‖emb (a + b)‖ = ‖emb a + emb b‖ := by rw [hadd]
    _ ≤ ‖emb a‖ + ‖emb b‖ := norm_add_le _ _

/-- `xᵀ (Sᵀ S) x = ‖S x‖²`. -/
theorem quad_transpose_mul {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (S : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (x : ι → ℝ) :
    dotProduct x ((Sᵀ * S).mulVec x) = dotProduct (S.mulVec x) (S.mulVec x) := by
  rw [← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, Matrix.dotProduct_mulVec, ← Matrix.mulVec_transpose,
    Matrix.transpose_transpose]

/-- `vᵀ (S X Sᵀ) v = (Sᵀ v)ᵀ X (Sᵀ v)`. -/
theorem quad_conj {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (S X : Matrix ι ι ℝ) (v : ι → ℝ) :
    dotProduct v ((S * X * Sᵀ).mulVec v) =
      dotProduct (Sᵀ.mulVec v) (X.mulVec (Sᵀ.mulVec v)) := by
  rw [← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, ← Matrix.mulVec_mulVec, Matrix.dotProduct_mulVec,
    ← Matrix.mulVec_transpose]

/-- **§8.2, from the response inequality.** On a finite coarse space with weights `ν ≥ 0`, let `M(y)
= S(y)ᵀ S(y)`, `∇g(y) = h(y) + r(y)`, `(t · r(y))² ≤ (tᵀ X(y) t) 𝒱_y` for all `t` (the conclusion of
§8.1), `𝒱_y ≥ 0`, `S X Sᵀ ≤ χ²` and `χ ≥ 0`. Then `√E_B ≤ √H + χ √V` with `E_B = ∑_y ν ∇gᵀ M ∇g`, `H
= ∑_y ν hᵀ M h` and `V = ∑_y ν 𝒱_y`. -/
theorem inter_fibre_comparison_of_response {Y ι : Type*} [Fintype Y] [Fintype ι]
    (ν : Y → ℝ) (hν : ∀ y, 0 ≤ ν y) (S M X : Y → Matrix ι ι ℝ)
    (hM : ∀ y, M y = (S y)ᵀ * S y) (G h r : Y → ι → ℝ) (V : Y → ℝ) {χ : ℝ}
    (hV : ∀ y, 0 ≤ V y) (hG : ∀ y, G y = h y + r y)
    (hresp : ∀ y t, dotProduct t (r y) ^ 2 ≤ dotProduct t ((X y).mulVec t) * V y)
    (hX : ∀ y v, dotProduct v ((S y * X y * (S y)ᵀ).mulVec v) ≤ χ ^ 2 * dotProduct v v)
    (hχ : 0 ≤ χ) :
    √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (G y) ((M y).mulVec (G y))) ≤
      √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (h y) ((M y).mulVec (h y))) + χ * √(∑ y, ν y * V y) := by
  have hres : ∀ y, dotProduct ((S y).mulVec (r y)) ((S y).mulVec (r y)) ≤ χ ^ 2 * V y := by
    intro y
    set v := (S y).mulVec (r y)
    have e1 : dotProduct v v = dotProduct ((S y)ᵀ.mulVec v) (r y) := by
      conv_lhs => rw [show v = (S y).mulVec (r y) from rfl]
      rw [Matrix.dotProduct_mulVec, ← Matrix.mulVec_transpose]
    have h1 := hresp y ((S y)ᵀ.mulVec v)
    rw [← e1, ← quad_conj] at h1
    have h2 := hX y v
    have hvv : 0 ≤ dotProduct v v := by
      simp only [dotProduct]; exact sum_nonneg fun i _ => mul_self_nonneg _
    have h3 : dotProduct v v ^ 2 ≤ χ ^ 2 * dotProduct v v * V y :=
      h1.trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right h2 (hV y))
    rcases hvv.eq_or_lt with h0 | hpos
    · rw [← h0]; exact mul_nonneg (sq_nonneg _) (hV y)
    · nlinarith
  have hEB : ∀ y, dotProduct (G y) ((M y).mulVec (G y)) =
      dotProduct ((S y).mulVec (h y) + (S y).mulVec (r y))
        ((S y).mulVec (h y) + (S y).mulVec (r y)) := fun y => by
    rw [hM, quad_transpose_mul, hG, Matrix.mulVec_add]
  have hH : ∀ y, dotProduct (h y) ((M y).mulVec (h y)) =
      dotProduct ((S y).mulVec (h y)) ((S y).mulVec (h y)) := fun y => by
    rw [hM, quad_transpose_mul]
  simp only [hEB, hH]
  refine (weighted_minkowski ν hν (fun y => (S y).mulVec (h y))
    (fun y => (S y).mulVec (r y))).trans (add_le_add le_rfl ?_)
  calc √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct ((S y).mulVec (r y)) ((S y).mulVec (r y)))
      ≤ √(∑ y, ν y * (χ ^ 2 * V y)) :=
        Real.sqrt_le_sqrt (sum_le_sum fun y _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hres y) (hν y))
    _ = χ * √(∑ y, ν y * V y) := by
        rw [show ∑ y, ν y * (χ ^ 2 * V y) = χ ^ 2 * ∑ y, ν y * V y by
          rw [mul_sum]; exact sum_congr rfl fun y _ => by ring]
        rw [Real.sqrt_mul (sq_nonneg _), Real.sqrt_sq hχ]

/-- **§8.2.** The inter-fibre comparison with the response inequality supplied by
`vector_response_bound` fibre by fibre: the fibre at `y` is a real inner-product space `E_y`, `u_y =
f_y − g(y)`, `r_y = (⟨s_{y,i}, u_y⟩)_i`, `𝒱_y = ‖R_y u_y‖²` and `X(y)` the Gram matrix of the
representers. Taking `S = M^{1/2}` gives the note's hypothesis `M^{1/2} X M^{1/2} ≤ χ²`. -/
theorem inter_fibre_comparison {Y ι : Type*} [Fintype Y] [Fintype ι]
    {E Fe : Y → Type*} [∀ y, NormedAddCommGroup (E y)] [∀ y, InnerProductSpace ℝ (E y)]
    [∀ y, NormedAddCommGroup (Fe y)] [∀ y, InnerProductSpace ℝ (Fe y)]
    (ν : Y → ℝ) (hν : ∀ y, 0 ≤ ν y) (R : ∀ y, E y →ₗ[ℝ] Fe y) (s : ∀ y, ι → E y)
    (w : ∀ y, ι → Fe y) (hw : ∀ y i u, inner ℝ (s y i) u = inner ℝ (w y i) (R y u))
    (u : ∀ y, E y) (S M : Y → Matrix ι ι ℝ) (hM : ∀ y, M y = (S y)ᵀ * S y)
    (G h : Y → ι → ℝ) {χ : ℝ} (hχ : 0 ≤ χ)
    (hG : ∀ y, G y = h y + fun i => inner ℝ (s y i) (u y))
    (hX : ∀ y v, dotProduct v ((S y * Matrix.gram ℝ (w y) * (S y)ᵀ).mulVec v) ≤
      χ ^ 2 * dotProduct v v) :
    √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (G y) ((M y).mulVec (G y))) ≤
      √(∑ y, ν y * dotProduct (h y) ((M y).mulVec (h y))) +
        χ * √(∑ y, ν y * ‖R y (u y)‖ ^ 2) := by
  refine inter_fibre_comparison_of_response ν hν S M (fun y => Matrix.gram ℝ (w y)) hM G h
    (fun y i => inner ℝ (s y i) (u y)) (fun y => ‖R y (u y)‖ ^ 2) (fun y => sq_nonneg _) hG
    (fun y t => ?_) hX hχ
  have := vector_response_bound (R y) (s y) (w y) (hw y) t (u y)
  rwa [inner_sum_smul_left] at this


/-! ## 9. §9.1: the algebraic step of the two-level bound -/

/-- `C*(A, B, D) = (A + D + √((A − D)² + 4B²))/2`, the largest eigenvalue of `[[A, B], [B, D]]`. -/
noncomputable def cstar (A B D : ℝ) : ℝ := (A + D + √((A - D) ^ 2 + 4 * B ^ 2)) / 2

/-- `C* ≥ A`, `C* ≥ D` and `(C* − A)(C* − D) = B²`. -/
theorem cstar_spec (A B D : ℝ) :
    A ≤ cstar A B D ∧ D ≤ cstar A B D ∧ (cstar A B D - A) * (cstar A B D - D) = B ^ 2 := by
  have h0 : 0 ≤ (A - D) ^ 2 + 4 * B ^ 2 := by positivity
  have hs := Real.sq_sqrt h0
  have hge : |A - D| ≤ √((A - D) ^ 2 + 4 * B ^ 2) := by
    rw [← Real.sqrt_sq_eq_abs]; exact Real.sqrt_le_sqrt (by nlinarith [sq_nonneg B])
  have h1 := le_abs_self (A - D)
  have h2 := neg_abs_le (A - D)
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · unfold cstar; linarith
  · unfold cstar; linarith
  · unfold cstar; nlinarith

/-- **`A x² + 2 B x y + D y² ≤ C* (x² + y²)`** for all real `x, y`. -/
theorem quad_le_cstar (A B D x y : ℝ) :
    A * x ^ 2 + 2 * B * x * y + D * y ^ 2 ≤ cstar A B D * (x ^ 2 + y ^ 2) := by
  obtain ⟨hA, hD, hprod⟩ := cstar_spec A B D
  set C := cstar A B D
  have key : (C - A) * ((C - A) * x ^ 2 - 2 * B * x * y + (C - D) * y ^ 2) =
      ((C - A) * x - B * y) ^ 2 := by
    linear_combination y ^ 2 * hprod
  rcases (sub_nonneg.mpr hA).eq_or_lt with h0 | hpos
  · have hB : B ^ 2 = 0 := by rw [← hprod, ← h0, zero_mul]
    have hB' : B = 0 := pow_eq_zero_iff (n := 2) (by norm_num) |>.mp hB
    have hCA : C = A := by linarith
    subst hB'
    rw [hCA] at hD
    nlinarith [mul_nonneg (sub_nonneg.mpr hD) (sq_nonneg y)]
  · have : 0 ≤ (C - A) * x ^ 2 - 2 * B * x * y + (C - D) * y ^ 2 := by
      have h := sq_nonneg ((C - A) * x - B * y)
      rw [← key] at h
      exact (mul_nonneg_iff_of_pos_left hpos).mp h
    nlinarith

/-- `C*(A, 0, D) = max(A, D)`. -/
theorem cstar_zero (A D : ℝ) : cstar A 0 D = max A D := by
  unfold cstar
  rw [show (A - D) ^ 2 + 4 * (0 : ℝ) ^ 2 = (A - D) ^ 2 by ring, Real.sqrt_sq_eq_abs]
  rcases le_total A D with h | h
  · rw [max_eq_right h, abs_of_nonpos (by linarith)]; ring
  · rw [max_eq_left h, abs_of_nonneg (by linarith)]; ring

/-- `λ⁻¹ V + γ⁻¹ (√H + χ √V)² = A (√V)² + 2 B √V √H + D (√H)²` with `A = λ⁻¹ + χ²/γ`, `B = χ/γ`, `D
= γ⁻¹`. -/
theorem expand_bridge {V H lam γ χ : ℝ} (hV : 0 ≤ V) :
    lam⁻¹ * V + γ⁻¹ * (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 =
      (lam⁻¹ + χ ^ 2 / γ) * √V ^ 2 + 2 * (χ / γ) * √V * √H + γ⁻¹ * √H ^ 2 := by
  calc lam⁻¹ * V + γ⁻¹ * (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 = lam⁻¹ * √V ^ 2 + γ⁻¹ * (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 := by
        rw [Real.sq_sqrt hV]
    _ = _ := by ring

/-- **§9.1, algebraic step.** From `Var = v̄ + Var_ν(g)`, `v̄ ≤ λ⁻¹ V`, `Var_ν(g) ≤ γ⁻¹ E_B`, `√E_B
≤ √H + χ √V`, `V, H, E_B ≥ 0` and `γ > 0`: `Var ≤ C*(λ⁻¹ + χ²/γ, χ/γ, γ⁻¹) (V + H)`. -/
theorem two_level_bound {Var vbar varg V H EB lam γ χ : ℝ} (hγ : 0 < γ)
    (hV : 0 ≤ V) (hH : 0 ≤ H) (hEB : 0 ≤ EB)
    (htv : Var = vbar + varg) (hfib : vbar ≤ lam⁻¹ * V) (hcoarse : varg ≤ γ⁻¹ * EB)
    (hcomp : √EB ≤ √H + χ * √V) :
    Var ≤ cstar (lam⁻¹ + χ ^ 2 / γ) (χ / γ) γ⁻¹ * (V + H) := by
  have h1 : EB ≤ (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 := by
    rw [← Real.sq_sqrt hEB]; exact pow_le_pow_left₀ (Real.sqrt_nonneg _) hcomp 2
  have h2 : Var ≤ lam⁻¹ * V + γ⁻¹ * (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 := by
    rw [htv]
    have := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h1 (inv_nonneg.mpr hγ.le)
    linarith
  have h3 := quad_le_cstar (lam⁻¹ + χ ^ 2 / γ) (χ / γ) γ⁻¹ (√V) (√H)
  rw [← expand_bridge hV, Real.sq_sqrt hV, Real.sq_sqrt hH] at h3
  linarith


/-! ## 10. §10.1: pair representation and the normalised cube energy -/

/-- The identity of §10.1 on one fibre: for weights `a ≥ 0` with total `ν` and mean `m`, `∑ a (f −
m)² = ½ ν ∑∑ (a/ν)(a'/ν)(f − f')²`. -/
theorem fibre_identity {Ω : Type*} [Fintype Ω] (a f : Ω → ℝ) (ha : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ a ω) :
    ∑ ω, a ω * (f ω - ∑ ω', a ω' / (∑ ω'', a ω'') * f ω') ^ 2 =
      1 / 2 * (∑ ω'', a ω'') *
        ∑ ω, ∑ ω', a ω / (∑ ω'', a ω'') * (a ω' / (∑ ω'', a ω'')) * (f ω - f ω') ^ 2 := by
  set ν := ∑ ω'', a ω''
  rcases (sum_nonneg fun ω (_ : ω ∈ univ) => ha ω).eq_or_lt with h0 | hpos
  · have hz : ∀ ω, a ω = 0 := fun ω =>
      (sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg fun ω _ => ha ω).mp h0.symm ω (mem_univ ω)
    simp [hz]
  · set A := ∑ ω, a ω * f ω ^ 2
    set B := ∑ ω, a ω * f ω
    have hm : ∑ ω', a ω' / ν * f ω' = B / ν := by
      rw [sum_div]; exact sum_congr rfl fun ω _ => by ring
    have e1 : ∑ ω, a ω * (f ω - B / ν) ^ 2 = A - 2 * (B / ν) * B + (B / ν) ^ 2 * ν := by
      have : ∀ ω, a ω * (f ω - B / ν) ^ 2 =
          a ω * f ω ^ 2 - 2 * (B / ν) * (a ω * f ω) + (B / ν) ^ 2 * a ω := fun ω => by ring
      simp only [this, sum_add_distrib, sum_sub_distrib, ← mul_sum, A, B, ν]
    have e2 : ∑ ω, ∑ ω', a ω / ν * (a ω' / ν) * (f ω - f ω') ^ 2 =
        (A * ν - 2 * B * B + ν * A) / ν ^ 2 := by
      have : ∀ ω ω', a ω / ν * (a ω' / ν) * (f ω - f ω') ^ 2 =
          ((a ω * f ω ^ 2) * a ω' - 2 * ((a ω * f ω) * (a ω' * f ω')) + a ω * (a ω' * f ω' ^ 2)) /
            ν ^ 2 := fun ω ω' => by field_simp; ring
      simp only [this, ← sum_div]
      congr 1
      simp only [sum_add_distrib, sum_sub_distrib, ← mul_sum, ← sum_mul, A, B, ν]
      ring
    have hν0 : ν ≠ 0 := hpos.ne'
    rw [hm, e1, e2]
    field_simp
    ring

/-- The exterior marginal `ν(η) = μ{e = η}`. -/
def margW {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq H] (μ : Ω → ℝ) (e : Ω → H) (η : H) : ℝ :=
  ∑ ω with e ω = η, μ ω

/-- The conditional law `μ^η` given the exterior `η`: `μ` restricted to `{e = η}` and normalised. -/
noncomputable def condLaw {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq H] (μ : Ω → ℝ) (e : Ω → H)
    (η : H) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  if e ω = η then μ ω / margW μ e η else 0

/-- The conditional expectation `P f (ω) = ∑_{ω'} μ^{e ω}(ω') f(ω')`. -/
noncomputable def condExp {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq H] (μ : Ω → ℝ) (e : Ω → H)
    (f : Ω → ℝ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑ ω', condLaw μ e (e ω) ω' * f ω'

/-- **§10.1, pair representation.** For weights `μ ≥ 0` on a finite configuration space and an
exterior map `e`: `‖f − P f‖²_μ = ½ ∑_η ν(η) ∑_{u, v} μ^η(u) μ^η(v) (f(u) − f(v))²`. -/
theorem pair_representation {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [Fintype H] [DecidableEq H]
    (μ : Ω → ℝ) (hμ : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ μ ω) (e : Ω → H) (f : Ω → ℝ) :
    ∑ ω, μ ω * (f ω - condExp μ e f ω) ^ 2 =
      1 / 2 * ∑ η, margW μ e η *
        ∑ u, ∑ v, condLaw μ e η u * condLaw μ e η v * (f u - f v) ^ 2 := by
  rw [← sum_fiberwise univ e, mul_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun η _ => ?_
  let a : Ω → ℝ := fun ω => if e ω = η then μ ω else 0
  have ha : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ a ω := fun ω => by simp only [a]; split_ifs <;> simp [hμ]
  have hν : margW μ e η = ∑ ω, a ω := by simp only [margW, a, sum_filter]
  have hc : ∀ ω, condLaw μ e η ω = a ω / ∑ ω'', a ω'' := fun ω => by
    simp only [condLaw, a, ← hν]; split_ifs <;> simp
  have hL : ∑ ω with e ω = η, μ ω * (f ω - condExp μ e f ω) ^ 2 =
      ∑ ω, a ω * (f ω - ∑ ω', a ω' / (∑ ω'', a ω'') * f ω') ^ 2 := by
    rw [sum_filter]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun ω _ => ?_
    by_cases h : e ω = η
    · have haω : a ω = μ ω := by simp [a, h]
      rw [if_pos h, haω]
      simp only [condExp, h, hc]
    · have haω : a ω = 0 := by simp [a, h]
      rw [if_neg h, haω]; simp
  rw [hL, fibre_identity a f ha, hν]
  simp only [hc]
  ring

/-- `ν(η) ≥ 0`. -/
theorem margW_nonneg {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq H] {μ : Ω → ℝ}
    (hμ : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ μ ω) (e : Ω → H) (η : H) : 0 ≤ margW μ e η :=
  sum_nonneg fun ω _ => hμ ω

/-- `μ^η(ω) ≥ 0`. -/
theorem condLaw_nonneg {Ω H : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq H] {μ : Ω → ℝ}
    (hμ : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ μ ω) (e : Ω → H) (η : H) (ω : Ω) : 0 ≤ condLaw μ e η ω := by
  unfold condLaw; split_ifs
  · exact div_nonneg (hμ ω) (margW_nonneg hμ e η)
  · exact le_rfl

/-- The normalised cube energy `ℰ_n(f) = n⁻⁴ ∑_x ‖f − P_x f‖²_μ` for finitely many cubes `x` with
exterior maps `ext x`. -/
noncomputable def cubeEnergy {Ω X : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [Fintype X] {H : X → Type*}
    [∀ x, DecidableEq (H x)] (n : ℕ) (μ : Ω → ℝ) (ext : ∀ x, Ω → H x) (f : Ω → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  1 / (n : ℝ) ^ 4 * ∑ x, ∑ ω, μ ω * (f ω - condExp μ (ext x) f ω) ^ 2

/-- `D_n f` in the pair space: the coordinate at `(x, η, u, v)` is `√(ν_x(η) μ_x^η(u) μ_x^η(v))
(2n⁴)^{-1/2} (f(u) − f(v))`. -/
noncomputable def pairVec {Ω X : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [Fintype X] {H : X → Type*}
    [∀ x, Fintype (H x)] [∀ x, DecidableEq (H x)] (n : ℕ) (μ : Ω → ℝ) (ext : ∀ x, Ω → H x)
    (f : Ω → ℝ) : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Σ x, H x × Ω × Ω) :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 fun p => √(margW μ (ext p.1) p.2.1 * condLaw μ (ext p.1) p.2.1 p.2.2.1 *
    condLaw μ (ext p.1) p.2.1 p.2.2.2) * (1 / √(2 * (n : ℝ) ^ 4) * (f p.2.2.1 - f p.2.2.2))

/-- **§10.1, normalisation.** `‖D_n f‖² = ℰ_n(f)` for `n > 0`. -/
theorem norm_pairVec_sq {Ω X : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [Fintype X] {H : X → Type*}
    [∀ x, Fintype (H x)] [∀ x, DecidableEq (H x)] {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) {μ : Ω → ℝ}
    (hμ : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ μ ω) (ext : ∀ x, Ω → H x) (f : Ω → ℝ) :
    ‖pairVec n μ ext f‖ ^ 2 = cubeEnergy n μ ext f := by
  have hn' : (0 : ℝ) < 2 * (n : ℝ) ^ 4 := by positivity
  have hterm : ∀ (x : X) (η : H x) (u v : Ω), (pairVec n μ ext f).ofLp ⟨x, (η, u, v)⟩ ^ 2 =
      1 / (2 * (n : ℝ) ^ 4) * (margW μ (ext x) η *
        (condLaw μ (ext x) η u * condLaw μ (ext x) η v * (f u - f v) ^ 2)) := by
    intro x η u v
    have hw : 0 ≤ margW μ (ext x) η * condLaw μ (ext x) η u * condLaw μ (ext x) η v :=
      mul_nonneg (mul_nonneg (margW_nonneg hμ _ _) (condLaw_nonneg hμ _ _ _))
        (condLaw_nonneg hμ _ _ _)
    simp only [pairVec, mul_pow, Real.sq_sqrt hw, div_pow, Real.sq_sqrt hn'.le, one_pow]
    ring
  rw [EuclideanSpace.real_norm_sq_eq, Fintype.sum_sigma]
  simp only [Fintype.sum_prod_type, hterm]
  rw [cubeEnergy, mul_sum]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
  rw [pair_representation μ hμ (ext x) f]
  simp only [← mul_sum]
  field_simp

/-! ## 11. §10.2: the energy-factorization criterion -/

/-- **§10.2.** If `V(f) = ‖T_V f‖²`, `H(f) = ‖T_H f‖²`, `‖D f‖² = ℰ(f)` and `(T_V f, T_H f) = A (D
f)` for a bounded `A : 𝒵 → 𝒱 ⊕ ℋ` with `‖A‖² ≤ K`, then `V(f) + H(f) ≤ K ℰ(f)`. -/
theorem energy_factorization {𝒟 Z V H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup Z] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Z]
    [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [NormedAddCommGroup H]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] (Vf Hf En : 𝒟 → ℝ) (TV : 𝒟 → V) (TH : 𝒟 → H) (D : 𝒟 → Z)
    (A : Z →L[ℝ] WithLp 2 (V × H)) {K : ℝ}
    (hV : ∀ f, Vf f = ‖TV f‖ ^ 2) (hH : ∀ f, Hf f = ‖TH f‖ ^ 2) (hD : ∀ f, ‖D f‖ ^ 2 = En f)
    (hA : ∀ f, WithLp.toLp 2 (TV f, TH f) = A (D f)) (hK : ‖A‖ ^ 2 ≤ K) (f : 𝒟) :
    Vf f + Hf f ≤ K * En f := by
  have h1 : Vf f + Hf f = ‖A (D f)‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [← hA, WithLp.prod_norm_sq_eq_of_L2, hV, hH]; rfl
  rw [h1, ← hD]
  calc ‖A (D f)‖ ^ 2 ≤ (‖A‖ * ‖D f‖) ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) (A.le_opNorm _) 2
    _ = ‖A‖ ^ 2 * ‖D f‖ ^ 2 := by ring
    _ ≤ K * ‖D f‖ ^ 2 := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hK (sq_nonneg _)

/-- The inclusion `z ↦ (z, 0)` of `Z` into the `ℓ²` sum `Z ⊕ H`. -/
noncomputable def inlL2 (Z H : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup Z] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Z]
    [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] : Z →L[ℝ] WithLp 2 (Z × H) :=
  LinearMap.mkContinuous
    { toFun := fun z => WithLp.toLp 2 (z, 0)
      map_add' := fun x y => by
        rw [← WithLp.toLp_add]; simp
      map_smul' := fun c x => by
        rw [RingHom.id_apply, ← WithLp.toLp_smul]; simp }
    1 fun z => by
      have h := WithLp.prod_norm_sq_eq_of_L2 (WithLp.toLp 2 ((z, 0) : Z × H))
      simp only [LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, one_mul]
      simp only [WithLp.toLp_fst, WithLp.toLp_snd, norm_zero, ne_eq, OfNat.ofNat_ne_zero,
        not_false_eq_true, zero_pow, add_zero] at h
      exact le_of_eq (by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (WithLp.toLp 2 ((z, 0) : Z × H)), norm_nonneg z])

/-- `‖inlL2‖ ≤ 1`. -/
theorem norm_inlL2_le (Z H : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup Z] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Z]
    [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] : ‖inlL2 Z H‖ ≤ 1 :=
  LinearMap.mkContinuous_norm_le _ zero_le_one _

/-- `inlL2 z = (z, 0)`. -/
theorem inlL2_apply (Z H : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup Z] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Z]
    [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] (z : Z) :
    inlL2 Z H z = WithLp.toLp 2 (z, 0) := rfl

/-- **§10.2 for the cube energy:** `V(f) + H(f) ≤ K ℰ_n(f)` when `(T_V f, T_H f) = A (D_n f)` and
`‖A‖² ≤ K`. -/
theorem energy_factorization_cube {Ω X : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [Fintype X] {H : X → Type*}
    [∀ x, Fintype (H x)] [∀ x, DecidableEq (H x)] {n : ℕ} (hn : 0 < n) {μ : Ω → ℝ}
    (hμ : ∀ ω, 0 ≤ μ ω) (ext : ∀ x, Ω → H x) {V Hs : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [NormedAddCommGroup Hs] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Hs]
    (Vf Hf : (Ω → ℝ) → ℝ) (TV : (Ω → ℝ) → V) (TH : (Ω → ℝ) → Hs)
    (A : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Σ x, H x × Ω × Ω) →L[ℝ] WithLp 2 (V × Hs)) {K : ℝ}
    (hV : ∀ f, Vf f = ‖TV f‖ ^ 2) (hH : ∀ f, Hf f = ‖TH f‖ ^ 2)
    (hA : ∀ f, WithLp.toLp 2 (TV f, TH f) = A (pairVec n μ ext f)) (hK : ‖A‖ ^ 2 ≤ K)
    (f : Ω → ℝ) :
    Vf f + Hf f ≤ K * cubeEnergy n μ ext f :=
  energy_factorization Vf Hf (cubeEnergy n μ ext) TV TH (pairVec n μ ext) A hV hH
    (fun f => norm_pairVec_sq hn hμ ext f) hA hK f


/-! ## 12. §10.3: gradient energy is not bounded by resampling energy -/

/-- The mean for the normalised Lebesgue measure on `[0, 2π]`. -/
noncomputable def circMean (f : ℝ → ℝ) : ℝ := 1 / (2 * π) * ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), f θ

/-- The variance, which is the full-resampling energy `‖f − P f‖²` with `P f` the mean. -/
noncomputable def circVar (f : ℝ → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  1 / (2 * π) * ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), (f θ - circMean f) ^ 2

/-- The gradient energy `(1/2π) ∫₀^{2π} |f′|²`. -/
noncomputable def gradEnergy (f : ℝ → ℝ) : ℝ := 1 / (2 * π) * ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), deriv f θ ^ 2

/-- `∫₀^{2π} sin(jθ) dθ = 0` for `j ≥ 1`. -/
theorem integral_sin_nat_mul {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) : ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), sin (j * θ) = 0 := by
  have hj' : (j : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hj.ne'
  rw [intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_left (fun x => sin x) hj', integral_sin]
  rw [show (j : ℝ) * (2 * π) = j * (2 * π) from rfl, cos_nat_mul_two_pi]
  simp

/-- `∫₀^{2π} sin²(jθ) dθ = π` for `j ≥ 1`. -/
theorem integral_sin_sq_nat_mul {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) :
    ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), sin (j * θ) ^ 2 = π := by
  have hj' : (j : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hj.ne'
  rw [intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_left (fun x => sin x ^ 2) hj', integral_sin_sq]
  have h1 : sin ((j : ℝ) * (2 * π)) = 0 := by
    rw [show (j : ℝ) * (2 * π) = ((2 * j : ℕ) : ℝ) * π by push_cast; ring, sin_nat_mul_pi]
  rw [h1]
  simp
  field_simp

/-- `∫₀^{2π} cos²(jθ) dθ = π` for `j ≥ 1`. -/
theorem integral_cos_sq_nat_mul {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) :
    ∫ θ in (0)..(2 * π), cos (j * θ) ^ 2 = π := by
  have hj' : (j : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast hj.ne'
  rw [intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_left (fun x => cos x ^ 2) hj', integral_cos_sq]
  have h1 : sin ((j : ℝ) * (2 * π)) = 0 := by
    rw [show (j : ℝ) * (2 * π) = ((2 * j : ℕ) : ℝ) * π by push_cast; ring, sin_nat_mul_pi]
  rw [h1]
  simp
  field_simp

/-- `(sin(j ·))′ = j cos(j ·)`. -/
theorem deriv_sin_nat_mul (j : ℕ) : deriv (fun θ => sin (j * θ)) = fun θ => j * cos (j * θ) := by
  funext θ
  have h := ((hasDerivAt_id θ).const_mul (j : ℝ)).sin
  simp only [id, mul_one] at h
  rw [h.deriv]; ring

/-- `sin(jθ)` has mean `0`. -/
theorem circMean_sin {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) : circMean (fun θ => sin (j * θ)) = 0 := by
  simp [circMean, integral_sin_nat_mul hj]

/-- `Var(sin(j ·)) = 1/2`. -/
theorem circVar_sin {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) : circVar (fun θ => sin (j * θ)) = 1 / 2 := by
  rw [circVar, circMean_sin hj]
  simp only [sub_zero]
  rw [integral_sin_sq_nat_mul hj]
  field_simp

/-- The gradient energy of `sin(j ·)` is `j²/2`. -/
theorem gradEnergy_sin {j : ℕ} (hj : 0 < j) :
    gradEnergy (fun θ => sin (j * θ)) = (j : ℝ) ^ 2 / 2 := by
  rw [gradEnergy, deriv_sin_nat_mul]
  simp only [mul_pow]
  rw [intervalIntegral.integral_const_mul, integral_cos_sq_nat_mul hj]
  field_simp

/-- `sin(j ·)` is `ContDiff ℝ ⊤`. -/
theorem contDiff_sin_nat_mul (j : ℕ) : ContDiff ℝ ⊤ (fun θ : ℝ => sin (j * θ)) :=
  contDiff_sin.comp (contDiff_const.mul contDiff_id)

/-- `sin(j ·)` is `2π`-periodic. -/
theorem periodic_sin_nat_mul (j : ℕ) : Function.Periodic (fun θ : ℝ => sin (j * θ)) (2 * π) := by
  intro θ
  simp only
  rw [show (j : ℝ) * (θ + 2 * π) = j * θ + j * (2 * π) by ring]
  exact (sin_periodic.nat_mul j) _

/-- **§10.3.** No constant `K` satisfies `∫ |f′|² ≤ K Var(f)` (normalised measure on the circle) for
every `2π`-periodic `f` of class `ContDiff ℝ ⊤`. -/
theorem no_gradient_bound_by_resampling :
    ¬ ∃ K : ℝ, ∀ f : ℝ → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ⊤ f → Function.Periodic f (2 * π) →
      gradEnergy f ≤ K * circVar f := by
  rintro ⟨K, hK⟩
  obtain ⟨j, hj⟩ := exists_nat_gt K
  have hj0 : 0 < j + 1 := Nat.succ_pos j
  have h := hK _ (contDiff_sin_nat_mul (j + 1)) (periodic_sin_nat_mul (j + 1))
  rw [gradEnergy_sin hj0, circVar_sin hj0] at h
  push_cast at h
  nlinarith


/-! ## 13. §11.1: defect absorption, and why rarity is not a defect estimate -/

/-- **§11.1.** If `Var ≤ C* (V + H)` and `V + H ≤ K ℰ + δ Var` with `C* > 0` and `K > 0`, then `((1
− C* δ)/(C* K)) Var ≤ ℰ`. -/
theorem defect_absorption {C K δ Var V H En : ℝ} (hC : 0 < C) (hK : 0 < K)
    (h1 : Var ≤ C * (V + H)) (h2 : V + H ≤ K * En + δ * Var) :
    (1 - C * δ) / (C * K) * Var ≤ En := by
  have h3 : (1 - C * δ) * Var ≤ C * K * En := by nlinarith
  rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, div_le_iff₀ (mul_pos hC hK)]
  linarith

/-- The constant `(1 − C* δ)/(C* K)` is positive when `C* δ < 1`. -/
theorem defect_absorption_pos {C K δ : ℝ} (hC : 0 < C) (hK : 0 < K) (hCδ : C * δ < 1) :
    0 < (1 - C * δ) / (C * K) :=
  div_pos (by linarith) (mul_pos hC hK)

/-- **§11.1, a rare bad set.** On a finite probability space, for `B` of probability `p` and `f =
1_B − p`: `E f = 0`, `Var f = p (1 − p)` and `∫_B f² = p (1 − p)²`. -/
theorem bad_set_ratio {Ω : Type*} [Fintype Ω] [DecidableEq Ω] (μ : Ω → ℝ) (h1 : ∑ ω, μ ω = 1)
    (B : Finset Ω) {p : ℝ} (hp : ∑ ω ∈ B, μ ω = p) :
    ∑ ω, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) = 0 ∧
      ∑ ω, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) ^ 2 = p * (1 - p) ∧
      ∑ ω ∈ B, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) ^ 2 = p * (1 - p) ^ 2 := by
  have hsplit : ∀ g : Ω → ℝ, ∑ ω, μ ω * g ω =
      ∑ ω ∈ B, μ ω * g ω + ∑ ω ∈ univ \ B, μ ω * g ω := fun g => by
    rw [← sum_union disjoint_sdiff, union_sdiff_of_subset (subset_univ B)]
  have hc : ∑ ω ∈ univ \ B, μ ω = 1 - p := by
    have := hsplit (fun _ => 1); simp only [mul_one] at this; linarith
  have hin1 : ∑ ω ∈ B, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) = (1 - p) * p := by
    rw [← hp, mul_sum]; exact sum_congr rfl fun ω hω => by rw [if_pos hω]; ring
  have hin2 : ∑ ω ∈ B, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) ^ 2 = (1 - p) ^ 2 * p := by
    rw [← hp, mul_sum]; exact sum_congr rfl fun ω hω => by rw [if_pos hω]; ring
  have hout1 : ∑ ω ∈ univ \ B, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) = (0 - p) * (1 - p) := by
    rw [← hc, mul_sum]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun ω hω => by rw [if_neg (mem_sdiff.mp hω).2]; ring
  have hout2 : ∑ ω ∈ univ \ B, μ ω * ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) ^ 2 =
      (0 - p) ^ 2 * (1 - p) := by
    rw [← hc, mul_sum]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun ω hω => by rw [if_neg (mem_sdiff.mp hω).2]; ring
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hsplit (fun ω => (if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p), hin1, hout1]; ring
  · rw [hsplit (fun ω => ((if ω ∈ B then 1 else 0) - p) ^ 2), hin2, hout2]; ring
  · rw [hin2]; ring

/-- The ratio `∫_B f² / Var f` equals `1 − p` for `0 < p < 1`. -/
theorem bad_set_ratio_eq {p : ℝ} (hp0 : 0 < p) (hp1 : p < 1) :
    p * (1 - p) ^ 2 / (p * (1 - p)) = 1 - p := by
  have : p * (1 - p) ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero hp0.ne' (by linarith)
  field_simp

/-- The ratio `1 − p` tends to `1`, not to `0`, as `p → 0⁺`. -/
theorem tendsto_bad_set_ratio : Tendsto (fun p : ℝ => 1 - p) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 1) := by
  have : Tendsto (fun p : ℝ => 1 - p) (𝓝 0) (𝓝 1) := by
    simpa using (tendsto_const_nhds (x := (1 : ℝ))).sub (tendsto_id (x := 𝓝 (0 : ℝ)))
  exact this.mono_left nhdsWithin_le_nhds


/-! ## 14. §12.1: the uniform conditional bridge and its constants -/

/-- For `V ≥ 0`, `λ ≥ λ₀ > 0`, `γ ≥ γ₀ > 0`, `0 ≤ χ ≤ χ₀`: `λ⁻¹ V + γ⁻¹ (√H + χ √V)² ≤ λ₀⁻¹ V + γ₀⁻¹
(√H + χ₀ √V)²`. -/
theorem bridge_mono {V H lam γ χ lam₀ γ₀ χ₀ : ℝ} (hV : 0 ≤ V)
    (hlam₀ : 0 < lam₀) (hlam : lam₀ ≤ lam) (hγ₀ : 0 < γ₀) (hγ : γ₀ ≤ γ) (hχ : 0 ≤ χ)
    (hχ₀ : χ ≤ χ₀) :
    lam⁻¹ * V + γ⁻¹ * (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 ≤ lam₀⁻¹ * V + γ₀⁻¹ * (√H + χ₀ * √V) ^ 2 := by
  have h1 : lam⁻¹ ≤ lam₀⁻¹ := inv_anti₀ hlam₀ hlam
  have h2 : γ⁻¹ ≤ γ₀⁻¹ := inv_anti₀ hγ₀ hγ
  have h3 : (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 ≤ (√H + χ₀ * √V) ^ 2 := by
    apply pow_le_pow_left₀ (by positivity)
    have := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hχ₀ (Real.sqrt_nonneg V)
    linarith
  have h4 : 0 ≤ (√H + χ * √V) ^ 2 := sq_nonneg _
  nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right h1 hV, mul_le_mul h2 h3 h4 (inv_pos.mpr hγ₀).le]

/-- **§12.1, the uniform conditional bridge.** For a family of domains `𝒟_p` with the inputs of
§7–§9 and §11 (total variance, fibre and coarse bounds, comparison, defect) and constants `λ_p ≥ λ₀
> 0`, `γ_p ≥ γ₀ > 0`, `0 ≤ χ_p ≤ χ₀`, `K_p ≤ K₀`, `δ_p ≤ δ₀`, with `K₀ > 0` and `C₀ δ₀ < 1` where
`C₀ = C*(λ₀⁻¹ + χ₀²/γ₀, χ₀/γ₀, γ₀⁻¹)`: `ϖ₀ = (1 − C₀ δ₀)/(C₀ K₀) > 0` and `ϖ₀ Var ≤ ℰ` on every
`𝒟_p`. -/
theorem uniform_bridge {P : Type*} {𝒟 : P → Type*}
    (Var vbar varg V H EB En : ∀ p, 𝒟 p → ℝ) (lam γ χ K δ : P → ℝ)
    {lam₀ γ₀ χ₀ K₀ δ₀ : ℝ} (hlam₀ : 0 < lam₀) (hγ₀ : 0 < γ₀) (hK₀ : 0 < K₀)
    (hlam : ∀ p, lam₀ ≤ lam p) (hγ : ∀ p, γ₀ ≤ γ p) (hχ : ∀ p, 0 ≤ χ p ∧ χ p ≤ χ₀)
    (hK : ∀ p, K p ≤ K₀) (hδ : ∀ p, δ p ≤ δ₀)
    (hVar : ∀ p f, 0 ≤ Var p f) (hV : ∀ p f, 0 ≤ V p f) (hH : ∀ p f, 0 ≤ H p f)
    (hEB : ∀ p f, 0 ≤ EB p f) (hEn : ∀ p f, 0 ≤ En p f)
    (htv : ∀ p f, Var p f = vbar p f + varg p f)
    (hfib : ∀ p f, vbar p f ≤ (lam p)⁻¹ * V p f)
    (hcoarse : ∀ p f, varg p f ≤ (γ p)⁻¹ * EB p f)
    (hcomp : ∀ p f, √(EB p f) ≤ √(H p f) + χ p * √(V p f))
    (hdefect : ∀ p f, V p f + H p f ≤ K p * En p f + δ p * Var p f)
    (hsmall : cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ * δ₀ < 1) :
    0 < (1 - cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ * δ₀) /
        (cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ * K₀) ∧
      ∀ p f, (1 - cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ * δ₀) /
        (cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ * K₀) * Var p f ≤ En p f := by
  set C₀ := cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹
  have hC₀ : 0 < C₀ := lt_of_lt_of_le (inv_pos.mpr hγ₀) (cstar_spec _ _ _).2.1
  refine ⟨defect_absorption_pos hC₀ hK₀ hsmall, fun p f => ?_⟩
  have hgp : 0 < γ p := hγ₀.trans_le (hγ p)
  have h1 : EB p f ≤ (√(H p f) + χ p * √(V p f)) ^ 2 := by
    rw [← Real.sq_sqrt (hEB p f)]; exact pow_le_pow_left₀ (Real.sqrt_nonneg _) (hcomp p f) 2
  have h2 : Var p f ≤ (lam p)⁻¹ * V p f + (γ p)⁻¹ * (√(H p f) + χ p * √(V p f)) ^ 2 := by
    rw [htv]
    have := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h1 (inv_nonneg.mpr hgp.le)
    linarith [hfib p f, hcoarse p f]
  have h3 := bridge_mono (H := H p f) (hV p f) hlam₀ (hlam p) hγ₀ (hγ p) (hχ p).1 (hχ p).2
  have h4 := quad_le_cstar (lam₀⁻¹ + χ₀ ^ 2 / γ₀) (χ₀ / γ₀) γ₀⁻¹ (√(V p f)) (√(H p f))
  rw [← expand_bridge (hV p f), Real.sq_sqrt (hV p f),
    Real.sq_sqrt (hH p f)] at h4
  have hvar : Var p f ≤ C₀ * (V p f + H p f) := by linarith
  have hdef : V p f + H p f ≤ K₀ * En p f + δ₀ * Var p f := by
    have := hdefect p f
    nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hK p) (hEn p f),
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (hδ p) (hVar p f)]
  exact defect_absorption hC₀ hK₀ hvar hdef

/-- **§12.1, extension.** An inequality `ϖ Var ≤ ℰ` between continuous functions on a dense set
holds everywhere. -/
theorem bp_extend_of_dense {𝒜 : Type*} [TopologicalSpace 𝒜] {D : Set 𝒜} (hD : Dense D)
    {Var En : 𝒜 → ℝ} (hVar : Continuous Var) (hEn : Continuous En) {ϖ : ℝ}
    (h : ∀ f ∈ D, ϖ * Var f ≤ En f) (f : 𝒜) : ϖ * Var f ≤ En f := by
  have hc : IsClosed {f | ϖ * Var f ≤ En f} := isClosed_le (continuous_const.mul hVar) hEn
  have : closure D ⊆ {f | ϖ * Var f ≤ En f} := hc.closure_subset_iff.mpr h
  exact this (hD.closure_eq ▸ Set.mem_univ f)

/-- **The primitive cost of §4.2 (and the §16 table):** `(3321/500)(10000/23851) = 66420/23851`. -/
theorem primitive_cost : (3321 / 500 : ℝ) * (10000 / 23851) = 66420 / 23851 := by norm_num


/-! ## 15. §13.1: first-chaos transfer

First the abstract statement for commuting orthogonal projections, then the coordinate model of
`H^{⊗r}` for `H = ℝⁿ`. The projections are indexed by `ℕ`; only the indices `j < r` enter, and a
family of `r` projections is extended by `Q_j = I` for `j ≥ r`. -/

/-- An orthogonal projection: a symmetric idempotent linear map. -/
def IsOrthProj {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) : Prop :=
  Q.IsSymmetric ∧ Q * Q = Q

/-- `⟨u, Q u⟩ = ‖Q u‖²`. -/
theorem IsOrthProj.inner_self {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hQ : IsOrthProj Q) (u : E) : inner ℝ u (Q u) = ‖Q u‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h : Q (Q u) = Q u := by
    have := congrArg (fun T : E →ₗ[ℝ] E => T u) hQ.2
    simpa using this
  rw [← real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, ← hQ.1 (Q u) u, h, real_inner_comm]

/-- `‖Q u‖ ≤ ‖u‖`. -/
theorem IsOrthProj.norm_le {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hQ : IsOrthProj Q) (u : E) : ‖Q u‖ ≤ ‖u‖ := by
  have h1 := hQ.inner_self u
  have h2 : inner ℝ u (Q u) ≤ ‖u‖ * ‖Q u‖ := real_inner_le_norm _ _
  rcases (norm_nonneg (Q u)).eq_or_lt with h0 | hpos
  · rw [← h0]; exact norm_nonneg _
  · nlinarith

/-- The product of commuting orthogonal projections is an orthogonal projection. -/
theorem IsOrthProj.mul {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {P Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hP : IsOrthProj P) (hQ : IsOrthProj Q) (hPQ : P * Q = Q * P) :
    IsOrthProj (P * Q) := by
  refine ⟨fun u v => ?_, ?_⟩
  · simp only [Module.End.mul_apply]
    rw [hP.1, hQ.1]
    have := congrArg (fun T : E →ₗ[ℝ] E => T v) hPQ
    simp only [Module.End.mul_apply] at this
    rw [this]
  · calc P * Q * (P * Q) = P * (Q * P) * Q := by noncomm_ring
      _ = P * (P * Q) * Q := by rw [hPQ]
      _ = (P * P) * (Q * Q) := by noncomm_ring
      _ = P * Q := by rw [hP.2, hQ.2]

/-- `⟨u, P Q u⟩ ≤ ⟨u, P u⟩` for commuting orthogonal projections. -/
theorem IsOrthProj.inner_mul_le_left {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {P Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hP : IsOrthProj P) (hQ : IsOrthProj Q) (hPQ : P * Q = Q * P) (u : E) :
    inner ℝ u ((P * Q) u) ≤ inner ℝ u (P u) := by
  rw [(hP.mul hQ hPQ).inner_self, hP.inner_self, hPQ, Module.End.mul_apply]
  exact pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) (hQ.norm_le _) 2

/-- `⟨u, P Q u⟩ ≤ ⟨u, Q u⟩` for commuting orthogonal projections. -/
theorem IsOrthProj.inner_mul_le_right {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {P Q : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hP : IsOrthProj P) (hQ : IsOrthProj Q) (hPQ : P * Q = Q * P) (u : E) :
    inner ℝ u ((P * Q) u) ≤ inner ℝ u (Q u) := by
  rw [hPQ]; exact hQ.inner_mul_le_left hP hPQ.symm u

/-- The ordered product `Q 0 * Q 1 * ⋯ * Q (k − 1)`. -/
def pprod {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Q : ℕ → E →ₗ[ℝ] E) : ℕ → (E →ₗ[ℝ] E)
  | 0 => 1
  | k + 1 => pprod Q k * Q k

/-- For pairwise commuting orthogonal projections, `∏_{j<k} Q_j` is an orthogonal projection,
commutes with every `Q_j`, and `⟨u, ∏_{j<k} Q_j u⟩ ≤ ⟨u, Q_j u⟩` for `j < k`. -/
theorem pprod_spec {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Q : ℕ → E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hQ : ∀ j, IsOrthProj (Q j)) (hcomm : ∀ i j, Q i * Q j = Q j * Q i)
    (k : ℕ) :
    IsOrthProj (pprod Q k) ∧ (∀ j, pprod Q k * Q j = Q j * pprod Q k) ∧
      ∀ j < k, ∀ u, inner ℝ u (pprod Q k u) ≤ inner ℝ u (Q j u) := by
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    refine ⟨⟨fun u v => by simp [pprod], by simp [pprod]⟩, fun j => by simp [pprod],
      fun j hj => absurd hj (Nat.not_lt_zero j)⟩
  | succ k ih =>
    obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩ := ih
    refine ⟨h1.mul (hQ k) (h2 k), fun j => ?_, fun j hj u => ?_⟩
    · simp only [pprod]
      rw [mul_assoc, hcomm k j, ← mul_assoc, h2 j, mul_assoc]
    · simp only [pprod]
      rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.mp hj with hlt | heq
      · exact (h1.inner_mul_le_left (hQ k) (h2 k) u).trans (h3 j hlt u)
      · rw [heq]; exact h1.inner_mul_le_right (hQ k) (h2 k) u

/-- **`I − ∏_j Q_j ≥ (1/r) ∑_j (I − Q_j)`** for pairwise commuting orthogonal projections, `r ≥ 1`.
-/
theorem one_sub_pprod_ge_avg {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Q : ℕ → E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hQ : ∀ j, IsOrthProj (Q j)) (hcomm : ∀ i j, Q i * Q j = Q j * Q i)
    {r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) (u : E) :
    1 / (r : ℝ) * ∑ j ∈ range r, inner ℝ u ((1 - Q j) u) ≤ inner ℝ u ((1 - pprod Q r) u) := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, h3⟩ := pprod_spec Q hQ hcomm r
  have hr' : (0 : ℝ) < r := by exact_mod_cast hr
  have : ∑ j ∈ range r, inner ℝ u ((1 - Q j) u) ≤
      ∑ j ∈ range r, inner ℝ u ((1 - pprod Q r) u) :=
    sum_le_sum fun j hj => by
      simp only [LinearMap.sub_apply, Module.End.one_apply, inner_sub_right]
      linarith [h3 j (mem_range.mp hj) u]
  rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul] at this
  rw [div_mul_eq_mul_div, one_mul, div_le_iff₀ hr']
  linarith

/-- **§13.1, abstract form.** For blocks `x` with weights `w_x ≥ 0` and pairwise commuting
orthogonal projections `Q_{x,j}`: if `∑_x w_x (I − Q_{x,j}) ≥ g` for every `j < r`, then `∑_x w_x (I
− ∏_{j<r} Q_{x,j}) ≥ g`. -/
theorem first_chaos_transfer {E X : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [Fintype X] (w : X → ℝ) (hw : ∀ x, 0 ≤ w x) (Q : X → ℕ → E →ₗ[ℝ] E)
    (hQ : ∀ x j, IsOrthProj (Q x j)) (hcomm : ∀ x i j, Q x i * Q x j = Q x j * Q x i)
    {r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) {g : ℝ}
    (hA₁ : ∀ j < r, ∀ u, g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - Q x j) u)) (u : E) :
    g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - pprod (Q x) r) u) := by
  have hr' : (0 : ℝ) < r := by exact_mod_cast hr
  calc g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 = 1 / (r : ℝ) * ∑ j ∈ range r, g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 := by
        rw [sum_const, card_range, nsmul_eq_mul]; field_simp
    _ ≤ 1 / (r : ℝ) * ∑ j ∈ range r, ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - Q x j) u) :=
        mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (sum_le_sum fun j hj => hA₁ j (mem_range.mp hj) u)
          (by positivity)
    _ = ∑ x, w x * (1 / (r : ℝ) * ∑ j ∈ range r, inner ℝ u ((1 - Q x j) u)) := by
        rw [sum_comm, mul_sum]
        refine sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
        rw [← mul_sum]; ring
    _ ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - pprod (Q x) r) u) :=
        sum_le_sum fun x _ => mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left
          (one_sub_pprod_ge_avg (Q x) (hQ x) (hcomm x) hr u) (hw x)

/-- The same inequality on any subspace (for instance the symmetric tensors). -/
theorem first_chaos_transfer_restrict {E X : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [Fintype X] (W : Submodule ℝ E) (w : X → ℝ) (hw : ∀ x, 0 ≤ w x)
    (Q : X → ℕ → E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (hQ : ∀ x j, IsOrthProj (Q x j))
    (hcomm : ∀ x i j, Q x i * Q x j = Q x j * Q x i) {r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) {g : ℝ}
    (hA₁ : ∀ j < r, ∀ u, g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - Q x j) u)) :
    ∀ u ∈ W, g * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ u ((1 - pprod (Q x) r) u) :=
  fun u _ => first_chaos_transfer w hw Q hQ hcomm hr hA₁ u


/-! ### The coordinate model `H = ℝⁿ`, `H^{⊗r} = ℝ^{(Fin r → Fin n)}` -/

/-- The coordinate model of `H^{⊗r}` for `H = ℝⁿ`. -/
abbrev Tens (n r : ℕ) := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin r → Fin n)

/-- `⟨F, G⟩ = ∑_i F i G i`. -/
theorem inner_tens {n r : ℕ} (F G : Tens n r) : inner ℝ F G = ∑ i, F i * G i := by
  rw [PiLp.inner_apply]; exact sum_congr rfl fun i _ => real_inner_apply _ _

/-- `‖F‖² = ∑_i F i²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_tens {n r : ℕ} (F : Tens n r) : ‖F‖ ^ 2 = ∑ i, F i ^ 2 :=
  EuclideanSpace.real_norm_sq_eq F

/-- `(M)_j`: the matrix `M` acting in tensor position `j`. -/
noncomputable def posOp {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) :
    Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] Tens n r →ₗ[ℝ] Tens n r :=
  LinearMap.mk₂ ℝ (fun M F => WithLp.toLp 2 fun i => ∑ a, M (i j) a * F (Function.update i j a))
    (fun M₁ M₂ F => by ext i; simp [add_mul, sum_add_distrib])
    (fun c M F => by ext i; simp [mul_sum, mul_assoc])
    (fun M F₁ F₂ => by ext i; simp [mul_add, sum_add_distrib])
    (fun c M F => by ext i; simp [mul_sum]; exact sum_congr rfl fun a _ => by ring)

/-- `((M)_j F)(i) = ∑_a M(i_j, a) F(i with i_j := a)`. -/
theorem posOp_apply {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) (M : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) (F : Tens n r)
    (i : Fin r → Fin n) : posOp j M F i = ∑ a, M (i j) a * F (Function.update i j a) := rfl

/-- `(I)_j = I`. -/
theorem posOp_one {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) : posOp (n := n) j 1 = 1 := by
  apply LinearMap.ext; intro F; ext i
  rw [posOp_apply]
  simp [Matrix.one_apply]

/-- `(M)_j (N)_j = (M N)_j`. -/
theorem posOp_mul {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) (M N : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) :
    posOp j M * posOp j N = posOp j (M * N) := by
  apply LinearMap.ext; intro F; ext i
  simp only [Module.End.mul_apply, posOp_apply, Function.update_self, Function.update_idem,
    Matrix.mul_apply, mul_sum, sum_mul]
  rw [sum_comm]
  exact sum_congr rfl fun b _ => sum_congr rfl fun a _ => by ring

/-- Operators in different positions commute. -/
theorem posOp_comm {n r : ℕ} {j k : Fin r} (hjk : j ≠ k) (M N : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) :
    posOp j M * posOp k N = posOp k N * posOp j M := by
  apply LinearMap.ext; intro F; ext i
  simp only [Module.End.mul_apply, posOp_apply, Function.update_of_ne hjk.symm,
    Function.update_of_ne hjk, mul_sum]
  rw [sum_comm]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun b _ => sum_congr rfl fun a _ => ?_
  rw [Function.update_comm hjk]
  ring

/-- The involution `(i, a) ↦ (i with i_j := a, i_j)`. -/
def swapAt {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) : (Fin r → Fin n) × Fin n ≃ (Fin r → Fin n) × Fin n :=
  Function.Involutive.toPerm (fun p => (Function.update p.1 j p.2, p.1 j)) fun p => by
    simp [Function.update_idem]

/-- `swapAt j (i, a) = (i with i_j := a, i_j)`. -/
theorem swapAt_apply {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) (p : (Fin r → Fin n) × Fin n) :
    swapAt j p = (Function.update p.1 j p.2, p.1 j) := rfl

/-- `(M)_j` is symmetric when `M` is. -/
theorem posOp_symm {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) {M : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ} (hM : Mᵀ = M) :
    (posOp j M).IsSymmetric := by
  intro F G
  rw [inner_tens, inner_tens]
  simp only [posOp_apply, sum_mul, mul_sum]
  rw [← Fintype.sum_prod_type', ← Fintype.sum_prod_type']
  rw [← (swapAt j).sum_comp]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun p _ => ?_
  simp only [swapAt_apply, Function.update_self, Function.update_idem,
    Function.update_eq_self]
  have : M (p.1 j) p.2 = M p.2 (p.1 j) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← hM]
    rfl
  rw [this]
  ring

/-- `(P)_j` is an orthogonal projection when `P` is a symmetric idempotent matrix. -/
theorem posOp_isOrthProj {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) {P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ} (hPs : Pᵀ = P)
    (hPi : P * P = P) :
    (posOp j P).IsSymmetric ∧ posOp j P * posOp j P = posOp j P :=
  ⟨posOp_symm j hPs, by rw [posOp_mul, hPi]⟩

/-- Changing coordinate `j` in the split form. -/
theorem piSplitAt_symm_update {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) (c a : Fin n)
    (ρ : (k : {k // k ≠ j}) → Fin n) :
    Function.update ((Equiv.piSplitAt j (fun _ => Fin n)).symm (c, ρ)) j a =
      (Equiv.piSplitAt j (fun _ => Fin n)).symm (a, ρ) := by
  funext k
  by_cases hk : k = j
  · subst hk; simp [Equiv.piSplitAt_symm_apply]
  · rw [Function.update_of_ne hk]; simp [Equiv.piSplitAt_symm_apply, hk]

/-- **`A ≥ g` on `ℝⁿ` implies `(A)_j ≥ g` on `H^{⊗r}`.** -/
theorem posOp_lower {n r : ℕ} (j : Fin r) {A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ} {g : ℝ}
    (hA : ∀ v : Fin n → ℝ, g * ∑ c, v c ^ 2 ≤ ∑ c, v c * ∑ a, A c a * v a) (F : Tens n r) :
    g * ‖F‖ ^ 2 ≤ inner ℝ F (posOp j A F) := by
  rw [inner_tens, norm_sq_tens]
  simp only [posOp_apply]
  set σ := (Equiv.piSplitAt j (fun _ => Fin n)).symm
  rw [← σ.sum_comp, ← σ.sum_comp, Fintype.sum_prod_type_right, Fintype.sum_prod_type_right,
    mul_sum]
  refine sum_le_sum fun ρ _ => ?_
  have hσj : ∀ c, σ (c, ρ) j = c := fun c => by simp [σ, Equiv.piSplitAt_symm_apply]
  have hσu : ∀ c a, Function.update (σ (c, ρ)) j a = σ (a, ρ) := fun c a =>
    piSplitAt_symm_update j c a ρ
  simp only [hσj, hσu]
  exact hA (fun c => F (σ (c, ρ)))


/-- `Q_j = (P)_j` for `j < r`, and `I` for `j ≥ r`. -/
noncomputable def posSeq {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) (j : ℕ) :
    Tens n r →ₗ[ℝ] Tens n r :=
  if h : j < r then posOp ⟨j, h⟩ P else 1

/-- `P^{⊗r} = (P)_0 (P)_1 ⋯ (P)_{r−1}`; its kernel is the Kronecker power (`tpow_apply`). -/
noncomputable def tpow {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) : Tens n r →ₗ[ℝ] Tens n r :=
  pprod (posSeq P) r

/-- Each `Q_j` is an orthogonal projection. -/
theorem posSeq_isOrthProj {n r : ℕ} {P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ} (hPs : Pᵀ = P)
    (hPi : P * P = P) (j : ℕ) : IsOrthProj (posSeq (r := r) P j) := by
  unfold posSeq
  split_ifs with h
  · exact posOp_isOrthProj _ hPs hPi
  · exact ⟨fun u v => by simp, by simp⟩

/-- The `Q_j` commute pairwise. -/
theorem posSeq_comm {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) (i j : ℕ) :
    posSeq (r := r) P i * posSeq P j = posSeq P j * posSeq P i := by
  unfold posSeq
  split_ifs with hi hj hj
  · by_cases hij : i = j
    · subst hij; rfl
    · exact posOp_comm (fun h => hij (congrArg Fin.val h)) _ _
  all_goals simp

/-- **§13.1 on `H = ℝⁿ`.** For symmetric idempotent matrices `P_x`, weights `w_x ≥ 0` and `A₁ = ∑_x
w_x (I − P_x) ≥ g` on `ℝⁿ`: `A_r = ∑_x w_x (I − P_x^{⊗r}) ≥ g` on `H^{⊗r}`, `r ≥ 1`. -/
theorem first_chaos_transfer_tensor {n r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) {X : Type*} [Fintype X]
    (w : X → ℝ) (hw : ∀ x, 0 ≤ w x) (P : X → Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)
    (hPs : ∀ x, (P x)ᵀ = P x) (hPi : ∀ x, P x * P x = P x) {g : ℝ}
    (hA₁ : ∀ v : Fin n → ℝ, g * ∑ c, v c ^ 2 ≤ ∑ c, v c * ∑ a, (∑ x, w x • (1 - P x)) c a * v a)
    (F : Tens n r) :
    g * ‖F‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ F ((1 - tpow (P x)) F) := by
  refine first_chaos_transfer w hw (fun x => posSeq (P x))
    (fun x j => posSeq_isOrthProj (hPs x) (hPi x) j) (fun x i j => posSeq_comm (P x) i j) hr
    (fun j hj u => ?_) F
  have h := posOp_lower ⟨j, hj⟩ hA₁ u
  simp only [map_sum, map_smul, map_sub, posOp_one] at h
  simp only [LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply,
    Module.End.one_apply, inner_sum, real_inner_smul_right] at h
  simpa [posSeq, hj] using h

/-- The symmetric tensors: `F (i ∘ σ) = F i` for every permutation `σ` of the positions. -/
def symTensors (n r : ℕ) : Submodule ℝ (Tens n r) where
  carrier := {F | ∀ (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin r)) (i : Fin r → Fin n), F (i ∘ σ) = F i}
  add_mem' := by
    intro F G hF hG σ i
    have h1 : F (i ∘ σ) = F i := hF σ i
    have h2 : G (i ∘ σ) = G i := hG σ i
    simp [h1, h2]
  zero_mem' := by intro σ i; simp
  smul_mem' := by
    intro c F hF σ i
    have h1 : F (i ∘ σ) = F i := hF σ i
    simp [h1]

/-- **§13.1, symmetric tensors:** the same inequality restricted to `symTensors n r`. -/
theorem first_chaos_transfer_tensor_sym {n r : ℕ} (hr : 0 < r) {X : Type*} [Fintype X]
    (w : X → ℝ) (hw : ∀ x, 0 ≤ w x) (P : X → Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ)
    (hPs : ∀ x, (P x)ᵀ = P x) (hPi : ∀ x, P x * P x = P x) {g : ℝ}
    (hA₁ : ∀ v : Fin n → ℝ, g * ∑ c, v c ^ 2 ≤ ∑ c, v c * ∑ a, (∑ x, w x • (1 - P x)) c a * v a) :
    ∀ F ∈ symTensors n r, g * ‖F‖ ^ 2 ≤ ∑ x, w x * inner ℝ F ((1 - tpow (P x)) F) :=
  fun F _ => first_chaos_transfer_tensor hr w hw P hPs hPi hA₁ F

/-- The kernel of `(P)_0 ⋯ (P)_{m−1}`: `P(i_j, k_j)` in the positions `j < m`, `δ(i_j, k_j)`
elsewhere. -/
noncomputable def partK {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) (m : ℕ)
    (i k : Fin r → Fin n) : ℝ :=
  ∏ j : Fin r, if (j : ℕ) < m then P (i j) (k j) else if i j = k j then 1 else 0

/-- One more position: `∑_c K_m(i, l with l_m := c) P(c, l_m) = K_{m+1}(i, l)`. -/
theorem partK_succ {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) {m : ℕ} (hm : m < r)
    (i l : Fin r → Fin n) :
    ∑ c, partK P m i (Function.update l ⟨m, hm⟩ c) * P c (l ⟨m, hm⟩) = partK P (m + 1) i l := by
  set m' : Fin r := ⟨m, hm⟩
  have hsplit : ∀ c, partK P m i (Function.update l m' c) =
      (if i m' = c then 1 else 0) *
        ∏ j ∈ {m'}ᶜ, (if (j : ℕ) < m + 1 then P (i j) (l j) else if i j = l j then 1 else 0) := by
    intro c
    rw [partK, Fintype.prod_eq_mul_prod_compl m']
    congr 1
    · simp [m']
    · refine prod_congr rfl fun j hj => ?_
      have hjm : j ≠ m' := by simpa using hj
      have hjm' : (j : ℕ) ≠ m := fun h => hjm (Fin.ext h)
      rw [Function.update_of_ne hjm]
      have : ((j : ℕ) < m) ↔ ((j : ℕ) < m + 1) := by omega
      simp only [this]
  simp only [hsplit]
  rw [partK, Fintype.prod_eq_mul_prod_compl m']
  simp only [ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul, sum_ite_eq, mem_univ, if_true]
  simp [m']
  ring

/-- `((P)_0 ⋯ (P)_{m−1} F)(i) = ∑_k K_m(i, k) F(k)` for `m ≤ r`. -/
theorem pprod_posSeq_apply {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) :
    ∀ m ≤ r, ∀ (F : Tens n r) (i : Fin r → Fin n),
      pprod (posSeq P) m F i = ∑ k, partK P m i k * F k := by
  intro m
  induction m with
  | zero =>
    intro _ F i
    have : ∀ k : Fin r → Fin n, partK P 0 i k = if i = k then 1 else 0 := by
      intro k
      rw [partK]
      simp only [Nat.not_lt_zero, if_false]
      rw [prod_boole]
      simp [funext_iff]
    simp only [this, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul, sum_ite_eq, mem_univ, if_true]
    simp [pprod]
  | succ m ih =>
    intro hm F i
    have hmr : m < r := hm
    rw [pprod, Module.End.mul_apply, ih (le_of_lt hmr)]
    simp only [posSeq, hmr, dif_pos, posOp_apply, mul_sum]
    rw [← Fintype.sum_prod_type', ← (swapAt ⟨m, hmr⟩).sum_comp]
    simp only [swapAt_apply, Function.update_self, Function.update_idem, Function.update_eq_self]
    rw [Fintype.sum_prod_type]
    refine sum_congr rfl fun l _ => ?_
    rw [← partK_succ P hmr i l, sum_mul]
    exact sum_congr rfl fun c _ => by ring

/-- **`P^{⊗r}` is the Kronecker power:** `(P^{⊗r} F)(i) = ∑_k (∏_j P(i_j, k_j)) F(k)`. -/
theorem tpow_apply {n r : ℕ} (P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) (F : Tens n r)
    (i : Fin r → Fin n) : tpow P F i = ∑ k, (∏ j, P (i j) (k j)) * F k := by
  rw [tpow, pprod_posSeq_apply P r le_rfl]
  refine sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
  congr 1
  exact prod_congr rfl fun j _ => by simp [j.2]


/-! ## 16. §14.1: propagation across fixed physical scales -/

/-- **§14.1.** If `ℰ_{j+1} ≥ c_{j+1} ℰ_j` with `c_j ≥ 0` and `ℰ_0 ≥ ϖ_base Var`, then `ℰ_J ≥ ϖ_base
(∏_{j=1}^{J} c_j) Var`. -/
theorem scale_propagation (En : ℕ → ℝ) (c : ℕ → ℝ) {Var ϖ : ℝ} (hc : ∀ j, 0 ≤ c j)
    (hstep : ∀ j, c (j + 1) * En j ≤ En (j + 1)) (hbase : ϖ * Var ≤ En 0) (J : ℕ) :
    ϖ * (∏ j ∈ range J, c (j + 1)) * Var ≤ En J := by
  induction J with
  | zero => simpa using hbase
  | succ J ih =>
    rw [prod_range_succ]
    calc ϖ * ((∏ j ∈ range J, c (j + 1)) * c (J + 1)) * Var
        = c (J + 1) * (ϖ * (∏ j ∈ range J, c (j + 1)) * Var) := by ring
      _ ≤ c (J + 1) * En J := mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ih (hc _)
      _ ≤ En (J + 1) := hstep J

/-- For `0 ≤ c < 1`, `c^J → 0`: a tower whose length grows does not give a uniform constant. -/
theorem tower_degenerates {c : ℝ} (hc0 : 0 ≤ c) (hc1 : c < 1) :
    Tendsto (fun J : ℕ => c ^ J) atTop (𝓝 0) :=
  tendsto_pow_atTop_nhds_zero_of_lt_one hc0 hc1


