/-! # Part V. `SchurSplit` (the text of `SchurSplitCriterion.lean` after its import line) -/

/-!
# The simultaneous fibre/coarse split: an exact Schur-complement criterion

A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalisation of the abstract operator statements in the note *The concrete
advance*: the exact criterion for the simultaneous inequality `D_f ≥ α (I − Π) + β J D_c J*`, its
approximate-inverse certificate, the mixed block of cube resampling, and the resulting gap. The
file imports Mathlib only and its namespace is `SchurSplit`. Except in Section 2 (a Hilbert space
and a bounded `A`), everything is proved for real inner product spaces and linear maps (Section 5
for modules); nothing here is specific to the Wilson measure.

## Setting

`H` is a real inner product space (in the note, the centred gauge-invariant space) and `Π` an
orthogonal projection on it (`OrthProj`: a symmetric linear map with `Π² = Π`). Then
`H_f = ker Π` (`OrthProj.Hf`) and `H_c = ran Π` (`OrthProj.Hc`); the note's
`H_c = ran Π ∩ L²₀(μ)` is `ran Π` because `H` is already centred. The generator `D` (the note's
`D_f`) is a symmetric linear map on `H`. The coarse observables form a second space `Y` with a
linear map `D_c`, and `J : Y → H` has the adjoint `J*` (`Jt`, with `⟪J y, x⟫ = ⟪y, J* x⟫`). The
blocks of `D` on `H_f ⊕ H_c` are `A = (I − Π) D` on `H_f` (`blkA`), `B = (I − Π) D` from `H_c` to
`H_f` (`blkB`) and `C = Π D` on `H_c` (`blkC`); the coarse form is
`⟪v, G v⟫ = ⟪J* v, D_c J* v⟫` (`gC`). The target is Mathlib's Loewner inequality `splitOp ≤ D`
(`LinearMap.le_def`: `D − splitOp` is positive), where `splitOp = α (I − Π) + β J D_c J*`.

Inverses and adjoints are not primitives. `B* K⁻¹ B`, `Q` and `R* R` enter as quadratic forms:
`⟪v, B* K⁻¹ B v⟫ = ⟪B v, K⁻¹ B v⟫`, `⟪v, Q v⟫ = 2 ⟪B v, X v⟫ − ⟪X v, K X v⟫` (`qForm`) and
`⟪v, R* R v⟫ = ‖R v‖²`, with `K = A − α I` (`shiftOp`) and `R = B − K X` (`resid`). Sections 1–3
are stated for any two spaces `E`, `F`, maps `A`, `B`, `C` and a function `g` for the coarse
form; Section 4 applies them to `H_f` and `H_c`.

## Main results

* `split_identity`: the exact identity
  `⟪u, K u⟫ + 2 ⟪u, B v⟫ + ⟪v, (C − β G) v⟫ = ⟪w, K w⟫ + ⟪v, (C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B) v⟫` with
  `w = u + K⁻¹ B v`, for symmetric `A` and `K K⁻¹ = I`. The note writes `⟪w, K w⟫` as
  `‖K^{1/2} w‖²`; the square root is not needed and is not formalised.
* `split_iff_schur`: if `A` is symmetric, `A ≥ λ I`, `α ≤ λ` and `K K⁻¹ = I`, the target holds
  iff `C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B ≥ 0`; necessity takes `u = −K⁻¹ B v`. On a Hilbert space with bounded
  `A` and `α < λ`, `exists_shiftOp_inverse` constructs a bounded two-sided `K⁻¹` (Lax–Milgram),
  and `split_iff_schur_complete` states the criterion without an inverse hypothesis.
* `response_expansion`: `B* K⁻¹ B = Q + R* K⁻¹ R` for symmetric `A`, every trial `X` and a
  two-sided `K⁻¹`; if moreover `A ≥ λ I` and `α < λ`, `qForm_le_response`: `Q ≤ B* K⁻¹ B` and
  `response_le_cert`: `B* K⁻¹ B ≤ Q + (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R`.
* `split_of_certificate`: if `C − β G − Q − (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R ≥ 0` for some trial `X`, the target
  holds. No inverse of `K` is used. `residual_essential`: the residual term cannot be dropped.
* On `H`: `splitOp_le_iff` (the Loewner inequality as forms), `le_iff_split` (the target as a
  block target on `H_f ⊕ H_c`, given `ran J ⊆ H_c`), `le_iff_schur` and `le_of_certificate`.
  `le_iff_schur` takes the inverse of `A − α I` on `H_f` as a hypothesis; Section 2 is not
  applied on `H_f`.
* `gap_of_le`: if the target holds, `D_c ≥ ϖ I`, `J J* = Π` and `β ≥ 0`, then
  `D ≥ min(α, β ϖ) I`, that is `ϖ_f ≥ min(α, β ϖ_c)`; `gap_of_certificate` combines it with
  `le_of_certificate`.
* `resampling_offdiag`: if `Π² = Π` and `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`, then
  `(I − Π) D Π = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. `resampling_offdiag_uniform` is the case `wₓ = c` (the
  note's `n⁻⁴`); `blkB_coe_eq` identifies `B` with `(I − Π) D Π` on `H_c`; and if every `Pₓ`
  maps `ran Π` into itself, the mixed block vanishes (`resampling_offdiag_eq_zero`).

## Differences from the note

* The note assumes `0 < α < λ` and `β > 0`. The criterion needs only `α ≤ λ` together with the
  inverse, or `α < λ` on a Hilbert space with bounded `A` (Section 2); the certificate needs
  `α < λ`; the gap needs `β ≥ 0`. Positivity of `α` is not used.
* The note gives no formula for `D_f` in terms of the cube expectations; the formula for `B` is
  proved for `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`, which with `wₓ = n⁻⁴` gives the note's
  `B = −n⁻⁴ ∑ₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. `Pₓ` need not be projections.
* `split_iff_schur` assumes only `K K⁻¹ = I`; `response_expansion` uses `K K⁻¹ = K⁻¹ K = I`.
  Boundedness and completeness are used only in Section 2.
* The block form of the target and the results built on it assume `ran J ⊆ ran Π` (`hJ`), and
  the gap assumes `J J* = Π` (`hJJ`, so `‖J* x‖ = ‖Π x‖`); the note leaves both implicit (there
  `J` embeds the coarse observables onto `H_c`).

## Not formalised

The identification of `D_f`, `Π`, `Pₓ`, `J` and `D_c` with the Wilson cube-resampling generator,
the coarse-measurable projection, the cube conditional expectations and the coarse law; the
construction of a trial `X` and the bound on its residual for the interacting conditional laws;
the positive remainder uniformly in the spacings and volumes; the coarse gap `D_c ≥ ϖ_c`; and the
relation of exact finite matrix certificates to these `L²` operators. These are the tasks the note
leaves open; the coarse gap is a hypothesis there. The note's last paragraph comments on a review;
its one mathematical demand, a theorem identifying the Wilson operators and certifying the
remainder with uniform constants, is among the items above. Nothing here is about the Yang–Mills
measure, and the mass gap remains open.

## Closed applications (non-vacuity)

On `ℝ`: `cert_example` (an inexact trial `X`, so `R ≠ 0`), `response_example`, `complete_example`
(Lax–Milgram) and `residual_essential`. On `ℝ²`, a two-cube model (`pT`, `PcT`, `DT`, `JT`,
`JtT`): `Π = diag(1, 0)`, `D = ∑ₓ (1/2)(I − Pₓ)` with `Pₓ` the orthogonal projections onto
`(1, 1)` and `(1, 0)` (the second is `Π` itself), and `D_c = I`. In the model the mixed block is
nonzero (`toy_offdiag`; in the uniform form `toy_offdiag_uniform`) and comes from the diagonal
cube alone, since the axis cube preserves `ran Π` (`toy_offdiag_axis`); `B (1, 0) = (0, −1/4)`
(`toy_blkB`). The split holds at `(α, β) = (1/4, 1/8)` (`toy_le`, `toy_split`) and
gives the lower bound `D ≥ (1/8) I` (`toy_gap`; the least eigenvalue of `D` is `1/2 − √2/4`);
the certificate with the inexact `XT` proves it at `(1/4, 1/16)` (`toy_cert`, `toy_cert_le`,
`toy_gap_cert`); and by `le_iff_schur` it fails at `(1/4, 1/4)` (`toy_not_le`). In these models
`A = λ` on a one-dimensional fibre, so the residual bound is exact there (the certificate with
`XT` also reaches `β = 1/8`); in `response_strict_example`, with `A = diag(1, 2)` on `ℝ²`, it is
strict. Numerical agreement is never used as proof.
-/

namespace SchurSplit

open scoped InnerProductSpace

/-! ## 1. The block criterion -/

section Block

variable {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F]

/-- The quadratic form `⟪u, A u⟫ + 2 ⟪u, B v⟫ + ⟪v, C v⟫` of the block operator
`[[A, B], [B*, C]]` on `E ⊕ F` at `(u, v)`. -/
def blockForm (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F) (u : E) (v : F) : ℝ :=
  ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ + 2 * ⟪u, B v⟫_ℝ + ⟪v, C v⟫_ℝ

/-- The target `[[A, B], [B*, C]] ≥ [[α I, 0], [0, β G]]` as quadratic forms; `g v` is the
value `⟪v, G v⟫` of the coarse form. -/
def SplitTarget (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F) (g : F → ℝ) (α β : ℝ) : Prop :=
  ∀ u v, α * ‖u‖ ^ 2 + β * g v ≤ blockForm A B C u v

/-- `K = A − α I`. -/
def shiftOp (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) : E →ₗ[ℝ] E := A - α • LinearMap.id

theorem shiftOp_apply (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) (u : E) : shiftOp A α u = A u - α • u := by
  simp [shiftOp]

theorem inner_shiftOp (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) (u : E) :
    ⟪u, shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ = ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ - α * ‖u‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [shiftOp_apply, inner_sub_right, real_inner_smul_right, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq]

theorem shiftOp_isSymmetric {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) (α : ℝ) :
    (shiftOp A α).IsSymmetric := fun x y => by
  rw [shiftOp_apply, shiftOp_apply, inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right, real_inner_smul_left,
    real_inner_smul_right, hA x y]

/-- If `A ≥ λ I` then `A − α I ≥ (λ − α) I`. -/
theorem shiftOp_coercive {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} {lam : ℝ} (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ)
    (α : ℝ) (u : E) : (lam - α) * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [inner_shiftOp, sub_mul]; linarith [hlam u]

/-- The Schur-complement form `⟪v, (C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B) v⟫` for a given inverse `Kinv` of
`K = A − α I`, written without adjoints: `⟪v, C v⟫ − β g v − ⟪B v, K⁻¹ B v⟫`. -/
def schurForm (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F) (g : F → ℝ) (β : ℝ) (Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E)
    (v : F) : ℝ :=
  ⟪v, C v⟫_ℝ - β * g v - ⟪B v, Kinv (B v)⟫_ℝ

/-- **The exact identity.** For symmetric `A`, with `K = A − α I` and `K K⁻¹ = I`,
`⟪u, K u⟫ + 2 ⟪u, B v⟫ + ⟪v, (C − β G) v⟫ = ⟪w, K w⟫ + ⟪v, (C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B) v⟫`
with `w = u + K⁻¹ B v`. The left side is written as `blockForm − (α ‖u‖² + β g v)`. -/
theorem split_identity {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F)
    (g : F → ℝ) (α β : ℝ) {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp A α (Kinv x) = x) (u : E)
    (v : F) :
    blockForm A B C u v - (α * ‖u‖ ^ 2 + β * g v) =
      ⟪u + Kinv (B v), shiftOp A α (u + Kinv (B v))⟫_ℝ + schurForm B C g β Kinv v := by
  have hs := shiftOp_isSymmetric hA α
  have e1 : ⟪u + Kinv (B v), shiftOp A α (u + Kinv (B v))⟫_ℝ =
      ⟪u, shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ + ⟪u, B v⟫_ℝ + ⟪Kinv (B v), shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ +
        ⟪Kinv (B v), B v⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [map_add, hK, inner_add_left, inner_add_right, inner_add_right]; ring
  have e2 : ⟪Kinv (B v), shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ = ⟪u, B v⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [← hs (Kinv (B v)) u, hK]; exact real_inner_comm u (B v)
  have e3 : ⟪Kinv (B v), B v⟫_ℝ = ⟪B v, Kinv (B v)⟫_ℝ := real_inner_comm _ _
  rw [e1, e2, e3, inner_shiftOp]
  simp only [blockForm, schurForm]
  ring

/-- **The criterion.** If `A` is symmetric, `A ≥ λ I`, `α ≤ λ` and `Kinv` is a right inverse of
`K = A − α I`, then the target holds if and only if `C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B ≥ 0`. Necessity takes
`u = −K⁻¹ B v`. -/
theorem split_iff_schur {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α ≤ lam) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F)
    (g : F → ℝ) (β : ℝ) {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp A α (Kinv x) = x) :
    SplitTarget A B C g α β ↔ ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm B C g β Kinv v := by
  constructor
  · intro h v
    have hid := split_identity hA B C g α β hK (-Kinv (B v)) v
    rw [neg_add_cancel, map_zero, inner_zero_left, zero_add] at hid
    linarith [h (-Kinv (B v)) v]
  · intro h u v
    have hid := split_identity hA B C g α β hK u v
    have hw := shiftOp_coercive hlam α (u + Kinv (B v))
    have h0 : 0 ≤ (lam - α) * ‖u + Kinv (B v)‖ ^ 2 := mul_nonneg (by linarith) (sq_nonneg _)
    linarith [h v]

end Block

/-! ## 2. The inverse on a Hilbert space (Lax–Milgram) -/

section Complete

variable {V F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [InnerProductSpace ℝ V] [CompleteSpace V]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F]

/-- On a Hilbert space, if `A` is bounded with `A ≥ λ I` and `α < λ`, then `K = A − α I` has a
bounded two-sided inverse (Lax–Milgram, `IsCoercive.continuousLinearEquivOfBilin`). -/
theorem exists_shiftOp_inverse (A : V →L[ℝ] V) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) :
    ∃ Kinv : V →L[ℝ] V, (∀ x, shiftOp (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) α (Kinv x) = x) ∧
      ∀ x, Kinv (shiftOp (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) α x) = x := by
  let K : V →L[ℝ] V := A - α • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ V
  have hK : ∀ x, K x = shiftOp (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) α x := fun x => by simp [K, shiftOp_apply]
  let Bf : V →L[ℝ] V →L[ℝ] ℝ := (innerSL ℝ : V →L[ℝ] V →L[ℝ] ℝ).comp K
  have hBf : ∀ v w, Bf v w = ⟪K v, w⟫_ℝ := fun v w => by simp [Bf]
  have hco : IsCoercive Bf := by
    refine ⟨lam - α, by linarith, fun u => ?_⟩
    rw [hBf, hK, real_inner_comm]
    have h := shiftOp_coercive (A := (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V)) hlam α u
    nlinarith [h]
  have hT : ∀ v, hco.continuousLinearEquivOfBilin v = K v := fun v =>
    ext_inner_right ℝ fun w => by rw [IsCoercive.continuousLinearEquivOfBilin_apply, hBf]
  refine ⟨(hco.continuousLinearEquivOfBilin.symm : V →L[ℝ] V), fun x => ?_, fun x => ?_⟩
  · rw [← hK, ← hT]; simp
  · rw [← hK, ← hT]; simp

/-- **The criterion on a Hilbert space**, with the inverse constructed: for bounded symmetric
`A ≥ λ I` and `α < λ`, `K = A − α I` has a bounded two-sided inverse `K⁻¹`, and the target holds
if and only if `C − β G − B* K⁻¹ B ≥ 0`. -/
theorem split_iff_schur_complete (A : V →L[ℝ] V) (hA : (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V).IsSymmetric)
    {lam α : ℝ} (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] V)
    (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F) (g : F → ℝ) (β : ℝ) :
    ∃ Kinv : V →L[ℝ] V, (∀ x, shiftOp (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) α (Kinv x) = x) ∧
      (∀ x, Kinv (shiftOp (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) α x) = x) ∧
      (SplitTarget (A : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) B C g α β ↔
        ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm B C g β (Kinv : V →ₗ[ℝ] V) v) := by
  obtain ⟨Kinv, h1, h2⟩ := exists_shiftOp_inverse A hlam hα
  exact ⟨Kinv, h1, h2, split_iff_schur hA hlam hα.le B C g β (Kinv := (Kinv : V →ₗ[ℝ] V)) h1⟩

end Complete

/-! ## 3. The approximate-inverse certificate -/

section Certificate

variable {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [InnerProductSpace ℝ F]

/-- The residual `R = B − (A − α I) X` of a trial operator `X : F → E`. -/
def resid (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) : F →ₗ[ℝ] E :=
  B - shiftOp A α ∘ₗ X

theorem resid_apply (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : F) :
    resid A B α X v = B v - shiftOp A α (X v) := by
  simp [resid]

/-- `⟪v, Q v⟫` for `Q = B* X + X* B − X* (A − α I) X`, written without adjoints:
`2 ⟪B v, X v⟫ − ⟪X v, (A − α I) X v⟫`. -/
def qForm (A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : F) : ℝ :=
  2 * ⟪B v, X v⟫_ℝ - ⟪X v, shiftOp A α (X v)⟫_ℝ

/-- If `K ≥ μ I` with `μ > 0` and `K K⁻¹ = I`, then `0 ≤ ⟪r, K⁻¹ r⟫ ≤ ‖r‖² / μ`. -/
theorem inner_inv_bounds {K : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hK : ∀ x, μ * ‖x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪x, K x⟫_ℝ) {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hinv : ∀ x, K (Kinv x) = x)
    (r : E) : 0 ≤ ⟪r, Kinv r⟫_ℝ ∧ ⟪r, Kinv r⟫_ℝ ≤ ‖r‖ ^ 2 / μ := by
  have h1 : ⟪r, Kinv r⟫_ℝ = ⟪Kinv r, K (Kinv r)⟫_ℝ := by rw [hinv, real_inner_comm]
  have h2 : μ * ‖Kinv r‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪r, Kinv r⟫_ℝ := by rw [h1]; exact hK (Kinv r)
  have h3 := real_inner_le_norm r (Kinv r)
  have h4 : 0 ≤ μ * ‖Kinv r‖ ^ 2 := mul_nonneg hμ.le (sq_nonneg _)
  refine ⟨by linarith, ?_⟩
  rw [le_div_iff₀ hμ]
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg (‖r‖ - μ * ‖Kinv r‖), mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h3 hμ.le,
    mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 hμ.le]

/-- **The expansion** `B* K⁻¹ B = Q + R* K⁻¹ R`, as forms, for any trial operator `X`, given
symmetric `A` and a two-sided inverse `K⁻¹` of `K = A − α I`. -/
theorem response_expansion {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (α : ℝ)
    {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp A α (Kinv x) = x)
    (hK' : ∀ x, Kinv (shiftOp A α x) = x) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : F) :
    ⟪B v, Kinv (B v)⟫_ℝ =
      qForm A B α X v + ⟪resid A B α X v, Kinv (resid A B α X v)⟫_ℝ := by
  have hs := shiftOp_isSymmetric hA α
  have hB : B v = resid A B α X v + shiftOp A α (X v) := by rw [resid_apply]; abel
  simp only [qForm]
  rw [hB]
  generalize resid A B α X v = r
  generalize X v = x
  have e1 : ⟪shiftOp A α x, Kinv r⟫_ℝ = ⟪r, x⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [hs x (Kinv r), hK]; exact real_inner_comm r x
  have e2 : ⟪shiftOp A α x, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪x, shiftOp A α x⟫_ℝ := real_inner_comm _ _
  have e3 : ⟪x, r⟫_ℝ = ⟪r, x⟫_ℝ := real_inner_comm _ _
  simp only [map_add, hK', inner_add_left, inner_add_right]
  linarith [e1, e2, e3]

/-- For symmetric `A ≥ λ I`, `α < λ` and a two-sided inverse `K⁻¹`, `Q` alone is a lower bound
on the response: `⟪v, Q v⟫ ≤ ⟪v, B* K⁻¹ B v⟫`. -/
theorem qForm_le_response {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E)
    {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp A α (Kinv x) = x)
    (hK' : ∀ x, Kinv (shiftOp A α x) = x) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : F) :
    qForm A B α X v ≤ ⟪B v, Kinv (B v)⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [response_expansion hA B α hK hK' X v]
  linarith [(inner_inv_bounds (sub_pos.2 hα) (shiftOp_coercive hlam α) hK
    (resid A B α X v)).1]

/-- **The residual bound** `B* K⁻¹ B ≤ Q + (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R`, as forms, for symmetric `A ≥ λ I`,
`α < λ` and a two-sided inverse `K⁻¹`. -/
theorem response_le_cert {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E)
    {Kinv : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp A α (Kinv x) = x)
    (hK' : ∀ x, Kinv (shiftOp A α x) = x) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (v : F) :
    ⟪B v, Kinv (B v)⟫_ℝ ≤ qForm A B α X v + ‖resid A B α X v‖ ^ 2 / (lam - α) := by
  rw [response_expansion hA B α hK hK' X v]
  linarith [(inner_inv_bounds (sub_pos.2 hα) (shiftOp_coercive hlam α) hK
    (resid A B α X v)).2]

/-- If `K ≥ μ I` with `μ > 0`, then `⟪w, K w⟫ + 2 ⟪w, r⟫ + ‖r‖² / μ ≥ 0`. -/
theorem form_add_two_inner_nonneg {K : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hK : ∀ x, μ * ‖x‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪x, K x⟫_ℝ) (w r : E) :
    0 ≤ ⟪w, K w⟫_ℝ + 2 * ⟪w, r⟫_ℝ + ‖r‖ ^ 2 / μ := by
  have h1 := hK w
  have h2 : -(‖w‖ * ‖r‖) ≤ ⟪w, r⟫_ℝ := by
    have := abs_real_inner_le_norm w r
    linarith [neg_abs_le ⟪w, r⟫_ℝ]
  have h3 : μ * (‖r‖ ^ 2 / μ) = ‖r‖ ^ 2 := by field_simp
  have h4 : μ * 0 ≤ μ * (⟪w, K w⟫_ℝ + 2 * ⟪w, r⟫_ℝ + ‖r‖ ^ 2 / μ) := by
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (μ * ‖w‖ - ‖r‖), mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h1 hμ.le,
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 hμ.le]
  exact le_of_mul_le_mul_left h4 hμ

/-- **The certificate.** If `A` is symmetric, `A ≥ λ I`, `α < λ`, and a trial operator `X`
satisfies `C − β G − Q − (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R ≥ 0` as forms, then the target holds. No inverse of
`A − α I` is used. -/
theorem split_of_certificate {A : E →ₗ[ℝ] E} (hA : A.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, A u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (B : F →ₗ[ℝ] E) (C : F →ₗ[ℝ] F)
    (g : F → ℝ) (β : ℝ) (X : F →ₗ[ℝ] E)
    (hcert : ∀ v, β * g v + qForm A B α X v + ‖resid A B α X v‖ ^ 2 / (lam - α) ≤
      ⟪v, C v⟫_ℝ) :
    SplitTarget A B C g α β := by
  intro u v
  have hs := shiftOp_isSymmetric hA α
  have hlow := form_add_two_inner_nonneg (sub_pos.2 hα) (shiftOp_coercive hlam α) (u + X v)
    (resid A B α X v)
  have hB : B v = resid A B α X v + shiftOp A α (X v) := by rw [resid_apply]; abel
  have hc := hcert v
  have e0 := inner_shiftOp A α u
  simp only [qForm] at hc
  simp only [blockForm]
  rw [hB] at hc ⊢
  generalize resid A B α X v = r at hc hlow ⊢
  generalize X v = x at hc hlow ⊢
  have e1 : ⟪x, shiftOp A α u⟫_ℝ = ⟪u, shiftOp A α x⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [← hs x u]; exact real_inner_comm u (shiftOp A α x)
  have e2 : ⟪shiftOp A α x, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪x, shiftOp A α x⟫_ℝ := real_inner_comm _ _
  have e3 : ⟪r, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪x, r⟫_ℝ := real_inner_comm _ _
  simp only [map_add, inner_add_left, inner_add_right] at hc hlow ⊢
  linarith [e1, e2, e3]

end Certificate

/-! ## 4. The split on `H = H_f ⊕ H_c` -/

/-- An orthogonal projection `Π` on `H`: a linear map with `Π² = Π` that is symmetric. -/
structure OrthProj (H : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] where
  /-- The projection `Π`. -/
  P : H →ₗ[ℝ] H
  /-- `Π² = Π`. -/
  idem : ∀ x, P (P x) = P x
  /-- `Π` is symmetric. -/
  symm : P.IsSymmetric

namespace OrthProj

variable {H Y : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]
  [NormedAddCommGroup Y] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Y] (pj : OrthProj H)

/-- The fibre space `H_f = ker Π`. -/
abbrev Hf : Submodule ℝ H := LinearMap.ker pj.P

/-- The coarse space `H_c = ran Π`. -/
abbrev Hc : Submodule ℝ H := LinearMap.range pj.P

theorem mem_Hf {u : H} : u ∈ pj.Hf ↔ pj.P u = 0 := LinearMap.mem_ker

theorem P_of_mem_Hc {v : H} (hv : v ∈ pj.Hc) : pj.P v = v := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := LinearMap.mem_range.1 hv; exact pj.idem y

theorem sub_mem_Hf (x : H) : x - pj.P x ∈ pj.Hf := by
  rw [mem_Hf, map_sub, pj.idem, sub_self]

theorem P_mem_Hc (x : H) : pj.P x ∈ pj.Hc := LinearMap.mem_range_self pj.P x

theorem inner_Hf_Hc {u v : H} (hu : pj.P u = 0) (hv : pj.P v = v) : ⟪u, v⟫_ℝ = 0 := by
  rw [← hv, ← pj.symm u v, hu, inner_zero_left]

/-- Pythagoras: `‖x‖² = ‖x − Π x‖² + ‖Π x‖²`. -/
theorem norm_sq_split (x : H) : ‖x‖ ^ 2 = ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 + ‖pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h0 := pj.inner_Hf_Hc ((pj.mem_Hf).1 (pj.sub_mem_Hf x)) (pj.idem x)
  have h := norm_add_sq_real (x - pj.P x) (pj.P x)
  rw [sub_add_cancel, h0, mul_zero, add_zero] at h
  exact h

/-- `⟪x, (I − Π) x⟫ = ‖(I − Π) x‖²`. -/
theorem inner_sub_P_self (x : H) : ⟪x, x - pj.P x⟫_ℝ = ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h0 := pj.inner_Hf_Hc ((pj.mem_Hf).1 (pj.sub_mem_Hf x)) (pj.idem x)
  calc ⟪x, x - pj.P x⟫_ℝ = ⟪(x - pj.P x) + pj.P x, x - pj.P x⟫_ℝ := by rw [sub_add_cancel]
    _ = ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := by
      rw [inner_add_left, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, real_inner_comm (x - pj.P x), h0,
        add_zero]

/-- `⟪x, Π x⟫ = ‖Π x‖²`. -/
theorem inner_P_self (x : H) : ⟪x, pj.P x⟫_ℝ = ‖pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := by
  calc ⟪x, pj.P x⟫_ℝ = ⟪x, pj.P (pj.P x)⟫_ℝ := by rw [pj.idem]
    _ = ⟪pj.P x, pj.P x⟫_ℝ := (pj.symm x (pj.P x)).symm
    _ = ‖pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq _

/-- The block `A = (I − Π) D` on `H_f`. -/
def blkA (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) : pj.Hf →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf :=
  (D - pj.P ∘ₗ D).restrict fun x _ => pj.sub_mem_Hf (D x)

/-- The block `B = (I − Π) D` from `H_c` to `H_f`. -/
def blkB (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf :=
  (D - pj.P ∘ₗ D).restrict fun x _ => pj.sub_mem_Hf (D x)

/-- The block `C = Π D` on `H_c`. -/
def blkC (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hc :=
  (pj.P ∘ₗ D).restrict fun x _ => pj.P_mem_Hc (D x)

/-- The coarse form on `H_c`: `g v = ⟪J* v, D_c J* v⟫`, which is `⟪v, J D_c J* v⟫` when `Jt` is
the adjoint `J*` of `J`. -/
def gC (Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (v : pj.Hc) : ℝ := ⟪Jt v, Dc (Jt v)⟫_ℝ

@[simp] theorem blkA_coe (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (u : pj.Hf) :
    ((pj.blkA D u : pj.Hf) : H) = D u - pj.P (D u) := rfl

@[simp] theorem blkB_coe (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ((pj.blkB D v : pj.Hf) : H) = D v - pj.P (D v) := rfl

@[simp] theorem blkC_coe (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ((pj.blkC D v : pj.Hc) : H) = pj.P (D v) := rfl

theorem inner_blkA (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (u u' : pj.Hf) :
    ⟪u, pj.blkA D u'⟫_ℝ = ⟪(u : H), D u'⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [Submodule.coe_inner, blkA_coe, inner_sub_right, ← pj.symm (u : H) (D u'),
    (pj.mem_Hf).1 u.2, inner_zero_left, sub_zero]

theorem inner_blkB (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (u : pj.Hf) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ⟪u, pj.blkB D v⟫_ℝ = ⟪(u : H), D v⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [Submodule.coe_inner, blkB_coe, inner_sub_right, ← pj.symm (u : H) (D v),
    (pj.mem_Hf).1 u.2, inner_zero_left, sub_zero]

theorem inner_blkC (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (v v' : pj.Hc) :
    ⟪v, pj.blkC D v'⟫_ℝ = ⟪(v : H), D v'⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [Submodule.coe_inner, blkC_coe, ← pj.symm (v : H) (D v'), pj.P_of_mem_Hc v.2]

theorem blkA_isSymmetric {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) : (pj.blkA D).IsSymmetric :=
  fun u u' => by
    rw [real_inner_comm, inner_blkA, inner_blkA, ← hD (u' : H) u]
    exact real_inner_comm _ _

/-- The operator `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J*` on `H`; `Jt` is `J*`. -/
def splitOp (J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H) (Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (α β : ℝ) : H →ₗ[ℝ] H :=
  α • (LinearMap.id - pj.P) + β • (J ∘ₗ Dc ∘ₗ Jt)

theorem splitOp_apply (J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H) (Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (α β : ℝ) (x : H) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β x = α • (x - pj.P x) + β • J (Dc (Jt x)) := by
  simp [splitOp]

theorem inner_splitOp {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (α β : ℝ) (x : H) :
    ⟪pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β x, x⟫_ℝ = α * ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 + β * ⟪Jt x, Dc (Jt x)⟫_ℝ := by
  rw [splitOp_apply, inner_add_left, real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_smul_left,
    real_inner_comm x (x - pj.P x), pj.inner_sub_P_self, hadj, real_inner_comm (Jt x)]

theorem splitOp_isSymmetric {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric)
    (α β : ℝ) : (pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β).IsSymmetric := fun x y => by
  have h2 : ⟪J (Dc (Jt x)), y⟫_ℝ = ⟪x, J (Dc (Jt y))⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [hadj, real_inner_comm (J (Dc (Jt y))) x, hadj, hDc (Jt y) (Jt x)]
    exact real_inner_comm _ _
  simp only [splitOp_apply, inner_add_left, inner_add_right, real_inner_smul_left,
    real_inner_smul_right, inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right]
  rw [pj.symm x y, h2]

/-- The form of the Loewner inequality `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` (no symmetry needed). -/
theorem form_of_le {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y} {α β : ℝ}
    (hle : pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D) (x : H) :
    α * ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 + β * ⟪Jt x, Dc (Jt x)⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪x, D x⟫_ℝ := by
  have h := ((LinearMap.isPositive_iff _).1 ((LinearMap.le_def _ _).1 hle)).2 x
  rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, inner_sub_left, pj.inner_splitOp hadj, real_inner_comm x (D x)] at h
  linarith

/-- **The Loewner inequality as forms.** For symmetric `D` and `D_c` and `J* = Jt`,
`α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` holds iff `α ‖(I − Π) x‖² + β ⟪J* x, D_c J* x⟫ ≤ ⟪x, D x⟫`
for every `x`. -/
theorem splitOp_le_iff {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H}
    {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric) (α β : ℝ) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D ↔
      ∀ x, α * ‖x - pj.P x‖ ^ 2 + β * ⟪Jt x, Dc (Jt x)⟫_ℝ ≤ ⟪x, D x⟫_ℝ := by
  refine ⟨pj.form_of_le hadj, fun h => ?_⟩
  rw [LinearMap.le_def, LinearMap.isPositive_iff]
  have hS := pj.splitOp_isSymmetric hadj hDc α β
  refine ⟨fun x y => ?_, fun x => ?_⟩
  · rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.sub_apply, inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right, hD x y,
      hS x y]
  · rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, inner_sub_left, pj.inner_splitOp hadj, real_inner_comm x (D x)]
    linarith [h x]

/-- If `ran J ⊆ H_c` then `J*` vanishes on `H_f`. -/
theorem Jt_eq_zero {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y) {u : H} (hu : pj.P u = 0) : Jt u = 0 := by
  have h : ⟪Jt u, Jt u⟫_ℝ = 0 := by
    rw [← hadj, ← hJ, pj.symm (J (Jt u)) u, hu, inner_zero_right]
  exact inner_self_eq_zero.1 h

theorem form_decomp {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) (u : pj.Hf) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ⟪(u : H) + v, D ((u : H) + v)⟫_ℝ = blockForm (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) (pj.blkC D) u v := by
  have e : ⟪(v : H), D u⟫_ℝ = ⟪(u : H), D v⟫_ℝ := by
    rw [← hD (v : H) (u : H)]; exact real_inner_comm _ _
  simp only [blockForm, pj.inner_blkA, pj.inner_blkB, pj.inner_blkC]
  rw [map_add, inner_add_left, inner_add_right, inner_add_right, e]
  ring

theorem target_decomp {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y)
    (α β : ℝ) (u : pj.Hf) (v : pj.Hc) :
    α * ‖((u : H) + v) - pj.P ((u : H) + v)‖ ^ 2 +
        β * ⟪Jt ((u : H) + v), Dc (Jt ((u : H) + v))⟫_ℝ =
      α * ‖u‖ ^ 2 + β * pj.gC Jt Dc v := by
  have hu : pj.P u = 0 := (pj.mem_Hf).1 u.2
  have hv : pj.P v = v := pj.P_of_mem_Hc v.2
  have hJu : Jt u = 0 := pj.Jt_eq_zero hadj hJ hu
  simp only [map_add, hu, hv, hJu, zero_add, add_sub_cancel_right]
  rfl

/-- **The target on `H` as a block target.** For symmetric `D` and `D_c`, `J* = Jt` and
`ran J ⊆ H_c`: `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` iff the block form of `D` on `H_f ⊕ H_c` dominates
`α ‖u‖² + β ⟪v, G v⟫`. -/
theorem le_iff_split {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric) (α β : ℝ) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D ↔
      SplitTarget (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) (pj.blkC D) (pj.gC Jt Dc) α β := by
  rw [pj.splitOp_le_iff hD hadj hDc]
  constructor
  · intro h u v
    have h1 := h ((u : H) + v)
    rw [pj.target_decomp hadj hJ, pj.form_decomp hD] at h1
    exact h1
  · intro h x
    have h1 := h ⟨x - pj.P x, pj.sub_mem_Hf x⟩ ⟨pj.P x, pj.P_mem_Hc x⟩
    rw [← pj.form_decomp hD, ← pj.target_decomp hadj hJ] at h1
    simpa using h1

/-- **The criterion on `H`**: for symmetric `D` and `D_c`, `J* = Jt` and `ran J ⊆ H_c`, with
`A ≥ λ` on `H_f`, `α ≤ λ` and a right inverse of `A − α I` on `H_f`,
`α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` iff `C − β G − B* (A − α I)⁻¹ B ≥ 0`. -/
theorem le_iff_schur {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ} (hlam : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫_ℝ)
    (hα : α ≤ lam) (β : ℝ) {Kinv : pj.Hf →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf}
    (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp (pj.blkA D) α (Kinv x) = x) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D ↔
      ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm (pj.blkB D) (pj.blkC D) (pj.gC Jt Dc) β Kinv v :=
  (pj.le_iff_split hD hadj hJ hDc α β).trans
    (split_iff_schur (pj.blkA_isSymmetric hD)
      (fun u => by rw [pj.inner_blkA]; exact hlam u ((pj.mem_Hf).1 u.2)) hα _ _ _ β hK)

/-- **The certificate on `H`**: for symmetric `D` and `D_c`, `J* = Jt` and `ran J ⊆ H_c`, with
`A ≥ λ` on `H_f`, `α < λ` and a trial operator `X : H_c → H_f` with
`C − β G − Q − (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R ≥ 0`, the split `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` holds. -/
theorem le_of_certificate {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H}
    {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y)
    {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (β : ℝ)
    (X : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf)
    (hcert : ∀ v, β * pj.gC Jt Dc v + qForm (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v +
      ‖resid (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v‖ ^ 2 / (lam - α) ≤ ⟪v, pj.blkC D v⟫_ℝ) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D :=
  (pj.le_iff_split hD hadj hJ hDc α β).2
    (split_of_certificate (pj.blkA_isSymmetric hD)
      (fun u => by rw [pj.inner_blkA]; exact hlam u ((pj.mem_Hf).1 u.2)) hα _ _ _ β X hcert)

/-- **The gap.** If `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D`, `D_c ≥ ϖ I`, `J J* = Π` and `β ≥ 0`, then
`D ≥ min(α, β ϖ) I`. -/
theorem gap_of_le {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y}
    (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJJ : ∀ x, J (Jt x) = pj.P x)
    {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y} {α β ϖ : ℝ} (hβ : 0 ≤ β) (hc : ϖ • LinearMap.id ≤ Dc)
    (hle : pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D) : min α (β * ϖ) • LinearMap.id ≤ D := by
  have hcf : ∀ y, ϖ * ‖y‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪y, Dc y⟫_ℝ := by
    intro y
    have h := ((LinearMap.isPositive_iff _).1 ((LinearMap.le_def _ _).1 hc)).2 y
    rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, inner_sub_left,
      real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, real_inner_comm y (Dc y)] at h
    linarith
  have hJn : ∀ x, ‖Jt x‖ ^ 2 = ‖pj.P x‖ ^ 2 := by
    intro x
    rw [← real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, ← hadj, hJJ, real_inner_comm, pj.inner_P_self]
  rw [LinearMap.le_def, LinearMap.isPositive_iff]
  refine ⟨fun x y => ?_, fun x => ?_⟩
  · simp only [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, inner_sub_left,
      inner_sub_right, real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_smul_right, hD x y]
  · rw [LinearMap.sub_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, inner_sub_left,
      real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, real_inner_comm x (D x)]
    have h1 := pj.form_of_le hadj hle x
    have h2 := hcf (Jt x)
    rw [hJn] at h2
    rw [pj.norm_sq_split x]
    nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 hβ,
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_left α (β * ϖ)) (sq_nonneg ‖x - pj.P x‖),
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (min_le_right α (β * ϖ)) (sq_nonneg ‖pj.P x‖)]

/-- **Certificate and coarse gap give the fine gap**: `D ≥ min(α, β ϖ) I`. -/
theorem gap_of_certificate {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hD : D.IsSymmetric) {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H}
    {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hadj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ) (hJ : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y)
    (hJJ : ∀ x, J (Jt x) = pj.P x) {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y} (hDc : Dc.IsSymmetric) {lam α β ϖ : ℝ}
    (hlam : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (hβ : 0 ≤ β)
    (hc : ϖ • LinearMap.id ≤ Dc) (X : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf)
    (hcert : ∀ v, β * pj.gC Jt Dc v + qForm (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v +
      ‖resid (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v‖ ^ 2 / (lam - α) ≤ ⟪v, pj.blkC D v⟫_ℝ) :
    min α (β * ϖ) • LinearMap.id ≤ D :=
  pj.gap_of_le hD hadj hJJ hβ hc (pj.le_of_certificate hD hadj hJ hDc hlam hα β X hcert)

/-- The block `B` is the restriction of `(I − Π) D Π` to `H_c`. -/
theorem blkB_coe_eq (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ((pj.blkB D v : pj.Hf) : H) = ((1 - pj.P) * D * pj.P) v := by
  rw [blkB_coe, Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply, pj.P_of_mem_Hc v.2,
    LinearMap.sub_apply, Module.End.one_apply]

theorem P_mul_P : pj.P * pj.P = pj.P := LinearMap.ext pj.idem

end OrthProj

/-! ## 5. The mixed block of cube resampling -/

section Resampling

variable {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module ℝ M]

/-- **The mixed block.** If `Π² = Π` and `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`, then
`(I − Π) D Π = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. -/
theorem resampling_offdiag {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (Pc : ι → Module.End ℝ M)
    {P : Module.End ℝ M} (hP : P * P = P) :
    (1 - P) * (∑ x ∈ s, w x • (1 - Pc x)) * P = -∑ x ∈ s, w x • ((1 - P) * Pc x * P) := by
  have h0 : (1 - P) * P = 0 := by rw [sub_mul, one_mul, hP, sub_self]
  rw [Finset.mul_sum, Finset.sum_mul, ← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
  rw [mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc, ← smul_neg]
  congr 1
  rw [mul_sub, sub_mul, mul_one, h0, zero_sub]

/-- The uniform case `D = c ∑ₓ (I − Pₓ)` (in the note `c = n⁻⁴`):
`(I − Π) D Π = −c ∑ₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. -/
theorem resampling_offdiag_uniform {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (c : ℝ)
    (Pc : ι → Module.End ℝ M) {P : Module.End ℝ M} (hP : P * P = P) :
    (1 - P) * (c • ∑ x ∈ s, (1 - Pc x)) * P = -(c • ∑ x ∈ s, (1 - P) * Pc x * P) := by
  rw [Finset.smul_sum, Finset.smul_sum]
  exact resampling_offdiag s (fun _ => c) Pc hP

/-- If every `Pₓ` maps `ran Π` into itself (`Pₓ Π = Π Pₓ Π`), the mixed block vanishes. -/
theorem resampling_offdiag_eq_zero {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ)
    (Pc : ι → Module.End ℝ M) {P : Module.End ℝ M} (hP : P * P = P)
    (hpres : ∀ x ∈ s, Pc x * P = P * Pc x * P) :
    (1 - P) * (∑ x ∈ s, w x • (1 - Pc x)) * P = 0 := by
  have h0 : (1 - P) * P = 0 := by rw [sub_mul, one_mul, hP, sub_self]
  rw [resampling_offdiag s w Pc hP, neg_eq_zero]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun x hx => ?_
  have h : (1 - P) * Pc x * P = 0 := by
    rw [mul_assoc, hpres x hx, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, h0, zero_mul, zero_mul]
  rw [h, smul_zero]

end Resampling

/-! ## 6. Closed applications (non-vacuity) -/

section Examples

/-- On `ℝ`, `⟪x, y⟫ = x y`. -/
theorem inner_real (x y : ℝ) : ⟪x, y⟫_ℝ = x * y := by
  rw [RCLike.inner_apply, conj_trivial, mul_comm]

/-- Multiplication by `c` on `ℝ`. -/
def scal (c : ℝ) : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ := c • LinearMap.id

theorem scal_apply (c x : ℝ) : scal c x = c * x := by simp [scal]

theorem scal_isSymmetric (c : ℝ) : (scal c).IsSymmetric := fun x y => by
  rw [scal_apply, scal_apply, inner_real, inner_real]; ring

theorem norm_sq_real (x : ℝ) : ‖x‖ ^ 2 = x ^ 2 := by rw [Real.norm_eq_abs, sq_abs]

/-- `A = 2`, `α = 1`, `B = 1`, `C = 3`, `G = 1`, `β = 1` on `ℝ`, certified with the inexact
trial `X = 1/2` (the exact `K⁻¹ B` is `1`): here `Q = 3/4`, `R = 1/2`. -/
theorem cert_example : SplitTarget (scal 2) (scal 1) (scal 3) (fun v => v ^ 2) 1 1 := by
  refine split_of_certificate (scal_isSymmetric 2) (lam := 2) (fun u => ?_) (by norm_num)
    (scal 1) (scal 3) (fun v => v ^ 2) 1 (scal (1 / 2)) (fun v => ?_)
  · rw [scal_apply, inner_real, norm_sq_real]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg u]
  · simp only [qForm, resid_apply, shiftOp_apply, scal_apply, inner_real, smul_eq_mul,
      norm_sq_real]
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg v]

/-- **The residual term is essential.** With `A = 1`, `α = 1/2`, `B = C = 1`, `β = 0` and
`X = 0`, the check `C − β G − Q ≥ 0` without the residual holds, but the target fails
(at `u = −2`, `v = 1`). -/
theorem residual_essential :
    (∀ v, 0 * v ^ 2 + qForm (scal 1) (scal 1) (1 / 2) 0 v ≤ ⟪v, scal 1 v⟫_ℝ) ∧
      ¬ SplitTarget (scal 1) (scal 1) (scal 1) (fun v => v ^ 2) (1 / 2) 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun v => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · simp only [qForm, LinearMap.zero_apply, inner_zero_left, inner_zero_right, scal_apply,
      inner_real]
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg v]
  · have h1 := h (-2) 1
    simp only [blockForm, scal_apply, inner_real, norm_sq_real] at h1
    norm_num at h1

/-- The Hilbert-space criterion on `ℝ` (with `A = 2`, `α = 1`): the inverse exists, and the
Schur form of `cert_example` is nonnegative. -/
theorem complete_example : ∃ Kinv : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ, (∀ x, shiftOp (scal 2) 1 (Kinv x) = x) ∧
    ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm (scal 1) (scal 3) (fun v => v ^ 2) 1 (Kinv : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) v := by
  have e : (((2 : ℝ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ ℝ : ℝ →L[ℝ] ℝ) : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) = scal 2 :=
    LinearMap.ext fun x => by simp [scal_apply]
  obtain ⟨Kinv, h1, -, hiff⟩ := split_iff_schur_complete ((2 : ℝ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ ℝ)
    (by rw [e]; exact scal_isSymmetric 2) (lam := 2)
    (fun u => by
      have h2u : ((2 : ℝ) • ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ ℝ) u = 2 * u := by simp
      rw [h2u, inner_real, norm_sq_real]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg u])
    (by norm_num : (1 : ℝ) < 2) (scal 1) (scal 3) (fun v => v ^ 2) 1
  rw [e] at h1 hiff
  exact ⟨Kinv, h1, hiff.1 cert_example⟩

/-- `A = 2`, `α = 1`, `B = 1`, `X = 1/2` on `ℝ`, with `K⁻¹ = 1`: the response `⟪B v, K⁻¹ B v⟫ = v²`
lies between `⟪v, Q v⟫ = (3/4) v²` and `⟪v, Q v⟫ + (λ − α)⁻¹ ‖R v‖² = v²`. -/
theorem response_example (v : ℝ) :
    qForm (scal 2) (scal 1) 1 (scal (1 / 2)) v ≤ ⟪scal 1 v, scal 1 (scal 1 v)⟫_ℝ ∧
      ⟪scal 1 v, scal 1 (scal 1 v)⟫_ℝ ≤
        qForm (scal 2) (scal 1) 1 (scal (1 / 2)) v +
          ‖resid (scal 2) (scal 1) 1 (scal (1 / 2)) v‖ ^ 2 / (2 - 1) := by
  have hK : ∀ x, shiftOp (scal 2) 1 (scal 1 x) = x := fun x => by
    rw [shiftOp_apply, scal_apply, scal_apply, smul_eq_mul]; ring
  have hK' : ∀ x, scal 1 (shiftOp (scal 2) 1 x) = x := fun x => by
    rw [shiftOp_apply, scal_apply, scal_apply, smul_eq_mul]; ring
  have hlam : ∀ u : ℝ, 2 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, scal 2 u⟫_ℝ := fun u => by
    rw [scal_apply, inner_real, norm_sq_real]; nlinarith [sq_nonneg u]
  exact ⟨qForm_le_response (scal_isSymmetric 2) hlam (by norm_num) (scal 1) hK hK' _ v,
    response_le_cert (scal_isSymmetric 2) hlam (by norm_num) (scal 1) hK hK' _ v⟩

/-! ### A two-dimensional cube-resampling model -/

/-- `ℝ²` with its Euclidean inner product. -/
abbrev R2 : Type := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 2)

/-- The linear map of the matrix `[[a, b], [c, d]]` on `ℝ²`. -/
noncomputable def mat2 (a b c d : ℝ) : R2 →ₗ[ℝ] R2 where
  toFun x := !₂[a * x 0 + b * x 1, c * x 0 + d * x 1]
  map_add' x y := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp <;> ring
  map_smul' r x := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp <;> ring

@[simp] theorem mat2_apply_zero (a b c d : ℝ) (x : R2) :
    mat2 a b c d x 0 = a * x 0 + b * x 1 := by simp [mat2]

@[simp] theorem mat2_apply_one (a b c d : ℝ) (x : R2) :
    mat2 a b c d x 1 = c * x 0 + d * x 1 := by simp [mat2]

theorem inner_R2 (x y : R2) : ⟪x, y⟫_ℝ = x 0 * y 0 + x 1 * y 1 := by
  simp [PiLp.inner_apply, Fin.sum_univ_two]
  ring

theorem norm_sq_R2 (x : R2) : ‖x‖ ^ 2 = x 0 ^ 2 + x 1 ^ 2 := by
  rw [EuclideanSpace.real_norm_sq_eq, Fin.sum_univ_two]

theorem mat2_isSymmetric (a b d : ℝ) : (mat2 a b b d).IsSymmetric := fun x y => by
  rw [inner_R2, inner_R2]; simp only [mat2_apply_zero, mat2_apply_one]; ring

theorem id_isSymmetric : (LinearMap.id : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ).IsSymmetric := fun _ _ => rfl

/-- `B v = (v, v)` from `ℝ` to `ℝ²`. -/
noncomputable def bT : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] R2 where
  toFun y := !₂[y, y]
  map_add' a b := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp
  map_smul' r a := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp

@[simp] theorem bT_apply_zero (y : ℝ) : bT y 0 = y := by simp [bT]

@[simp] theorem bT_apply_one (y : ℝ) : bT y 1 = y := by simp [bT]

/-- A non-scalar fibre block: `A = diag(1, 2)` on `ℝ²` (so `λ = 1`), `α = 1/2`,
`K⁻¹ = diag(2, 2/3)`, `B v = (v, v)` and the trial `X = 0`, so `Q = 0` and `R = B`. The response
`⟪B v, K⁻¹ B v⟫ = (8/3) v²` lies between `Q = 0` and `Q + (λ − α)⁻¹ ‖R v‖² = 4 v²`
(`qForm_le_response`, `response_le_cert`), strictly for `v ≠ 0`: the residual bound is not exact. -/
theorem response_strict_example (v : ℝ) :
    qForm (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v = 0 ∧
      ⟪bT v, mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) (bT v)⟫_ℝ = 8 / 3 * v ^ 2 ∧
      qForm (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v +
          ‖resid (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v‖ ^ 2 / (1 - 1 / 2) = 4 * v ^ 2 ∧
      qForm (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v ≤ ⟪bT v, mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) (bT v)⟫_ℝ ∧
      ⟪bT v, mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) (bT v)⟫_ℝ ≤
        qForm (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v +
          ‖resid (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v‖ ^ 2 / (1 - 1 / 2) := by
  have hK : ∀ x, shiftOp (mat2 1 0 0 2) (1 / 2) (mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) x) = x := fun x => by
    ext i; fin_cases i <;> (simp [shiftOp_apply]; try ring)
  have hK' : ∀ x, mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) (shiftOp (mat2 1 0 0 2) (1 / 2) x) = x := fun x => by
    ext i; fin_cases i <;> (simp [shiftOp_apply]; try ring)
  have hlam : ∀ u, 1 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, mat2 1 0 0 2 u⟫_ℝ := fun u => by
    rw [norm_sq_R2, inner_R2]
    simp only [mat2_apply_zero, mat2_apply_one]
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (u 1)]
  have hA := mat2_isSymmetric 1 0 2
  have hq : qForm (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v = 0 := by simp [qForm]
  have hr : ⟪bT v, mat2 2 0 0 (2 / 3) (bT v)⟫_ℝ = 8 / 3 * v ^ 2 := by
    rw [inner_R2]
    simp only [mat2_apply_zero, mat2_apply_one, bT_apply_zero, bT_apply_one]
    ring
  have hb : ‖resid (mat2 1 0 0 2) bT (1 / 2) 0 v‖ ^ 2 = 2 * v ^ 2 := by
    rw [resid_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply, map_zero, sub_zero, norm_sq_R2, bT_apply_zero,
      bT_apply_one]
    ring
  exact ⟨hq, hr, by rw [hq, hb]; ring,
    qForm_le_response hA hlam (by norm_num) bT hK hK' 0 v,
    response_le_cert hA hlam (by norm_num) bT hK hK' 0 v⟩

/-- The coarse projection `Π = diag(1, 0)`: the first coordinate is coarse, the second fine. -/
noncomputable def pT : OrthProj R2 where
  P := mat2 1 0 0 0
  idem x := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp
  symm := mat2_isSymmetric 1 0 0

theorem pT_P : pT.P = mat2 1 0 0 0 := rfl

/-- Two cube projections: onto the diagonal `(1, 1)` and onto the first axis. -/
noncomputable def PcT : Fin 2 → Module.End ℝ R2 :=
  ![mat2 (1 / 2) (1 / 2) (1 / 2) (1 / 2), mat2 1 0 0 0]

/-- The generator `D = [[1/4, −1/4], [−1/4, 3/4]]`. -/
noncomputable def DT : R2 →ₗ[ℝ] R2 := mat2 (1 / 4) (-1 / 4) (-1 / 4) (3 / 4)

theorem DT_isSymmetric : DT.IsSymmetric := mat2_isSymmetric _ _ _

/-- `D = ∑ₓ (1/2) (I − Pₓ)`: resample one of the two cubes, chosen uniformly. -/
theorem DT_eq : DT = ∑ x, (1 / 2 : ℝ) • (1 - PcT x) := by
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_two]
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [DT, PcT] <;> ring

/-- The coarse embedding `J y = (y, 0)` of `ℝ`. -/
noncomputable def JT : ℝ →ₗ[ℝ] R2 where
  toFun y := !₂[y, 0]
  map_add' a b := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp
  map_smul' r a := by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp

/-- `J* x = x₀`. -/
noncomputable def JtT : R2 →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ where
  toFun x := x 0
  map_add' x y := by simp
  map_smul' r x := by simp

@[simp] theorem JT_apply_zero (y : ℝ) : JT y 0 = y := by simp [JT]

@[simp] theorem JT_apply_one (y : ℝ) : JT y 1 = 0 := by simp [JT]

@[simp] theorem JtT_apply (x : R2) : JtT x = x 0 := rfl

theorem hadjT : ∀ y x, ⟪JT y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, JtT x⟫_ℝ := fun y x => by
  rw [inner_R2, inner_real]; simp

theorem hJT : ∀ y, pT.P (JT y) = JT y := fun y => by
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [pT_P]

theorem hJJT : ∀ x, JT (JtT x) = pT.P x := fun x => by
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [pT_P]

/-- The mixed block of the model is `−(1/2)(I − Π) P₀ Π − (1/2)(I − Π) P₁ Π`, and it is not
zero: the diagonal cube does not preserve the coarse coordinate. -/
theorem toy_offdiag :
    (1 - pT.P) * DT * pT.P = -∑ x, (1 / 2 : ℝ) • ((1 - pT.P) * PcT x * pT.P) ∧
      (1 - pT.P) * DT * pT.P ≠ 0 := by
  refine ⟨by rw [DT_eq]; exact resampling_offdiag _ _ _ pT.P_mul_P, fun h => ?_⟩
  have h1 := congrArg (fun T : Module.End ℝ R2 => T (!₂[1, 0]) 1) h
  simp [DT, pT_P, Module.End.mul_apply] at h1

/-- `A = 3/4` on `H_f`: `⟪u, D u⟫ ≥ (3/4) ‖u‖²` when `Π u = 0`. -/
theorem toy_hlam : ∀ u, pT.P u = 0 → 3 / 4 * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, DT u⟫_ℝ := fun u hu => by
  have h0 : u 0 = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun z : R2 => z 0) hu
    simpa [pT_P] using h
  rw [norm_sq_R2, inner_R2]
  simp [DT, h0]
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg (u 1)]

/-- The split `(1/4)(I − Π) + (1/8) J J* ≤ D` holds in the model (`D_c = I`). -/
theorem toy_le : pT.splitOp JT JtT LinearMap.id (1 / 4) (1 / 8) ≤ DT := by
  rw [pT.splitOp_le_iff DT_isSymmetric hadjT id_isSymmetric]
  intro x
  rw [norm_sq_R2, inner_R2, inner_real]
  simp [DT, pT_P]
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg (x 0 - 2 * x 1)]

/-- The block form of `toy_le`. -/
theorem toy_split :
    SplitTarget (pT.blkA DT) (pT.blkB DT) (pT.blkC DT) (pT.gC JtT LinearMap.id) (1 / 4) (1 / 8) :=
  (pT.le_iff_split DT_isSymmetric hadjT hJT id_isSymmetric _ _).1 toy_le

/-- With `D_c = I ≥ 1 · I`, `gap_of_le` gives the lower bound `min(1/4, 1/8) = 1/8`:
`D ≥ (1/8) I` (the least eigenvalue of `D` is `1/2 − √2/4`). -/
theorem toy_gap : (1 / 8 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ DT := by
  have h := pT.gap_of_le DT_isSymmetric hadjT hJJT (ϖ := 1) (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 8)
    (le_of_eq (one_smul ℝ _)) toy_le
  rwa [show min (1 / 4 : ℝ) (1 / 8 * 1) = 1 / 8 by norm_num] at h

/-- The trial operator `X v = (0, −v₀/4)` from `H_c` to `H_f`; the exact `(A − α I)⁻¹ B` is
`v ↦ (0, −v₀/2)`. -/
noncomputable def XT : pT.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pT.Hf :=
  (mat2 0 0 (-1 / 4) 0).restrict fun x _ => by
    rw [OrthProj.mem_Hf, pT_P]; ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp

/-- The certificate of the model with `α = 1/4`, `β = 1/16`, `λ = 3/4` and the inexact trial
`XT`: `β g + Q + (λ − α)⁻¹ ‖R‖² = (3/16) v₀² ≤ (1/4) v₀² = ⟪v, C v⟫`, with `R v = (0, −v₀/8)`.
Since `A = λ` on the one-dimensional `H_f`, the residual bound is exact here, and the same
certificate also proves `β = 1/8`. -/
theorem toy_cert : ∀ v : pT.Hc, 1 / 16 * pT.gC JtT LinearMap.id v +
    qForm (pT.blkA DT) (pT.blkB DT) (1 / 4) XT v +
      ‖resid (pT.blkA DT) (pT.blkB DT) (1 / 4) XT v‖ ^ 2 / (3 / 4 - 1 / 4) ≤
        ⟪v, pT.blkC DT v⟫_ℝ := fun v => by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := LinearMap.mem_range.1 v.2
  have h1 : (v : R2) 1 = 0 := by rw [← hy, pT_P]; simp
  simp only [qForm, resid_apply, shiftOp_apply, OrthProj.gC, Submodule.coe_inner,
    Submodule.coe_norm, Submodule.coe_sub, Submodule.coe_smul, OrthProj.blkA_coe,
    OrthProj.blkB_coe, OrthProj.blkC_coe, XT, LinearMap.coe_restrict_apply, inner_R2, norm_sq_R2,
    inner_real, JtT_apply, LinearMap.id_apply, PiLp.sub_apply, PiLp.smul_apply, smul_eq_mul, DT,
    pT_P, mat2_apply_zero, mat2_apply_one, h1]
  ring_nf
  nlinarith [sq_nonneg ((v : R2) 0)]

/-- The split `(1/4)(I − Π) + (1/16) J J* ≤ D`, proved by the certificate `toy_cert`. -/
theorem toy_cert_le : pT.splitOp JT JtT LinearMap.id (1 / 4) (1 / 16) ≤ DT :=
  pT.le_of_certificate DT_isSymmetric hadjT hJT id_isSymmetric toy_hlam (by norm_num) (1 / 16)
    XT toy_cert

/-- The gap from the certificate: `D ≥ min(1/4, 1/16) I = (1/16) I`. -/
theorem toy_gap_cert : (1 / 16 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ DT := by
  have h := pT.gap_of_certificate DT_isSymmetric hadjT hJT hJJT id_isSymmetric (ϖ := 1)
    toy_hlam (by norm_num) (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 16) (le_of_eq (one_smul ℝ _)) XT
    toy_cert
  rwa [show min (1 / 4 : ℝ) (1 / 16 * 1) = 1 / 16 by norm_num] at h

/-- The inverse `(A − α I)⁻¹ = 2 I` on `H_f` (there `A = 3/4` and `α = 1/4`). -/
noncomputable def KinvT : pT.Hf →ₗ[ℝ] pT.Hf := (2 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id

theorem KinvT_spec : ∀ x, shiftOp (pT.blkA DT) (1 / 4) (KinvT x) = x := fun x => by
  have h0 : (x : R2) 0 = 0 := by
    have h := congrArg (fun z : R2 => z 0) ((pT.mem_Hf).1 x.2)
    simpa [pT_P] using h
  apply Subtype.ext
  simp only [shiftOp_apply, KinvT, Submodule.coe_sub, Submodule.coe_smul, OrthProj.blkA_coe,
    LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply]
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> (simp [DT, pT_P, h0]; try ring)

/-- The coarse vector `(1, 0) ∈ H_c`. -/
noncomputable def e0T : pT.Hc := ⟨!₂[1, 0], ⟨!₂[1, 0], by ext i; fin_cases i <;> simp [pT_P]⟩⟩

/-- **Necessity in the model.** The Schur form at `(1, 0)` is `1/4 − β − 1/8`, so by
`le_iff_schur` the split with `α = 1/4` fails for `β = 1/4`. -/
theorem toy_not_le : ¬ pT.splitOp JT JtT LinearMap.id (1 / 4) (1 / 4) ≤ DT := by
  intro h
  have h1 := (pT.le_iff_schur DT_isSymmetric hadjT hJT id_isSymmetric toy_hlam
    (by norm_num) (1 / 4) KinvT_spec).1 h e0T
  simp [schurForm, OrthProj.gC, KinvT, e0T, DT, pT_P, inner_R2, Submodule.coe_inner] at h1
  norm_num at h1

/-- **The uniform form in the model.** `D = (1/2) ∑ₓ (I − Pₓ)`, so `resampling_offdiag_uniform`
with `c = 1/2` gives `(I − Π) D Π = −(1/2) ∑ₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. -/
theorem toy_offdiag_uniform :
    (1 - pT.P) * DT * pT.P = -((1 / 2 : ℝ) • ∑ x, (1 - pT.P) * PcT x * pT.P) := by
  have hD : DT = (1 / 2 : ℝ) • ∑ x, (1 - PcT x) := by rw [DT_eq, Finset.smul_sum]
  rw [hD]
  exact resampling_offdiag_uniform _ _ _ pT.P_mul_P

/-- **The axis cube has no mixed block.** `P₁ = Π` maps `ran Π` into itself, so by
`resampling_offdiag_eq_zero` its part `(1/2)(I − P₁)` of the generator has zero mixed block: the
nonzero mixed block of `toy_offdiag` comes from the diagonal cube `P₀` alone. -/
theorem toy_offdiag_axis :
    (1 - pT.P) * (∑ x ∈ ({1} : Finset (Fin 2)), (1 / 2 : ℝ) • (1 - PcT x)) * pT.P = 0 := by
  have h1 : PcT 1 = pT.P := by simp [PcT, pT_P]
  refine resampling_offdiag_eq_zero _ _ _ pT.P_mul_P fun x hx => ?_
  rw [Finset.mem_singleton] at hx
  subst hx
  rw [h1, pT.P_mul_P, pT.P_mul_P]

/-- **The block `B` in the model** (`blkB_coe_eq`): `B` is the restriction of `(I − Π) D Π` to
`H_c`, and `B (1, 0) = (0, −1/4)`. -/
theorem toy_blkB :
    ((pT.blkB DT e0T : pT.Hf) : R2) = ((1 - pT.P) * DT * pT.P) (e0T : R2) ∧
      ((pT.blkB DT e0T : pT.Hf) : R2) = !₂[0, -1 / 4] := by
  refine ⟨pT.blkB_coe_eq DT e0T, ?_⟩
  rw [pT.blkB_coe_eq DT e0T]
  ext i; fin_cases i <;> (simp [DT, pT_P, e0T, Module.End.mul_apply]; try norm_num)


end Examples

end SchurSplit

/-! # Part VI. `YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit` (the text of `CubeSplitInterface.lean` after
its import line; it uses Part V) -/

/-!
# The Schur-complement split as an interface for the cube-resampling generator

## (a) Formal target

Let `H` be a real inner product space with an orthogonal projection `Π` (`H_f = ker Π`,
`H_c = ran Π`), let `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)` be a cube-resampling generator on `H`, and let `J : Y → H`
be a coarse map with adjoint `J*` and `D_c` a coarse generator on `Y`. The targets are the exact
criterion for the split `α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` (`CubeSplitInputs.split_iff_schur`) and the
lower bound `D ≥ min(α, β ϖ_c) I` (`CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual`), with the mixed block and
the residual written in terms of the cube operators `Pₓ`.

## (b) What is proved

* `cubeGen`, `cubeGen_isSymmetric`: `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`, symmetric when every `Pₓ` is.
* `CubeSplitInputs`: the identification inputs bundled as one hypothesis, called `hWilson` in every
  theorem: `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)` with every `Pₓ` symmetric, `⟪J y, x⟫ = ⟪y, J* x⟫`,
  `ran J ⊆ ran Π`, `J J* = Π` and `D_c` symmetric.
* `CubeSplitInputs.mixed_eq`, `CubeSplitInputs.blkB_eq`: `(I − Π) D Π = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`, so
  the mixed block is `B v = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ v` for `v ∈ H_c`.
* `CubeSplitInputs.resid_eq`: the residual of a trial `X : H_c → H_f` is
  `R v = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ v − (A − α I) X v`.
* `CubeSplitInputs.split_iff_schur`: given `A ≥ λ` on `H_f`, `α ≤ λ` and an inverse of `A − α I`,
  the split holds iff the Schur complement `C − β G − B* (A − α I)⁻¹ B` is nonnegative.
* `CubeSplitInputs.gap_of_residual`: `hWilson`, `hFibre`, `hResidual` and `hCoarseGap` give
  `D ≥ min(α, β ϖ_c) I`.
* `toy_inputs`, `toy_blkB_cube`, `toy_mixed_ne_zero`, `toy_resid_cube`, `toy_split_iff`,
  `toy_gap_of_residual`: every input proved in the two-cube model on `ℝ²` of
  `SchurSplitCriterion` (`Π = diag(1, 0)`, `P₀`, `P₁` the orthogonal projections onto `(1, 1)`
  and `(1, 0)`, `wₓ = 1/2`, `D_c = I`). There the mixed block is present: `B (1, 0) = (0, −1/4)`.

The block, residual, criterion and gap results apply theorems of `SchurSplitCriterion`
(`resampling_offdiag`, `OrthProj.blkB_coe_eq`, `OrthProj.le_iff_schur`,
`OrthProj.gap_of_certificate`); `cubeGen_apply` and `cubeGen_isSymmetric` are proved directly
from Mathlib lemmas. Nothing proved there is proved again here.

## (c) Hypotheses that remain open for the Wilson model

* `hWilson` (**Open**): the identification. `H` is the centred gauge-invariant `L²` space of the
  Wilson measure, `Pₓ` the cube conditional expectations (orthogonal projections, so symmetric),
  `wₓ = n⁻⁴`, `Π` the coarse-measurable projection, `J` the coarse embedding and `D_c` the coarse
  generator; the fields of `CubeSplitInputs` must be proved for them. This library defines none of
  these objects, so no Wilson instance is constructed.
* `hFibre` (**Open**): `A ≥ λ` on `H_f`, that is `⟪u, D u⟫ ≥ λ ‖u‖²` when `Π u = 0`.
* `hResidual` (**Open**): a trial `X` with `β G + Q + (λ − α)⁻¹ R* R ≤ C` on `H_c`, where
  `Q = B* X + X* B − X* (A − α I) X` and `R = B − (A − α I) X`.
* `hCoarseGap` (**Open**): `D_c ≥ ϖ_c I` on the coarse space.

The hypotheses concern one fixed `D`, `λ`, `X` and `ϖ_c`. For the Wilson model the constants must
also be uniform in the spacing, the volume and the boundary condition; that is a requirement on
the instances, not part of any statement here. `split_iff_schur` also assumes an inverse of
`A − α I` on `H_f` (`hK`), which `gap_of_residual` does not need. On a Hilbert space with `D`
continuous it follows from `hFibre` and `α < λ` by Lax–Milgram (`exists_shiftOp_inverse` of
`SchurSplitCriterion`); that step is not formalised here.

## (d) Axioms and checks

Every declaration depends only on `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`; the sources
contain no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide` or `implemented_by`. The build, axiom audit
and `leanchecker` replay logs are kept outside the source tree.

## (e) Scope

This file is not a proof of a mass gap. It proves no lattice gap for the Wilson measure and nothing
about a continuum limit: the conclusion of `gap_of_residual` is only as strong as its four
hypotheses, all of which are open for the Wilson model. The two-cube model is a toy model, not the
Wilson model.
-/

namespace YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit

open SchurSplit
open scoped InnerProductSpace

section Interface

variable {H Y : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]
  [NormedAddCommGroup Y] [InnerProductSpace ℝ Y] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]

/-- The cube-resampling generator `D = ∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)`. -/
noncomputable def cubeGen (w : ι → ℝ) (P : ι → H →ₗ[ℝ] H) : H →ₗ[ℝ] H :=
  ∑ x, w x • (1 - P x)

theorem cubeGen_apply (w : ι → ℝ) (P : ι → H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (z : H) :
    cubeGen w P z = ∑ x, w x • (z - P x z) := by
  simp [cubeGen]

/-- `∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)` is symmetric when every `Pₓ` is (for instance when every `Pₓ` is an
orthogonal projection, as a conditional expectation is on `L²`). -/
theorem cubeGen_isSymmetric (w : ι → ℝ) {P : ι → H →ₗ[ℝ] H} (hP : ∀ x, (P x).IsSymmetric) :
    (cubeGen w P).IsSymmetric := fun u v => by
  rw [cubeGen_apply, cubeGen_apply, sum_inner, inner_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => ?_
  rw [real_inner_smul_left, real_inner_smul_right, inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right, hP x u v]

/-- **The identification inputs.** `D` is the cube-resampling generator `∑ₓ wₓ (I − Pₓ)` of
symmetric operators `Pₓ`; `Jt` is the adjoint of `J`; `J` maps into `ran Π` and `J J* = Π`; `D_c`
is symmetric. For the Wilson model these are the open identification step (`hWilson`): no instance
for the Wilson measure is constructed in this library. -/
structure CubeSplitInputs (D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (w : ι → ℝ) (P : ι → H →ₗ[ℝ] H) (pj : OrthProj H)
    (J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H) (Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y) (Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y) : Prop where
  gen_eq : D = cubeGen w P
  proj_symm : ∀ x, (P x).IsSymmetric
  adj : ∀ y x, ⟪J y, x⟫_ℝ = ⟪y, Jt x⟫_ℝ
  ran_J : ∀ y, pj.P (J y) = J y
  JJt : ∀ x, J (Jt x) = pj.P x
  Dc_symm : Dc.IsSymmetric

namespace CubeSplitInputs

variable {D : H →ₗ[ℝ] H} {w : ι → ℝ} {P : ι → H →ₗ[ℝ] H} {pj : OrthProj H}
  {J : Y →ₗ[ℝ] H} {Jt : H →ₗ[ℝ] Y} {Dc : Y →ₗ[ℝ] Y}

theorem isSymmetric (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) : D.IsSymmetric := by
  rw [hWilson.gen_eq]
  exact cubeGen_isSymmetric w hWilson.proj_symm

/-- **The mixed block of the cube generator**: `(I − Π) D Π = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ Π`. -/
theorem mixed_eq (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) :
    (1 - pj.P) * D * pj.P = -∑ x, w x • ((1 - pj.P) * P x * pj.P) := by
  rw [hWilson.gen_eq]
  unfold cubeGen
  exact resampling_offdiag _ _ _ pj.P_mul_P

/-- **The block `B` in cube terms**: for `v ∈ H_c`, `B v = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ v`. -/
theorem blkB_eq (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) (v : pj.Hc) :
    ((pj.blkB D v : pj.Hf) : H) = -∑ x, w x • (P x v - pj.P (P x v)) := by
  rw [pj.blkB_coe_eq D v, hWilson.mixed_eq]
  simp [Module.End.mul_apply, pj.P_of_mem_Hc v.2]

/-- **The residual in cube terms**: for a trial `X : H_c → H_f` and `v ∈ H_c`,
`R v = −∑ₓ wₓ (I − Π) Pₓ v − (A − α I) X v`. This is the quantity that `hResidual` must bound. -/
theorem resid_eq (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) (α : ℝ) (X : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf)
    (v : pj.Hc) :
    ((resid (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v : pj.Hf) : H) =
      -∑ x, w x • (P x v - pj.P (P x v)) - ((shiftOp (pj.blkA D) α (X v) : pj.Hf) : H) := by
  rw [resid_apply, Submodule.coe_sub, hWilson.blkB_eq v]

/-- **The exact criterion for the cube generator.** Under `hWilson`, with `A ≥ λ` on `H_f`
(`hFibre`), `α ≤ λ` and an inverse `Kinv` of `A − α I` on `H_f`, the split
`α (I − Π) + β J D_c J* ≤ D` holds iff `C − β G − B* (A − α I)⁻¹ B ≥ 0` on `H_c`. -/
theorem split_iff_schur (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) {lam α : ℝ}
    (hFibre : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α ≤ lam) (β : ℝ)
    {Kinv : pj.Hf →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf} (hK : ∀ x, shiftOp (pj.blkA D) α (Kinv x) = x) :
    pj.splitOp J Jt Dc α β ≤ D ↔
      ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm (pj.blkB D) (pj.blkC D) (pj.gC Jt Dc) β Kinv v :=
  pj.le_iff_schur hWilson.isSymmetric hWilson.adj hWilson.ran_J hWilson.Dc_symm hFibre hα β hK

/-- **The reduction.** The identification (`hWilson`), the fibre bound `A ≥ λ` (`hFibre`), a
trial `X` whose residual certificate holds (`hResidual`) and the coarse gap `D_c ≥ ϖ I`
(`hCoarseGap`) give `D ≥ min(α, β ϖ) I`. All four inputs are open for the Wilson model. -/
theorem gap_of_residual (hWilson : CubeSplitInputs D w P pj J Jt Dc) {lam α β ϖ : ℝ}
    (hFibre : ∀ u, pj.P u = 0 → lam * ‖u‖ ^ 2 ≤ ⟪u, D u⟫_ℝ) (hα : α < lam) (hβ : 0 ≤ β)
    (hCoarseGap : ϖ • LinearMap.id ≤ Dc) (X : pj.Hc →ₗ[ℝ] pj.Hf)
    (hResidual : ∀ v, β * pj.gC Jt Dc v + qForm (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v +
      ‖resid (pj.blkA D) (pj.blkB D) α X v‖ ^ 2 / (lam - α) ≤ ⟪v, pj.blkC D v⟫_ℝ) :
    min α (β * ϖ) • LinearMap.id ≤ D :=
  pj.gap_of_certificate hWilson.isSymmetric hWilson.adj hWilson.ran_J hWilson.JJt
    hWilson.Dc_symm hFibre hα hβ hCoarseGap X hResidual

end CubeSplitInputs

end Interface

/-! ## The two-cube model (a toy model, not the Wilson model) -/

section Toy

/-- The two cube projections of the model are symmetric. -/
theorem toy_PcT_symm : ∀ x, (PcT x).IsSymmetric := by
  intro x
  fin_cases x
  · exact mat2_isSymmetric (1 / 2) (1 / 2) (1 / 2)
  · exact mat2_isSymmetric 1 0 0

/-- **The model satisfies the identification inputs**: `D = ∑ₓ (1/2)(I − Pₓ)` (`DT_eq`),
symmetric `Pₓ`, `J* = Jt`, `ran J ⊆ ran Π`, `J J* = Π` and `D_c = I`. -/
theorem toy_inputs :
    CubeSplitInputs DT (fun _ => (1 / 2 : ℝ)) PcT pT JT JtT LinearMap.id :=
  ⟨by unfold cubeGen; exact DT_eq, toy_PcT_symm, hadjT, hJT, hJJT, id_isSymmetric⟩

/-- The cube formula for `B` in the model (`blkB_eq`), at the coarse vector `(1, 0)`. -/
theorem toy_blkB_cube :
    ((pT.blkB DT e0T : pT.Hf) : R2) =
      -∑ x, (1 / 2 : ℝ) • (PcT x e0T - pT.P (PcT x e0T)) :=
  toy_inputs.blkB_eq e0T

/-- **The mixed block is present in the model**: `B (1, 0) = (0, −1/4)` (`toy_blkB`), so
`B ≠ 0`. -/
theorem toy_mixed_ne_zero : pT.blkB DT ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  have h1 := toy_blkB.2
  rw [h, LinearMap.zero_apply] at h1
  have h2 := congrArg (fun z : R2 => z 1) h1
  norm_num at h2

/-- The residual of the trial `XT` in cube terms (`resid_eq`), at `(1, 0)`. -/
theorem toy_resid_cube :
    ((resid (pT.blkA DT) (pT.blkB DT) (1 / 4) XT e0T : pT.Hf) : R2) =
      -∑ x, (1 / 2 : ℝ) • (PcT x e0T - pT.P (PcT x e0T)) -
        ((shiftOp (pT.blkA DT) (1 / 4) (XT e0T) : pT.Hf) : R2) :=
  toy_inputs.resid_eq (1 / 4) XT e0T

/-- **The exact criterion in the model** (`split_iff_schur` with `λ = 3/4`, `α = 1/4`,
`K⁻¹ = 2 I`, `β = 1/8`), and the split itself at `(1/4, 1/8)` (`toy_le`). -/
theorem toy_split_iff :
    (pT.splitOp JT JtT LinearMap.id (1 / 4) (1 / 8) ≤ DT ↔
      ∀ v, 0 ≤ schurForm (pT.blkB DT) (pT.blkC DT) (pT.gC JtT LinearMap.id) (1 / 8) KinvT v) ∧
    pT.splitOp JT JtT LinearMap.id (1 / 4) (1 / 8) ≤ DT :=
  ⟨toy_inputs.split_iff_schur toy_hlam (by norm_num) (1 / 8) KinvT_spec, toy_le⟩

/-- **The reduction in the model** (`gap_of_residual` with `λ = 3/4`, `α = 1/4`, `β = 1/16`,
`ϖ = 1` and the certificate `toy_cert`): `D ≥ (1/16) I`. Every input is proved in this model; none
is proved for the Wilson model. -/
theorem toy_gap_of_residual : (1 / 16 : ℝ) • LinearMap.id ≤ DT := by
  have h := toy_inputs.gap_of_residual (ϖ := 1) toy_hlam (by norm_num)
    (by norm_num : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 1 / 16) (le_of_eq (one_smul ℝ _)) XT toy_cert
  rwa [show min (1 / 4 : ℝ) (1 / 16 * 1) = 1 / 16 by norm_num] at h

end Toy

end YangMills.StrongCoupling.CubeSplit
